683cd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/7c97ba04a8b0b3ac478aec9f9df4f01414683cd8"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/6ec6a3ba9c10b562ec59d189663994b2e8e28256","sha":"6ec6a3ba9c10b562ec59d189663994b2e8e28256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/6ec6a3ba9c10b562ec59d189663994b2e8e28256"}],"sha":"62305e868ef093cb7b3baf8ade05edc33f37bd1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/62305e868ef093cb7b3baf8ade05edc33f37bd1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/7c97ba04a8b0b3ac478aec9f9df4f01414683cd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:17:19Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:17:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"UX-179 - rpcn: save pipelines as drafts (#2624)\n\n* RPCN: save pipelines as drafts, without deploying them\n\nSave used to mean Start, and was gated on validation passing. So work in\nprogress could not be parked — an invalid config would not save at all, and a\nrefresh or a misclicked Back button lost everything typed — and a finished\nconfig could not be saved without going live.\n\nA pipeline can now be saved as a draft: persisted, not running, zero compute,\nand stored exactly as typed even when it does not lint. Validation moves to the\nmoment it matters, which is Start.\n\nAPI (proto/redpanda/api/dataplane/v1/pipeline.proto), all additive:\n\n  - Pipeline.State.STATE_DRAFT, omitted from ListPipelines unless\n    Filter.include_drafts is set, so clients written before drafts existed never\n    receive a state they cannot render.\n  - PipelineCreate.draft, and PipelineUpdate.draft as an *assertion* rather than\n    a transition: it means \"I am editing a draft\", and the update fails with\n    FAILED_PRECONDITION if the pipeline has since been started. Without that,\n    \"Save draft\" could silently deploy a config to a running pipeline because a\n    teammate started it mid-edit.\n  - Filter.states for state filtering, and Pipeline.created_by / create_time /\n    update_time so a shared draft pool is attributable and its staleness visible.\n  - config_yaml loses its field-level `required` rule; the service enforces it\n    for anything that is not a draft, with a sentence instead of a proto field\n    path. Pipeline keeps the invariant as a message-level CEL rule.\n\nConsole:\n\n  - Split save actions per context: Save draft (new pipelines and drafts),\n    Save and start, Save (stopped), Apply and restart (running — saying \"Save\"\n    would hide the restart, and there is no apply-later to make that untrue).\n  - Drafts are ordinary rows in the pipeline list: Draft chip, Drafts tab with a\n    count, sorted first and by last edited, resume / start / delete actions, and\n    \"Edited 5m ago · by someone\" in place of the id.\n  - A draft''s own page explains itself instead of offering monitoring it cannot\n    have, and starting one routes lint failures into the editor where they are\n    fixable.\n  - Lint results are warnings on a draft and block only Start; an unnamed draft\n    is auto-named rather than refused.\n  - localStorage is repurposed from \"drafts\" to what it is actually good for:\n    crash recovery for the editor buffer, offered back after a refresh and\n    dropped on a successful save.\n  - New Changes lane (YAML | Visual | Changes N) diffing the saved config\n    against the editor, with the components touched listed and clickable, and a\n    header line stating what applying will cost.\n\nDeliberate decisions, with reasoning, in frontend/specs/rp-connect-pipeline-drafts.md:\ndraft as a distinct state rather than an unapplied-changes flag; annotation\nstorage rather than a CRD field; drafts count against the pipeline quota; drafts\nare named and names may collide; org-wide visibility because pipeline RBAC has no\nownership predicate; no expiry, staleness shown instead. It also records the\nfeature''s real limit — a draft ends at first start, so \"save without going live\"\nis solved for pipelines that have never run and not for the ones that have — and\nthe design for closing that with a pending revision.\n\nShips behind enable-rpcn-pipeline-drafts. The flag must stay off until the\nredpanda-connect-api carrying draft support is deployed: an older API ignores\n`draft` on create and deploys what the user asked to park. Note that\nbackend/pkg/protogen must be regenerated even though no Go here implements\nPipelineService — console-enterprise proxies through these types, and Connect''s\nJSON codec discards unknown fields rather than passing them through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* More progress\n\n* Align to tokens better in change editor\n\n* Improving diffs view\n\n* improve change design\n\n* Improving the pipelines draft pages\n\n* show drafts in rpcn list all the time\n\n* More draft progress\n\n* Improving draft flows\n\n* Improving pipeline controls\n\n* More draft work\n\n* Improvements from review\n\n* rpcn: review fixes for pipeline drafts\n\n- Autosave restore resets the form without keepDirty, so a settings-only\n  restore arms the unsaved-changes guard (regression test added).\n- Regenerate proto/gen/openapi for the pipeline proto changes; CI\n  dirty-checks it alongside the protogen dirs.\n- Spec: deploy order is free while the flag is off; only the flag flip\n  is ordered.\n- Trim comments to the constraint, not the rationale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: re-run all checks on a fresh head\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* spec: cloudv2 pins the branch''s BSR label, not a hand-generated shim\n\nAlso lands under frontend/**, which the verify and dispatch workflows\nfilter on; the previous empty commit ran none of them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* cleanup pass\n\n* More cleanup\n\n* restore a run control update\n\n* Fixing unsaved tab for dark mode\n\n* addressing most PR feedback\n\n* rpcn: stop a draft the dataplane deployed, and stop hiding leftover drafts\n\n`draft` is a plain proto3 bool, so a pre-drafts dataplane drops it in\ntransit and CreatePipeline deploys for real. The editor already noticed\n(it trusts the response state, not the flag it sent) but only said so in\na toast, leaving an unwanted pipeline consuming from its inputs and\nwriting to its outputs until a human read the message and acted. The\nwindow is real on every cluster upgrade: `console_image_tag` and\n`redpanda_connect_api_version` ride the same install pack but roll as\nseparate deployments. Issue the follow-up stop instead — the same one\n`run: ''stopped''` already does for a create on a pre-drafts dataplane —\nand keep the old copy for when that stop itself fails. The stop does not\nundo what already ran, so the copy says so.\n\nListPipelines now asks for drafts whether or not the feature is enabled.\nThe flag gates making drafts, not seeing the ones already made, and\nturning it back off stranded them: excluded from the list, so no Drafts\ntab and no row to delete from, while each still counted against the\ncluster''s pipeline quota. Every draft affordance in the row keys off the\nrow''s own state, and a pre-drafts dataplane drops the field, so the\nrequest is inert until there is a draft to show.\n\nAlso guard the list''s status-badge variant lookup, as the label beside it\nand the detail page''s badge already do: an unrecognised state fell\nthrough to StatusBadge''s `informative` default next to an \"Unknown\"\nlabel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* improvements from review\n\n* a few more draft improements\n\n* One more cleanup pass\n\n* Min height adjustment\n\n* Copy pass\n\n* Cleanup pass\n\n* change pipeline list order\n\n* feedback review\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"898fdb9906fafbc60d92cd44a5126ae19622d9e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/898fdb9906fafbc60d92cd44a5126ae19622d9e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/7c97ba04a8b0b3ac478aec9f9df4f01414683cd8","verification":{"payload":"tree 898fdb9906fafbc60d92cd44a5126ae19622d9e4\nparent da988430c5f0c08c047e5e5854b29642f8251283\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1790000239 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790000239 -0700\n\nUX-179 - rpcn: save pipelines as drafts (#2624)\n\n* RPCN: save pipelines as drafts, without deploying them\n\nSave used to mean Start, and was gated on validation passing. So work in\nprogress could not be parked — an invalid config would not save at all, and a\nrefresh or a misclicked Back button lost everything typed — and a finished\nconfig could not be saved without going live.\n\nA pipeline can now be saved as a draft: persisted, not running, zero compute,\nand stored exactly as typed even when it does not lint. Validation moves to the\nmoment it matters, which is Start.\n\nAPI (proto/redpanda/api/dataplane/v1/pipeline.proto), all additive:\n\n  - Pipeline.State.STATE_DRAFT, omitted from ListPipelines unless\n    Filter.include_drafts is set, so clients written before drafts existed never\n    receive a state they cannot render.\n  - PipelineCreate.draft, and PipelineUpdate.draft as an *assertion* rather than\n    a transition: it means \"I am editing a draft\", and the update fails with\n    FAILED_PRECONDITION if the pipeline has since been started. Without that,\n    \"Save draft\" could silently deploy a config to a running pipeline because a\n    teammate started it mid-edit.\n  - Filter.states for state filtering, and Pipeline.created_by / create_time /\n    update_time so a shared draft pool is attributable and its staleness visible.\n  - config_yaml loses its field-level `required` rule; the service enforces it\n    for anything that is not a draft, with a sentence instead of a proto field\n    path. Pipeline keeps the invariant as a message-level CEL rule.\n\nConsole:\n\n  - Split save actions per context: Save draft (new pipelines and drafts),\n    Save and start, Save (stopped), Apply and restart (running — saying \"Save\"\n    would hide the restart, and there is no apply-later to make that untrue).\n  - Drafts are ordinary rows in the pipeline list: Draft chip, Drafts tab with a\n    count, sorted first and by last edited, resume / start / delete actions, and\n    \"Edited 5m ago · by someone\" in place of the id.\n  - A draft''s own page explains itself instead of offering monitoring it cannot\n    have, and starting one routes lint failures into the editor where they are\n    fixable.\n  - Lint results are warnings on a draft and block only Start; an unnamed draft\n    is auto-named rather than refused.\n  - localStorage is repurposed from \"drafts\" to what it is actually good for:\n    crash recovery for the editor buffer, offered back after a refresh and\n    dropped on a successful save.\n  - New Changes lane (YAML | Visual | Changes N) diffing the saved config\n    against the editor, with the components touched listed and clickable, and a\n    header line stating what applying will cost.\n\nDeliberate decisions, with reasoning, in frontend/specs/rp-connect-pipeline-drafts.md:\ndraft as a distinct state rather than an unapplied-changes flag; annotation\nstorage rather than a CRD field; drafts count against the pipeline quota; drafts\nare named and names may collide; org-wide visibility because pipeline RBAC has no\nownership predicate; no expiry, staleness shown instead. It also records the\nfeature''s real limit — a draft ends at first start, so \"save without going live\"\nis solved for pipelines that have never run and not for the ones that have — and\nthe design for closing that with a pending revision.\n\nShips behind enable-rpcn-pipeline-drafts. The flag must stay off until the\nredpanda-connect-api carrying draft support is deployed: an older API ignores\n`draft` on create and deploys what the user asked to park. Note that\nbackend/pkg/protogen must be regenerated even though no Go here implements\nPipelineService — console-enterprise proxies through these types, and Connect''s\nJSON codec discards unknown fields rather than passing them through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* More progress\n\n* Align to tokens better in change editor\n\n* Improving diffs view\n\n* improve change design\n\n* Improving the pipelines draft pages\n\n* show drafts in rpcn list all the time\n\n* More draft progress\n\n* Improving draft flows\n\n* Improving pipeline controls\n\n* More draft work\n\n* Improvements from review\n\n* rpcn: review fixes for pipeline drafts\n\n- Autosave restore resets the form without keepDirty, so a settings-only\n  restore arms the unsaved-changes guard (regression test added).\n- Regenerate proto/gen/openapi for the pipeline proto changes; CI\n  dirty-checks it alongside the protogen dirs.\n- Spec: deploy order is free while the flag is off; only the flag flip\n  is ordered.\n- Trim comments to the constraint, not the rationale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: re-run all checks on a fresh head\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* spec: cloudv2 pins the branch''s BSR label, not a hand-generated shim\n\nAlso lands under frontend/**, which the verify and dispatch workflows\nfilter on; the previous empty commit ran none of them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* cleanup pass\n\n* More cleanup\n\n* restore a run control update\n\n* Fixing unsaved tab for dark mode\n\n* addressing most PR feedback\n\n* rpcn: stop a draft the dataplane deployed, and stop hiding leftover drafts\n\n`draft` is a plain proto3 bool, so a pre-drafts dataplane drops it in\ntransit and CreatePipeline deploys for real. The editor already noticed\n(it trusts the response state, not the flag it sent) but only said so in\na toast, leaving an unwanted pipeline consuming from its inputs and\nwriting to its outputs until a human read the message and acted. The\nwindow is real on every cluster upgrade: `console_image_tag` and\n`redpanda_connect_api_version` ride the same install pack but roll as\nseparate deployments. Issue the follow-up stop instead — the same one\n`run: ''stopped''` already does for a create on a pre-drafts dataplane —\nand keep the old copy for when that stop itself fails. The stop does not\nundo what already ran, so the copy says so.\n\nListPipelines now asks for drafts whether or not the feature is enabled.\nThe flag gates making drafts, not seeing the ones already made, and\nturning it back off stranded them: excluded from the list, so no Drafts\ntab and no row to delete from, while each still counted against the\ncluster''s pipeline quota. Every draft affordance in the row keys off the\nrow''s own state, and a pre-drafts dataplane drops the field, so the\nrequest is inert until there is a draft to show.\n\nAlso guard the list''s status-badge variant lookup, as the label beside it\nand the detail page''s badge already do: an unrecognised state fell\nthrough to StatusBadge''s `informative` default next to an \"Unknown\"\nlabel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* improvements from review\n\n* a few more draft improements\n\n* One more cleanup pass\n\n* Min height adjustment\n\n* Copy pass\n\n* Cleanup pass\n\n* change pipeline list order\n\n* feedback review\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsTxvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAknYQAHSCSdLpQ3fKS19jgdcwHYub\naauH7mSMKp04jFGDCD8V2NBb/NigTVhfy+TPUgNePJ3t85FASwgDN+9RKa5mc8C5\nmxPprpTpghJtlCNoqer32Y8U7TQBvGbXkdSiYaUJvnpq9a15KxMDZQEftXRrn+m/\nYy9nKgJfHbZcDDie8FvtUahrw6wnvB4IBLF2XntEM6qU7tHZXR9ndWCHPEdDTRRN\nx4RRC7s/8H6qZkUuduDcQ1qOavropULAJVfGEz0NnF7dR4AfI8/gxaN1/RGRJRln\nzDFaRLD9/QBCVX1U4e0fxKKmxtlmUYwO5go9g1xCh0RM6oF2csxA/4SR7p0l+Kt0\nweaLgBK73WXbhA54/CuuGRiajVqS4p5j/ZiOt9djfus+mg5L0lktoa5+OmLMypwE\ncfvb9+9wrhI05chZl/3KvE1+m5gtISOMp0WNK6w+IVlHel/83RdJA0BVgvbpfU2L\nqK/jvcAKCmtDjVqfWn1HODDtk5tDk63/JOobU91Ow/mdYpS91eQjbxK4Y2l3MUlq\nkKgIL3jd/I3oWS2K+ww8o8I8T5Cm+Ucu3mQZ6yFuKQS1vngi05l+z6ZzTz7cGu0m\naUsOYf7+AhS/YMetx2bZhqP1m2+YzmvLMcCYAPR6rN9arohGR3wNwentWgEliBDg\nGSQrS45u0PzC9OOBw0UC\n=G7Yp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T14:17:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/7c97ba04a8b0b3ac478aec9f9df4f01414683cd8","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKDdjOTdiYTA0YThiMGIzYWM0NzhhZWM5ZjlkZjRmMDE0MTQ2ODNjZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/da988430c5f0c08c047e5e5854b29642f8251283","sha":"da988430c5f0c08c047e5e5854b29642f8251283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/da988430c5f0c08c047e5e5854b29642f8251283"}],"sha":"7c97ba04a8b0b3ac478aec9f9df4f01414683cd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/7c97ba04a8b0b3ac478aec9f9df4f01414683cd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9860550?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/malinskibeniamin","id":9860550,"login":"malinskibeniamin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NjA1NTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malinskibeniamin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https