:"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/cdba8db7460c0926a0e39e435da55b12d41716a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/cdba8db7460c0926a0e39e435da55b12d41716a7","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGNkYmE4ZGI3NDYwYzA5MjZhMGUzOWU0MzVkYTU1YjEyZDQxNzE2YTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d","sha":"f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d"}],"sha":"cdba8db7460c0926a0e39e435da55b12d41716a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/cdba8db7460c0926a0e39e435da55b12d41716a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:06:09Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:06:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"frontend: stop the reassignment wizard failing silently when the bandwidth throttle is set (#2644)\n\n* frontend: stop the reassignment wizard failing silently\n\n\"Start Reassignment\" did nothing visible whenever the bandwidth throttle was\nabove the slider minimum. Redpanda rejects per-broker property patches\n(\"INVALID_CONFIG: Setting broker properties on named brokers is unsupported\")\nper resource inside an HTTP 200, so `setTrafficLimit` throws, and all three\nlayers dropped it: `catch (_err) { closeToast(toastRef); return false; }`,\nthen `if (!success) return false`, then `if (success) {…}` with no `else`.\nThe loading toast flashed and the wizard sat on step 3, with nothing in the\nconsole either — while the sibling handler''s copy promised \"See console for\nmore information\".\n\nBoth catches now surface the message, which is the part an operator needs,\nand the handler that promises console detail logs. Whether the throttle should\nbe offered on Redpanda at all is a product call, left alone: it cannot work\nthere, and the codebase already branches on `api.isRedpanda` in this feature.\n\nReported on #2639 by a reviewer testing against a 3-broker cluster; pre-existing\nrather than a Chakra-exit regression, so it is split out of that PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Error format fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe6eed81be3cd2dea7af6922035351741d82f76b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/fe6eed81be3cd2dea7af6922035351741d82f76b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d","verification":{"payload":"tree fe6eed81be3cd2dea7af6922035351741d82f76b\nparent 6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1789571169 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789571169 -0700\n\nfrontend: stop the reassignment wizard failing silently when the bandwidth throttle is set (#2644)\n\n* frontend: stop the reassignment wizard failing silently\n\n\"Start Reassignment\" did nothing visible whenever the bandwidth throttle was\nabove the slider minimum. Redpanda rejects per-broker property patches\n(\"INVALID_CONFIG: Setting broker properties on named brokers is unsupported\")\nper resource inside an HTTP 200, so `setTrafficLimit` throws, and all three\nlayers dropped it: `catch (_err) { closeToast(toastRef); return false; }`,\nthen `if (!success) return false`, then `if (success) {…}` with no `else`.\nThe loading toast flashed and the wizard sat on step 3, with nothing in the\nconsole either — while the sibling handler''s copy promised \"See console for\nmore information\".\n\nBoth catches now surface the message, which is the part an operator needs,\nand the handler that promises console detail logs. Whether the throttle should\nbe offered on Redpanda at all is a product call, left alone: it cannot work\nthere, and the codebase already branches on `api.isRedpanda` in this feature.\n\nReported on #2639 by a reviewer testing against a 3-broker cluster; pre-existing\nrather than a Chakra-exit regression, so it is split out of that PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Error format fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrBhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArLsQAJixiYjoWsgX+yFzJgd+D2mV\nrR3RK3IVMkOHCi4MHC6zo6Q3ydN+HuEzFDSvKx13ONrpa4NfLmk8r3ZONWb1UYvA\nH+zDKVOnO/NIPArOdhmDx6sH2VmLthCiQvpUMM48e2k2TalPYjEbPREbgvFj3n+t\nb6ukLGLVpVm1n/UoqJwuxLcQJNENpqzWL7HZaaF9cjEmM317Cs6XhVFqHEnUNJkj\nMYd/fltdZnItTgVgPbGzByqxWJER93t+mODMWIXBJi+deGr5KOKeuZ34BIylKK/V\nHhLqP7q183hg25sIG/Tdv7EFXrixK5MQd/bwvmD2Ky5LTQldnYe72FdhaV/ZVH+Q\nFhpvlBxgulU+AhK1v33IBMkcwXmN6osWdgg9RCsUpqxVkdDOmpgqqM3DDg+c8j+m\nh2UwNgweKny6z9VKKkfI0lXB+35/19TNuhE2Seq6Q9cVka6tDsqv/v7hJg2SIA5w\nrCJGopOGA37+wP9jeesHovTSH2DNmZBqQleP1k0eT7Crta0yHw4yzTl8hpQln15h\nnYqd/oWj5SZ0jp0CvsQ4vvWVYAPfHWDNBHeyB/3XP08lKBXxvxaqNWnfTV0XZraK\nuxWTKSuimxIyidbPlpcc59NYhqQt6RyF0iHYU11KU3VfwL8E7HXAIjP35C6PtT2i\n0fPs2prUB2VVqBi7aOHe\n=/yAy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T15:06:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGY5NDI1NWM5ZGYwOTQyYjEwYjEwNjcwYTM5ZGE4ODBiNmFiMDQ4NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7","sha":"6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7"}],"sha":"f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/f94255c9df0942b10b10670a39da880b6ab0486d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:03:11Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:03:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): hide the overview trial banner when the cluster holds an active Enterprise licence (UX-1488) (#2642)\n\nConsole''s own licence is a boot-time snapshot (console-enterprise runs\nCheckLicense once in main.go). A cluster that was on its built-in trial\nwhen Console started keeps reporting \"Console Trial\" after an Enterprise\nlicence is uploaded, and OverviewLicenseNotification only looked at TRIAL\nlicences, so it told a licensed cluster it was on an Enterprise trial.\n\nAn unexpired ENTERPRISE licence with source REDPANDA_CORE now suppresses\nthe trial notice. A Console-side Enterprise licence with the core still\non trial keeps the notice, since the copy is about the cluster.\n\nPre-existing since cec4becba (2025-07-21); the Chakra-exit PR #2634 only\nswapped the Alert primitives and did not touch this logic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60241bafdf85b12ca074f6b1e9e4108b81bb468a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/60241bafdf85b12ca074f6b1e9e4108b81bb468a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 60241bafdf85b12ca074f6b1e9e4108b81bb468a\nparent 98702bbb5d7888aac59e2b904f35e2c7f04aeffc\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1789567391 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789567391 -0700\n\nfix(frontend): hide the overview trial banner when the cluster holds an active Enterprise licence (UX-1488) (#2642)\n\nConsole''s own licence is a boot-time snapshot (console-enterprise runs\nCheckLicense once in main.go). A cluster that was on its built-in trial\nwhen Console started keeps reporting \"Console Trial\" after an Enterprise\nlicence is uploaded, and OverviewLicenseNotification only looked at TRIAL\nlicences, so it told a licensed cluster it was on an Enterprise trial.\n\nAn unexpired ENTERPRISE licence with source REDPANDA_CORE now suppresses\nthe trial notice. A Console-side Enterprise licence with the core still\non trial keeps the notice, since the copy is about the cluster.\n\nPre-existing since cec4becba (2025-07-21); the Chakra-exit PR #2634 only\nswapped the Alert primitives and did not touch this logic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqGfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuUUQABCDDn611XRwm3g/dwB/b7Q5\nqS/wWc4HRbngir7SIUlifSvv4eQcqJ+4wKI7xAKdjTkZIDPKdQl6qQDeNqh/8iia\nbRwyeXB7GIf+oVWoFTn6fkXg+wrN6wGDJtadFxhOJKicGaBAVP1Vutqfg0/bX1Tc\n70MbRSO0S/NaivNhXrZroQAZoPArH6l49FPrTFoEPF/JdG6hKKvz/j01ISudq9Ys\nA2CsIcLsl7J8b0UtUmWcTmcetAptbVcKQBeLMeJixnvrl/Sjzki9Ad7I7dr2X/UL\nEV6q6DRnzFnstCD/volPZnt4VTrzRGBdcBZizTIVk2coFKa5s2TvoHBh+jBVc7+m\nomWKv6QayUkYjrw1rV5iGpH9MwcMDbmiQAlMRk7Q4wr3KAmQpw+6hzP6ScZfdrTD\n799AUjqBp478LeUnmo8+H+SzUKMdXmSxLlMmjiCldVbZlYh5oMs1XCoKWr+xQJNJ\n97pfM43CxdkjrSnibFl4INHBDyyPrz1TYOt6KSN/iyoV6uSJSp+CGjVvq83a+CKo\nW9Bop6l+3ibaNxk+YeBR6GU/EuUfIO8Xei04HZozEjsaAkUnwaN6LQU4foGCrKX+\nX5pSiVJoMKlsnEBUfRMEaUJy5bv4I2MAp6kz9s4pJxbJtENR1IH71s3XM3glZ9od\nx1XQ49rbK1zW4JTDFJao\n=fke+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T14:03:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKDY2OTdmNWU0MDVkYzFmN2NkYjM3N2QwOTQwYmMxZDExZTZiY2UwZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/98702bbb5d7888aac59e2b904f35e2c7f04aeffc","sha":"98702bbb5d7888aac59e2b904f35e2c7f04aeffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/98702bbb5d7888aac59e2b904f35e2c7f04aeffc"}],"sha":"6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/6697f5e405dc1f7cdb377d0940bc1d11e6bce0d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/98702bbb5d7888aac59e2b904f35e2c7f04aeffc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:00:19Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:00:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"frontend: stop shipping the react-hook-form DevTool, and retire the Chakra references (#2652)\n\n* frontend: stop shipping the react-hook-form DevTool, and drop emotion\n\n<DevTool control={form.control} /> rendered unguarded inside the shadowlink\ncreate form, so every user of that page downloaded and mounted a debugging\noverlay. Removing the render lets @hookform/devtools go, and with it the last\ndeclared path to @emotion/react, @emotion/styled and uuid@8.3.2 — so the\nSNYK-JS-UUID-16133035 ignore, whose only remaining path it was, goes too.\n\nnode_modules/@emotion is now absent. `motion` declares @emotion/is-prop-valid\nas an optional peer and probes for it in a try/catch; that probe now misses, so\nits own prop filter takes over. Checked: every motion call site here passes\nonly motion''s own props (transition/initial/animate/exit) plus className,\nstyle and key, all of which that filter already handles.\n\nGates on a clean node_modules (a reinstall, not an incremental install, since\nbun leaves removed packages on disk): type:check clean, production build green,\n997 unit + 1438 integration + 1 federation passing, lint leaves no drift.\nBundle 43,796.7 -> 43,794.1 kB raw — the win here is the dependency and the\nretired advisory, not bytes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs+frontend: retire the Chakra references the migration left behind\n\nA repo-wide grep for \"chakra\" now returns six lines, all of them about the\ncloud-ui HOST''s Chakra, which is still live: the two globals.css border rules\n(the var name is emitted by the host''s emotion, so it cannot be renamed) and\nthe registry-upgrade note that tells the next upgrader to keep them in step.\nEverything else is gone.\n\nDocs: dropped the uninstalled packages from the no-legacy prohibited table and\nits violation examples, from the icon-system forbidden list, from the\nuse-ui-registry and ui-development rules, and from biome''s noRestrictedImports\n(the packages are not installed, so type:check already fails TS2307 on a\nre-added import). Deleted form-refactorer''s migration-examples.md — every\n\"Before\" half mapped a Chakra API, and common-patterns.md covers the Field\nmaterial more densely. Regenerated licenses/third_party_js.csv per\nlicenses/README.md: 686 -> 519 rows, and it no longer attributes Chakra,\nemotion or the eight libraries that left with them to the shipped product.\n\nComments: the migration comparisons are restated as the constraint that holds\nnow, across fifteen files, plus eight icon cross-references. Also two stale\nreferences the same sweep turned up — AGENTS.md said React 18.3 (it is 19.2.7)\nand three test-setup suppressions could no longer fire, two justified by React\n18 behaviour and two naming Radix, which is absent from the tree.\n\nGates: type:check clean, per-file lint:check zero net-new (verified by linting\nHEAD''s content at the same path), lint leaves no drift, biome config valid,\nunit + integration + federation green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"472e106f00eb2f1e2e8a874e6bd66b9346ef7276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/472e106f00eb2f1e2e8a874e6bd66b9346ef7276"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/98702bbb5d7888aac59e2b904f35e2c7f04aeffc","verification":{"payload":"tree 472e106f00eb2f1e2e8a874e6bd66b9346ef7276\nparent ac6d57d6324e1b7ada401bd1d84edecd6a697a7f\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1789567219 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789567219 -0700\n\nfrontend: stop shipping the react-hook-form DevTool, and retire the Chakra references (#2652)\n\n* frontend: stop shipping the react-hook-form DevTool, and drop emotion\n\n<DevTool control={form.control} /> rendered unguarded inside the shadowlink\ncreate form, so every user of that page downloaded and mounted a debugging\noverlay. Removing the render lets @hookform/devtools go, and with it the last\ndeclared path to @emotion/react, @emotion/styled and uuid@8.3.2 — so the\nSNYK-JS-UUID-16133035 ignore, whose only remaining path it was, goes too.\n\nnode_modules/@emotion is now absent. `motion` declares @emotion/is-prop-valid\nas an optional peer and probes for it in a try/catch; that probe now misses, so\nits own prop filter takes over. Checked: every motion call site here passes\nonly motion''s own props (transition/initial/animate/exit) plus className,\nstyle and key, all of which that filter already handles.\n\nGates on a clean node_modules (a reinstall, not an incremental install, since\nbun leaves removed packages on disk): type:check clean, production build green,\n997 unit + 1438 integration + 1 federation passing, lint leaves no drift.\nBundle 43,796.7 -> 43,794.1 kB raw — the win here is the dependency and the\nretired advisory, not bytes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs+frontend: retire the Chakra references the migration left behind\n\nA repo-wide grep for \"chakra\" now returns six lines, all of them about the\ncloud-ui HOST''s Chakra, which is still live: the two globals.css border rules\n(the var name is emitted by the host''s emotion, so it cannot be renamed) and\nthe registry-upgrade note that tells the next upgrader to keep them in step.\nEverything else is gone.\n\nDocs: dropped the uninstalled packages from the no-legacy prohibited table and\nits violation examples, from the icon-system forbidden list, from the\nuse-ui-registry and ui-development rules, and from biome''s noRestrictedImports\n(the packages are not installed, so type:check already fails TS2307 on a\nre-added import). Deleted form-refactorer''s migration-examples.md — every\n\"Before\" half mapped a Chakra API, and common-patterns.md covers the Field\nmaterial more densely. Regenerated licenses/third_party_js.csv per\nlicenses/README.md: 686 -> 519 rows, and it no longer attributes Chakra,\nemotion or the eight libraries that left with them to the shipped product.\n\nComments: the migration comparisons are restated as the constraint that holds\nnow, across fifteen files, plus eight icon cross-references. Also two stale\nreferences the same sweep turned up — AGENTS.md said React 18.3 (it is 19.2.7)\nand three test-setup suppressions could no longer fire, two justified by React\n18 behaviour and two naming Radix, which is absent from the tree.\n\nGates: type:check clean, per-file lint:check zero net-new (verified by linting\nHEAD''s content at the same path), lint leaves no drift, biome config valid,\nunit + integration + federation green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqDzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3bIQABvC7kKfCLxa3mzZoYZXxLqj\niUsg4JyTv5TvHzWpGKUGN1TMUSnBkqj2tGeUrLBG8d5N9YWSOTHQYJywfozriMAg\nals5XWCfHXeZFnc3zruWk1BfVcMdajbpDPGK0wPtZGv5+IHt9FeA5nLWwf1Y4TLL\nQz/jMffkU833eUin+Vdi2PsDHqzuQvEAy6q0Af0SdTm7zZqMbWepjAMpb7I7NftB\nNZN4oB30wZjEGrLtywRWKCOcpPh+L1Gt+wZ1Vx9WE7RVWCKKCPq/qa1OGBWUaxRp\n5EuA7V84WBBbNon7a+fTFHI+0OL3S2fHrsLk1YGRyT7gnpPvX0wfURNr4QigQFWw\nd5rQkO4l6k1i2aBCk7GVufySyepLX2TQ713swNAUByosxAbQ4LzA4UlZq3+BKlfw\n/o1oxe42oACXtQ