n  The Registry Slider counts thumbs from an array; a scalar `value` fell through\n  to `[min, max]`, so a second thumb rendered with no value — invisible but\n  focusable, and one arrow key from `maxReplicationTraffic = NaN` and a\n  `setReplicationThrottleRate(brokers, NaN)` call. It takes `[sliderValue]` now.\n- **The value bubble was positioned at `left: -Infinity%`** in the default\n  state: `maxReplicationTraffic` defaults to 0, so `log10` is `-Infinity`. The\n  slider value is clamped once and used for the thumb, the bubble and the label.\n- **Four net-new lint errors were shipping.** `bun run lint` is `ultracite fix`,\n  which exits 0 with errors still present — `lint:check` is the real gate. The\n  two `biome-ignore` comments named a rule that does not fire on those nodes, so\n  they suppressed nothing: the search overlay''s handlers move onto the `Input`\n  (the actual interactive element), the slider wrapper uses pointer events, and\n  the select-all checkbox uses `checked` + `indeterminate` instead of a nested\n  ternary. Added to the gate recipe.\n- **The throttle dialog''s footer collapsed to the right.**\n  `className=\"justify-between\"` loses to the variant''s own `sm:justify-end`\n  (tailwind-merge drops only the unprefixed class), so \"Remove throttle\" no\n  longer sat opposite Close/Apply. It uses `justify=\"between\"` now.\n- **Dialog widths had jumped.** `minW=\"5xl\"` (64rem) had become `full` (90vw,\n  ~1728px on the Playwright viewport) and `minW=\"3xl\"` (48rem) had become `xl`\n  (56rem); they are `xl` and `lg` respectively.\n- **step 1 lost click-to-sort on four columns.** Chakra painted the affordance\n  itself; restored with `DataTableColumnHeader`. The topic-name column is\n  explicitly `enableSorting: false` because its header *is* the search control,\n  so the model no longer claims sortability there is no UI for.\n- **Two columns shared `accessorKey: ''partitions''`**, so both resolved to the\n  same TanStack column id — duplicate React keys and column lookups hitting the\n  wrong def. Pre-existing, but the array is rewritten here.\n- The \"no partitions\" state was unframed text: the `Empty` root sets only\n  `border-dashed` and Preflight leaves the width at 0. It has a border, an icon\n  and a title now.\n- Popover content is `w-auto max-w-[500px]` — the Registry''s fixed `w-72` was\n  halving the width Chakra''s `size=\"auto\"` gave partition errors; `aria-expanded`\n  on both expanders; `size-4` on the chevrons was overridden by the button\n  variant''s own `[&_svg]` rule; icons from `components/icons`; the\n  active-reassignments `tableOptions` restated the DataTable''s own default.\n\nNot fixed, pre-existing and unrelated to the migration: \"Remove throttle\" reads\n`newThrottleValue` from the same render it just set, so it re-applies the current\nthrottle instead of clearing it. Identical on the base commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: scope the reassign-partitions stat assertions to the header row\n\nStep 1''s SelectionInfoBar repeats \"Leader Partitions\" and \"Total\nPartitions\", so the page-wide exact match in the new smoke spec tripped\nPlaywright strict mode on every run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): restore reassignment table sorting\n\n* frontend: reassign partitions — drop the orphaned SearchTitle\n\nThe sorting fix replaced the Topic column''s SearchTitle header with DataTableColumnHeader; that overlay was already unreachable (nothing ever set filterOpen), and kowl-table.tsx had no other importer. Delete it and the filterOpen flag it wrote to.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: reassign partitions — legacy table parity and Stat\n\n- The wizard tables paginate like the legacy DataTable again: 50 a page with the pager only past that (10 for the active-reassignments list, which had defaultPageSize 10), instead of 10 a page with a permanent footer or, on the review step, no paging at all.\n- Column size hints the Registry never reads are gone from all four tables.\n- Statistic wrapper replaced by the Registry Stat on the header row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: reassign partitions — verified review findings\n\n- ''Remove throttle'' re-applied the existing throttle: the handler read the stale value from the render closure. It now takes the value explicitly, and the topic-throttle dialog closes after a successful reset.\n- Partition-error popovers open on hover again, are titled (the dialog was unnamed), and take the width their text needs; the cancel-confirm popover is titled and its buttons are a spaced pair, not an attached group.\n- The Size column sorted on a field that does not exist; it reads logDirSummary.totalSizeBytes. The Progress column takes the slack again.\n- Progress bars paint brand for active state, not the Registry default; the slider bubble was background-on-background; the slider''s dead ''Unlimited'' end is gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: reassign partitions — final review\n\n- The remove-throttle dialog''s hover note is a Registry Tooltip; the hand-rolled bubble was clipped by the Dialog''s overflow.\n- The dead topic-search path (Highlighter and the quickSearch read) goes with the deleted SearchTitle.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; the wizard-steps note no longer misstates the Registry Stepper.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: reassign partitions — hiding off at table level\n\nenableHiding: false moves from every column into each step''s shared table\noptions, so a column added later cannot bring the header menu''s \"Hide\" item back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: reassign partitions — fourth review round\n\n- `react-highlight-words` and its types leave `package.json` and both lockfiles: `SearchTitle` was the last importer.\n- Wizard icons come from `components/icons` (adds `InboxIcon`).\n- The throttle-dialog tooltip gets a `TooltipProvider` (150 ms, not Base UI''s 600) and a focusable trigger.\n- Nav buttons use `min-w-56`/`ml-auto` classes and the link buttons `size=\"xs\"` instead of inline styles; the loading skeleton''s margin moves onto a wrapper.\n- `uiSettings.reassignment.quickSearch`/`pageSizeSelect` are dropped: step 1 no longer reads them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: take sorting off the review step''s derived Brokers column\n\n`accessorKey: ''Brokers After''` reads no field, so table-level `sorting` marked\nthe column sortable while its header — the accessor key, rendered by TanStack''s\ndefault header — offers nothing to trigger it. Name it and opt out, as the other\nderived columns do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: keep the reassign-partitions sort menus and throttle alive across the poll\n\n`PageComponent` force-updates the whole page on every store write, and the\nreassignments poll fires every three seconds. The column arrays were built\ninline in render, so each poll handed TanStack fresh `header`/`cell` function\nidentities — v9''s `flexRender` calls `createElement` on those, so React saw a\nnew component type and remounted the header cells, taking any open sort menu\nwith them. Sorting worked, but only if you beat the poll to the menu item. The\nfive wizard tables now build their columns once.\n\nThe bandwidth slider and the throttle summary also lagged input by up to a\npoll: `settings.maxReplicationTraffic = x` mutates the nested object the\n`uiSettings` proxy''s `get` returns, so `updateSettings()` never ran and no\nsubscriber was notified. Master''s Chakra slider hid half of it behind its own\ninternal drag state; the Registry Slider is fully controlled, so the thumb\nfroze too. The write now goes through the top-level trap and `StepReview`\nsubscribes to the value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: default the quotas and consumer-group lists to ten rows a page\n\nBoth were on `DEFAULT_TABLE_PAGE_SIZE` (50), the legacy-parity size the Chakra\nDataTable used. Ten is the Registry pager''s own default and the first of its\n\"Rows per page\" options, and both pages keep the choice in the URL, so a wider\npage is one select away and survives a reload.\n\nThe quotas route''s `pageSize` fallback moves with it: `.catch(50)` only fires\nfor a URL value outside the schema''s range, and landing on 50 when the page\nnow defaults to 10 would be its own surprise.\n\n`quota-pagination.spec.ts` hardcoded 50 as the app default for its \"no pager\nbelow one page\" check, so it moves too. That assertion is vacuous today for an\nunrelated reason — it locates `[aria-label=\"pagination\"]` while the Registry\npager labels its group `\"Pagination\"` — and the pager renders unconditionally\non that page, so the spec cannot see either state. Left as found; noted so it\ncan be fixed as a spec change rather than inside this one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoevwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuyoQALAyDddqteYpBWw3dZpgwENG\nlxfkBGVDftFMhaeGKaHV4hH92U7FdHvsRXZRh/RPQXPGU8bO0gCwHPV5MRlcZmHQ\n9r+FdZCH8jiaEyg1XKwkyoh7GLbDZijLhu8VXlVVWiDxBVsH1nbdg7vWS+/1U/ch\naq5988nvf70pae1+qQlq5NC5u3ablePheW2KCEc5zon+5JMejRPsC9YhUC2HaGa9\nmUBRQgrtoDe0QuQPayax3Y8k8HE5r5Dg0H2kYJKzDM8C9DomaR8S80gE+APt61Mj\n7mW11RNOp9wfPzdo7FC+jmGTVSL6FyW9N0plcZQLOCX6oZqkFgZ0qJTJzDwmsTOo\nAzmBjckzcndgP0luiaxyw3yvXmgF3DZDaqwW//Uw7J+tVZc/ErHzLz0PIimbGUMW\nVbPaFGalQEuMREKhONVHhdOzPp+427bf22YJQHpOjmhC1KeREhhCWnJ96XLXIYQt\njMYkj4IInH/DjoaGJoJHKsptZq4FwzmXnPP7H8fyRkG3LwH1DEFilc1bS5T/uw1W\nmZeAKhtqMi+hevdM37eOkVS8vB76YSp574W5YD0UI80Nf33ea723rDUzFBu/8FXO\npS1DiInIf29JOOitKo/BGlHErKQ1QdelBi1NIWYFsRX1F3dsRV7JoAEsw6K7bLXt\nEtvEZvdnlFoVaoTX3lvk\n=Bfsm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T23:29:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/a6d71bef0395498f8141713e845590fb500605d8","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGE2ZDcxYmVmMDM5NTQ5OGY4MTQxNzEzZTg0NTU5MGZiNTAwNjA1ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b","sha":"851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b"}],"sha":"a6d71bef0395498f8141713e845590fb500605d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/a6d71bef0395498f8141713e845590fb500605d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:17:07Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:17:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 11/14] frontend: the Kafka Connect pages on Registry components (#2638)\n\n* frontend: the Kafka Connect dynamic-ui engine on Registry components\n\nEight files. This is the schema-driven form renderer: a connector''s config\nschema arrives from the backend and `PropertyComponent` picks an input per\n`definition.type`. The schema contract does not change and neither does the\nvalue written back — `updatePropertyValue` still writes `property.value` and\ncalls `notifyChange()`.\n\nOld -> new, by file:\n\n- forms/error-wrapper — Chakra `FormField` -> Field + FieldLabel +\n  FieldDescription + FieldError. This is the shell *every* property renders\n  through, so it is the widest hunk by reach. Its `onClick` stays on the field:\n  a property can carry several validation errors and clicking is what advances\n  `currentErrorIndex` to show the next one.\n- property-component — `NumberInput` -> `Input type=\"number\"`. Chakra''s emitted\n  a number; a native number input emits a string, so this coerces with\n  `valueAsNumber` or the config would carry `\"3\"` where the connector expects\n  `3`. `RadioGroup options={…}` -> composed RadioGroupItem + Label (Base UI has\n  no options prop), `Switch isChecked/onChange` -> `checked/onCheckedChange`.\n- forms/secret-input — the Registry Input already owns the reveal toggle for\n  `type=\"password\"` and disables it while read-only, which is exactly the state\n  an existing secret sits in before Edit, so the hand-rolled InputGroup +\n  InputRightElement + `useBoolean` all go. `key` on the Input is what re-masks\n  on Undo: the toggle''s state lives inside the Input, so leaving editing has to\n  remount it or Undo would leave the restored secret in plain text.\n- forms/topic-input — `Select isMulti` -> SimpleMultiSelect (string-valued, and\n  the property is a comma-joined string either way), FormControl/FormHelperText/\n  FormErrorMessage -> Field/FieldDescription/FieldError, labelled Checkbox.\n- list — the rename hint Tooltip was `isOpen={hasFocus}`, i.e. controlled by\n  focus rather than hover; it stays controlled via `open`.\n- property-group — Chakra''s `Accordion items={…}` -> composed\n  AccordionItem/Trigger/Content. **The sub-group heading rendered its name\n  twice**; that is fixed here rather than carried across.\n- components, connector-step — layout props and `Skeleton noOfLines` ->\n  `SkeletonText lines`.\n\nconnector.spec.ts exercises this end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: drop two dead biome suppressions from the dynamic-ui migration\n\n`ultracite check` reports both as `suppressions/unused`: `onClick` on a\n*component* (Field, FieldError) does not trip the bare-element a11y rules the\nignores named, so they suppressed nothing and only implied a hazard that is not\nthere. `bun run lint` is `ultracite fix` and exits 0 on these, which is why they\nsurvived the first pass — `lint:check` is the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the dynamic-ui engine migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch. The worst two were about the config\nthis form actually submits:\n\n- **Numeric properties changed wire type, and could submit `null`.** The comment\n  had it exactly backwards: Chakra''s `NumberInput.onChange` is\n  `(valueAsString, valueAsNumber)` and the old code took the *first* argument —\n  a string. `getConfigObject` sends `p.value` as-is and compares it `===` against\n  `default_value` to suppress untouched defaults, and `sanitizeDefaultValue`\n  numbers only the INT/LONG/SHORT defaults — so storing a number changed which\n  properties get sent, inconsistently across the numeric types. Clearing a field\n  also stored `NaN`, which `JSON.stringify` turns into `null` in both the JSON\n  tab and the validate/create request. Back to the string.\n- **Every property control was unlabeled.** Chakra''s `FormControl` generated an\n  id and wired `FormLabel htmlFor` to it; the Registry `Field` does not. A\n  derived `property-<name>` id now goes to both the control and the label, so\n  clicking a label focuses its control and a screen reader gets a name instead\n  of a bare \"textbox\" — on every field of the create/edit connector form.\n\nThe rest:\n\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP properties render inline with their label again\n  (Chakra''s FormField special-cased a Switch child), and the control is wrapped\n  so `Field`''s vertical `[&>*]:w-full` cannot stretch a Switch pill to the full\n  row.\n- Property documentation goes back above the control, where FormField had it.\n- **The Registry `Input` discards a caller''s `style`** — it applies its own\n  after the prop spread — so both list inputs had silently lost their flex\n  sizing. Moved to `containerClassName`, which is also what the\n  ui-development rule requires.\n- The numeric steppers are back (`showStepControls`; the Registry needs asking\n  where Chakra shipped them by default), with `step=\"any\"` for DOUBLE/FLOAT,\n  which the Registry otherwise pins to 1 — the browser then marks any\n  non-integer value invalid.\n- **`.ghostInput`''s transparent border needs `!important`** to beat the Registry\n  Input''s `!border-input`; without it the reorderable transform-name inputs\n  rendered permanently bordered on a transparent ground.\n- A selected topic missing from `api.topics` rendered a chip whose × did\n  nothing; the options are the union of the topic list and the current\n  selection, so a deleted topic stays removable.\n- `topics-use-regex` was a fixed id on a component rendered once per property\n  group — `useId()` now.\n- The Edit-secret tooltip gets a `TooltipProvider`; without one it inherited\n  Base UI''s 600ms delay instead of the app''s 150ms.\n- `inputWrapper${cond ? ''hasError'' : ''''}` was missing a space, so\n  `.inputWrapper.hasError` never matched and the new-entry validation message\n  rendered at opacity 0. Pre-existing, one character, inside a function this\n  branch edits.\n- Margins off Registry components, and `mx-4` on a Label dropped — it was a\n  Chakra-only hack to widen a click target inside its own radio label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the per-option `_field` test ids on the connector radio groups\n\nChakra''s RadioGroup rendered a RadioCard per option with\ndata-testid=\"${value}_field\"; the composed RadioGroupItem replacement\ndropped it and broke the kafka-connect e2e JSON-editor test, which\nclicks `json_field`. The dynamic property radio group gets the same\ntreatment for parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): preserve connector input values and labels\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — final review\n\n- Radio-group properties are named: a radiogroup div is not labelable, so the label carries an id and the group points at it with aria-labelledby.\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP fields are vertical again; Chakra''s FormField never inlined them (its Switch check never matched), so the horizontal Field row was a layout change, not parity.\n- The list ghost input''s transparent border is a Tailwind class on the element: an unlayered !important in index.scss lost to the Registry''s layered !border-input, so the field rendered bordered. The new-entry input fits its 29px row.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; the numeric-input comment no longer claims an empty field would render NaN.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — fourth review round\n\n- Heading/description gaps use `mt-*` on the following element: the `mb-*` they replaced is inert until PR 8 moves the margin reset into `@layer base`.\n- Required properties carry `required`/`aria-required` again (Chakra''s FormControl stamped them).\n- The transforms list''s new-entry input takes the property id so its label resolves.\n- The password test reveals the value before Undo, so it fails without the remount `key`.\n- `.stringList` rows and buttons use theme tokens instead of literal greys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: the Kafka Connect pages on Registry components\n\nSix files, ~3,200 LOC — the largest area in the codebase. Stacked on PR 10\n(the dynamic-ui engine), which these pages render.\n\nReading order: connector-box-card and cluster-details are the shallow ones,\nthen overview, then helper (shared building blocks all three pages import),\nthen connector-details and create-connector.\n\nThe hunks that carry judgement:\n\n- helper.tsx `ConfirmModal` — Chakra''s AlertDialog took\n  `leastDestructiveRef={cancelRef}` to put initial focus on \"No\". Base UI has\n  no such prop, so the ref goes and Cancel is placed first in the footer, which\n  is what gets it the initial focus.\n- connector-details `NoEditPermissionTooltip` — Chakra''s Tooltip took\n  `isDisabled` to suppress itself when the permission was present; Base UI has\n  no equivalent, so the wrapper renders its child bare instead. It also wraps\n  the trigger in a span: a disabled button fires no pointer events, so the\n  tooltip would never open.\n- connector-details tabs — Chakra''s `Tabs` took `isDisabled` as a *reason\n  string*. The app''s Tabs wrapper takes a boolean, so the reason moves to a\n  tooltip on the trigger and the Logs tab keeps its explanation.\n- connector-details logs — adds the expander column Chakra''s DataTable used to\n  inject for `subComponent`, and drops the controlled SortingState (nothing\n  else read it).\n- create-connector''s filter tabs render empty panels; the card grid below reacts\n  to the tab key. Called out in a comment so it does not read as a mistake.\n- The creating-connector dialog has no `onOpenChange`: it deliberately cannot\n  be dismissed while the request is in flight, as before.\n- The connector-details overview grid keeps `gridTemplateAreas` inline —\n  Tailwind has no arbitrary utility for it.\n\n`ConnectorClass`''s hover Popover becomes a click Popover with a real button\ntrigger; it was a hover-triggered popover with a close button, which is neither\na tooltip nor a popover cleanly.\n\nconnector.spec.ts and connect-cluster.spec.ts exercise these end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the Kafka Connect pages migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The connector status stripe painted nothing.** `statusColors` held Chakra\n  theme tokens (`green.500`), which only resolve through a Chakra style prop —\n  as raw CSS they are invalid and the declaration is dropped. They are now\n  `bg-*-strong` utilities applied as a class, so the stripe has a colour for\n  every status again.\n- **The disabled Logs tab could never explain itself.** The trigger sets\n  `aria-disabled:pointer-events-none`, which cascades to the nested tooltip\n  trigger — so the \"Logs topic … does not exist\" tooltip, the whole point of\n  moving the reason there, was unreachable. The span re-enables pointer events.\n- **Four tables lost click-to-sort.** Chakra''s DataTable painted the sort\n  affordance on every header itself; the Registry only sorts through\n  `DataTableColumnHeader`. Restored on the plugin, connector, task, log and\n  cluster-task tables, with `enableSorting: false` on the columns whose cells\n  are derived (Tasks, Cluster) and `enableHiding: false` throughout — these\n  pages have no `DataTableViewOptions`, so a hidden column could not come back.\n- **The \"Creating connector...\" dialog showed a close X that did nothing.**\n  `DialogContent` renders one by default and the dialog is deliberately\n  controlled with no `onOpenChange`; `showCloseButton={false}` restores the\n  Chakra original, which had no close affordance.\n- **\"Create connector\" stopped being a button.** `tests/shared/connector.utils.ts`\n  clicks it with `getByRole(''button'')`, which the original `<Link><Button>`\n  produced — so the nesting is back. (The Registry Button also takes no route\n  `params`, so `as={Link}` could not carry this one.) Note this is the opposite\n  contract to the debug-bundle and license links, which their own helpers read\n  as links — the test decides, per call site.\n- **`ConfirmModal` clipped long API errors.** `AlertDialogContent` is\n  `overflow-hidden max-h-[85vh]`; the bare `<div>` had no scroll container, so a\n  long error pushed the No/Retry footer out of view with no scrollbar. It is an\n  `AlertDialogDescription` with `min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`, which also restores\n  `aria-describedby`.\n- **The class-name popover overflowed.** `PopoverContent` is a fixed `w-72`\n  where Chakra''s `size=\"stretch\"` sized to content, so long fully-qualified\n  connector classes spilled outside the popup.\n- **The connector-error dialog lost JSON highlighting** — `SimpleCodeBlock` is\n  the drop-in that keeps `language`.\n- `NotConfigured` puts its heading in `EmptyTitle` and its CTA in\n  `EmptyContent`, matching the already-migrated `SchemaNotConfiguredPage`\n  instead of stranding the prose outside an oversized empty box.\n- The clear button stays mounted (`InputEnd` never resets the padding it\n  measured); `ConnectorsList`''s columns are memoised on `clusterName` rather\n  than rebuilt per keystroke; two `tableOptions` restated the DataTable''s own\n  default; icons come from `components/icons`; margins move off Registry\n  components and hand-rolled `text-[1rem]`/`text-[1.4em]`/`text-[0.85em]` onto\n  the named rungs, per the ui-development rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — status stripe on rounded-full, radius on the docs anchor\n\n- rounded-[3px] on the 5px status stripe (flagged by the lookout audit) becomes rounded-full, which is the same shape.\n- The docs anchor on the not-configured page adds rounded-md; the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — second review round\n\n- Both search boxes use the shared SearchInput (clear refocuses, click-through when empty, / and Escape restored).\n- Logs tab: columns are memoised (a fresh array per 200 ms poll tick re-created every header and cell, so the sort menu never stayed open), rows are keyed by partition+offset, column sizes the Registry ignores are gone and the Value column takes the slack again. ''View details'' carries the click instead of the whole banner.\n- helper: the connector-class popover opens on hover as before; the confirm dialog''s description was a flex column that stacked its inline sentence; the trace dialog title checks undefined, not null; the trace box is a SimpleCodeBlock like the connector error dialog; statusColors covers STOPPED and uses the disabled fill token; the docs CTA is a Registry Button; Statistic wrapper replaced by Stat.\n- Alerts use AlertTitle instead of a hand-rolled heading (five places). Tasks tab sorts on connectorName (the accessor pointed at a field that does not exist). InlineCode replaces the legacy .codeBox span.\n- Tables paginate like the legacy DataTable (50, pager only past that) on the plugin list and the three overview tabs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — final review\n\n- Connector-error dialog highlights its JSON again (SyncCodeBlock); the SimpleCodeBlock swap had dropped it.\n- Heading spacing uses padding: an unlayered margin reset in index.scss makes mb-* on bare headings inert until #2636 lands.\n- Connectors list and tasks table stay at ten a page (their legacy defaultPageSize), pager only past that.\n- Tasks tab columns are module-level so the sort menus survive the tab''s re-renders; the logs Value column is not sortable.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; shared SearchInput copy refreshed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: connect pages — hiding off at table level\n\nenableHiding: false moves from every column into each table''s options, so a\ncolumn added later cannot bring the header menu''s \"Hide\" item back. The two\nten-a-page tables (cluster connectors, connector tasks) get their own options\nobject rather than the 50-a-page one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — fourth review round\n\n- The four new tooltips open at the app''s 150 ms (`delayDuration`), not Base UI''s 600.\n- The confirm dialog''s pending button keeps its accessible name (`aria-label`).\n- Heading rungs match the Chakra sizes they replaced (create heading and status card `xl`, \"Connector Properties\" `lg`).\n- The validation warning keeps the `my-4` its sibling alerts have.\n- The logs table shows its pager only with rows, as the legacy table did.\n- The not-configured docs CTA is an anchor again (`buttonVariants` + `rounded-md`).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f164f8ff05cd03f6f7e62f1c96d76330da5478b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/f164f8ff05cd03f6f7e62f1c96d76330da5478b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b","verification":{"payload":"tree f164f8ff05cd03f6f7e62f1c96d76330da5478b7\nparent d206252d31fce82011c8e7758cd8fc2ccb4fe5c9\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788992227 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788992227 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 11/14] frontend: the Kafka Connect pages on Registry components (#2638)\n\n* frontend: the Kafka Connect dynamic-ui engine on Registry components\n\nEight files. This is the schema-driven form renderer: a connector''s config\nschema arrives from the backend and `PropertyComponent` picks an input per\n`definition.type`. The schema contract does not change and neither does the\nvalue written back — `updatePropertyValue` still writes `property.value` and\ncalls `notifyChange()`.\n\nOld -> new, by file:\n\n- forms/error-wrapper — Chakra `FormField` -> Field + FieldLabel +\n  FieldDescription + FieldError. This is the shell *every* property renders\n  through, so it is the widest hunk by reach. Its `onClick` stays on the field:\n  a property can carry several validation errors and clicking is what advances\n  `currentErrorIndex` to show the next one.\n- property-component — `NumberInput` -> `Input type=\"number\"`. Chakra''s emitted\n  a number; a native number input emits a string, so this coerces with\n  `valueAsNumber` or the config would carry `\"3\"` where the connector expects\n  `3`. `RadioGroup options={…}` -> composed RadioGroupItem + Label (Base UI has\n  no options prop), `Switch isChecked/onChange` -> `checked/onCheckedChange`.\n- forms/secret-input — the Registry Input already owns the reveal toggle for\n  `type=\"password\"` and disables it while read-only, which is exactly the state\n  an existing secret sits in before Edit, so the hand-rolled InputGroup +\n  InputRightElement + `useBoolean` all go. `key` on the Input is what re-masks\n  on Undo: the toggle''s state lives inside the Input, so leaving editing has to\n  remount it or Undo would leave the restored secret in plain text.\n- forms/topic-input — `Select isMulti` -> SimpleMultiSelect (string-valued, and\n  the property is a comma-joined string either way), FormControl/FormHelperText/\n  FormErrorMessage -> Field/FieldDescription/FieldError, labelled Checkbox.\n- list — the rename hint Tooltip was `isOpen={hasFocus}`, i.e. controlled by\n  focus rather than hover; it stays controlled via `open`.\n- property-group — Chakra''s `Accordion items={…}` -> composed\n  AccordionItem/Trigger/Content. **The sub-group heading rendered its name\n  twice**; that is fixed here rather than carried across.\n- components, connector-step — layout props and `Skeleton noOfLines` ->\n  `SkeletonText lines`.\n\nconnector.spec.ts exercises this end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: drop two dead biome suppressions from the dynamic-ui migration\n\n`ultracite check` reports both as `suppressions/unused`: `onClick` on a\n*component* (Field, FieldError) does not trip the bare-element a11y rules the\nignores named, so they suppressed nothing and only implied a hazard that is not\nthere. `bun run lint` is `ultracite fix` and exits 0 on these, which is why they\nsurvived the first pass — `lint:check` is the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the dynamic-ui engine migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch. The worst two were about the config\nthis form actually submits:\n\n- **Numeric properties changed wire type, and could submit `null`.** The comment\n  had it exactly backwards: Chakra''s `NumberInput.onChange` is\n  `(valueAsString, valueAsNumber)` and the old code took the *first* argument —\n  a string. `getConfigObject` sends `p.value` as-is and compares it `===` against\n  `default_value` to suppress untouched defaults, and `sanitizeDefaultValue`\n  numbers only the INT/LONG/SHORT defaults — so storing a number changed which\n  properties get sent, inconsistently across the numeric types. Clearing a field\n  also stored `NaN`, which `JSON.stringify` turns into `null` in both the JSON\n  tab and the validate/create request. Back to the string.\n- **Every property control was unlabeled.** Chakra''s `FormControl` generated an\n  id and wired `FormLabel htmlFor` to it; the Registry `Field` does not. A\n  derived `property-<name>` id now goes to both the control and the label, so\n  clicking a label focuses its control and a screen reader gets a name instead\n  of a bare \"textbox\" — on every field of the create/edit connector form.\n\nThe rest:\n\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP properties render inline with their label again\n  (Chakra''s FormField special-cased a Switch child), and the control is wrapped\n  so `Field`''s vertical `[&>*]:w-full` cannot stretch a Switch pill to the full\n  row.\n- Property documentation goes back above the control, where FormField had it.\n- **The Registry `Input` discards a caller''s `style`** — it applies its own\n  after the prop spread — so both list inputs had silently lost their flex\n  sizing. Moved to `containerClassName`, which is also what the\n  ui-development rule requires.\n- The numeric steppers are back (`showStepControls`; the Registry needs asking\n  where Chakra shipped them by default), with `step=\"any\"` for DOUBLE/FLOAT,\n  which the Registry otherwise pins to 1 — the browser then marks any\n  non-integer value invalid.\n- **`.ghostInput`''s transparent border needs `!important`** to beat the Registry\n  Input''s `!border-input`; without it the reorderable transform-name inputs\n  rendered permanently bordered on a transparent ground.\n- A selected topic missing from `api.topics` rendered a chip whose × did\n  nothing; the options are the union of the topic list and the current\n  selection, so a deleted topic stays removable.\n- `topics-use-regex` was a fixed id on a component rendered once per property\n  group — `useId()` now.\n- The Edit-secret tooltip gets a `TooltipProvider`; without one it inherited\n  Base UI''s 600ms delay instead of the app''s 150ms.\n- `inputWrapper${cond ? ''hasError'' : ''''}` was missing a space, so\n  `.inputWrapper.hasError` never matched and the new-entry validation message\n  rendered at opacity 0. Pre-existing, one character, inside a function this\n  branch edits.\n- Margins off Registry components, and `mx-4` on a Label dropped — it was a\n  Chakra-only hack to widen a click target inside its own radio label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the per-option `_field` test ids on the connector radio groups\n\nChakra''s RadioGroup rendered a RadioCard per option with\ndata-testid=\"${value}_field\"; the composed RadioGroupItem replacement\ndropped it and broke the kafka-connect e2e JSON-editor test, which\nclicks `json_field`. The dynamic property radio group gets the same\ntreatment for parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): preserve connector input values and labels\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — final review\n\n- Radio-group properties are named: a radiogroup div is not labelable, so the label carries an id and the group points at it with aria-labelledby.\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP fields are vertical again; Chakra''s FormField never inlined them (its Switch check never matched), so the horizontal Field row was a layout change, not parity.\n- The list ghost input''s transparent border is a Tailwind class on the element: an unlayered !important in index.scss lost to the Registry''s layered !border-input, so the field rendered bordered. The new-entry input fits its 29px row.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; the numeric-input comment no longer claims an empty field would render NaN.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — fourth review round\n\n- Heading/description gaps use `mt-*` on the following element: the `mb-*` they replaced is inert until PR 8 moves the margin reset into `@layer base`.\n- Required properties carry `required`/`aria-required` again (Chakra''s FormControl stamped them).\n- The transforms list''s new-entry input takes the property id so its label resolves.\n- The password test reveals the value before Undo, so it fails without the remount `key`.\n- `.stringList` rows and buttons use theme tokens instead of literal greys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: the Kafka Connect pages on Registry components\n\nSix files, ~3,200 LOC — the largest area in the codebase. Stacked on PR 10\n(the dynamic-ui engine), which these pages render.\n\nReading order: connector-box-card and cluster-details are the shallow ones,\nthen overview, then helper (shared building blocks all three pages import),\nthen connector-details and create-connector.\n\nThe hunks that carry judgement:\n\n- helper.tsx `ConfirmModal` — Chakra''s AlertDialog took\n  `leastDestructiveRef={cancelRef}` to put initial focus on \"No\". Base UI has\n  no such prop, so the ref goes and Cancel is placed first in the footer, which\n  is what gets it the initial focus.\n- connector-details `NoEditPermissionTooltip` — Chakra''s Tooltip took\n  `isDisabled` to suppress itself when the permission was present; Base UI has\n  no equivalent, so the wrapper renders its child bare instead. It also wraps\n  the trigger in a span: a disabled button fires no pointer events, so the\n  tooltip would never open.\n- connector-details tabs — Chakra''s `Tabs` took `isDisabled` as a *reason\n  string*. The app''s Tabs wrapper takes a boolean, so the reason moves to a\n  tooltip on the trigger and the Logs tab keeps its explanation.\n- connector-details logs — adds the expander column Chakra''s DataTable used to\n  inject for `subComponent`, and drops the controlled SortingState (nothing\n  else read it).\n- create-connector''s filter tabs render empty panels; the card grid below reacts\n  to the tab key. Called out in a comment so it does not read as a mistake.\n- The creating-connector dialog has no `onOpenChange`: it deliberately cannot\n  be dismissed while the request is in flight, as before.\n- The connector-details overview grid keeps `gridTemplateAreas` inline —\n  Tailwind has no arbitrary utility for it.\n\n`ConnectorClass`''s hover Popover becomes a click Popover with a real button\ntrigger; it was a hover-triggered popover with a close button, which is neither\na tooltip nor a popover cleanly.\n\nconnector.spec.ts and connect-cluster.spec.ts exercise these end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the Kafka Connect pages migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The connector status stripe painted nothing.** `statusColors` held Chakra\n  theme tokens (`green.500`), which only resolve through a Chakra style prop —\n  as raw CSS they are invalid and the declaration is dropped. They are now\n  `bg-*-strong` utilities applied as a class, so the stripe has a colour for\n  every status again.\n- **The disabled Logs tab could never explain itself.** The trigger sets\n  `aria-disabled:pointer-events-none`, which cascades to the nested tooltip\n  trigger — so the \"Logs topic … does not exist\" tooltip, the whole point of\n  moving the reason there, was unreachable. The span re-enables pointer events.\n- **Four tables lost click-to-sort.** Chakra''s DataTable painted the sort\n  affordance on every header itself; the Registry only sorts through\n  `DataTableColumnHeader`. Restored on the plugin, connector, task, log and\n  cluster-task tables, with `enableSorting: false` on the columns whose cells\n  are derived (Tasks, Cluster) and `enableHiding: false` throughout — these\n  pages have no `DataTableViewOptions`, so a hidden column could not come back.\n- **The \"Creating connector...\" dialog showed a close X that did nothing.**\n  `DialogContent` renders one by default and the dialog is deliberately\n  controlled with no `onOpenChange`; `showCloseButton={false}` restores the\n  Chakra original, which had no close affordance.\n- **\"Create connector\" stopped being a button.** `tests/shared/connector.utils.ts`\n  clicks it with `getByRole(''button'')`, which the original `<Link><Button>`\n  produced — so the nesting is back. (The Registry Button also takes no route\n  `params`, so `as={Link}` could not carry this one.) Note this is the opposite\n  contract to the debug-bundle and license links, which their own helpers read\n  as links — the test decides, per call site.\n- **`ConfirmModal` clipped long API errors.** `AlertDialogContent` is\n  `overflow-hidden max-h-[85vh]`; the bare `<div>` had no scroll container, so a\n  long error pushed the No/Retry footer out of view with no scrollbar. It is an\n  `AlertDialogDescription` with `min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`, which also restores\n  `aria-describedby`.\n- **The class-name popover overflowed.** `PopoverContent` is a fixed `w-72`\n  where Chakra''s `size=\"stretch\"` sized to content, so long fully-qualified\n  connector classes spilled outside the popup.\n- **The connector-error dialog lost JSON highlighting** — `SimpleCodeBlock` is\n  the drop-in that keeps `language`.\n- `NotConfigured` puts its heading in `EmptyTitle` and its CTA in\n  `EmptyContent`, matching the already-migrated `SchemaNotConfiguredPage`\n  instead of stranding the prose outside an oversized empty box.\n- The clear button stays mounted (`InputEnd` never resets the padding it\n  measured); `ConnectorsList`''s columns are memoised on `clusterName` rather\n  than rebuilt per keystroke; two `tableOptions` restated the DataTable''s own\n  default; icons come from `components/icons`; margins move off Registry\n  components and hand-rolled `text-[1rem]`/`text-[1.4em]`/`text-[0.85em]` onto\n  the named rungs, per the ui-development rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — status stripe on rounded-full, radius on the docs anchor\n\n- rounded-[3px] on the 5px status stripe (flagged by the lookout audit) becomes rounded-full, which is the same shape.\n- The docs anchor on the not-configured page adds rounded-md; the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — second review round\n\n- Both search boxes use the shared SearchInput (clear refocuses, click-through when empty, / and Escape restored).\n- Logs tab: columns are memoised (a fresh array per 200 ms poll tick re-created every header and cell, so the sort menu never stayed open), rows are keyed by partition+offset, column sizes the Registry ignores are gone and the Value column takes the slack again. ''View details'' carries the click instead of the whole banner.\n- helper: the connector-class popover opens on hover as before; the confirm dialog''s description was a flex column that stacked its inline sentence; the trace dialog title checks undefined, not null; the trace box is a SimpleCodeBlock like the connector error dialog; statusColors covers STOPPED and uses the disabled fill token; the docs CTA is a Registry Button; Statistic wrapper replaced by Stat.\n- Alerts use AlertTitle instead of a hand-rolled heading (five places). Tasks tab sorts on connectorName (the accessor pointed at a field that does not exist). InlineCode replaces the legacy .codeBox span.\n- Tables paginate like the legacy DataTable (50, pager only past that) on the plugin list and the three overview tabs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — final review\n\n- Connector-error dialog highlights its JSON again (SyncCodeBlock); the SimpleCodeBlock swap had dropped it.\n- Heading spacing uses padding: an unlayered margin reset in index.scss makes mb-* on bare headings inert until #2636 lands.\n- Connectors list and tasks table stay at ten a page (their legacy defaultPageSize), pager only past that.\n- Tasks tab columns are module-level so the sort menus survive the tab''s re-renders; the logs Value column is not sortable.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; shared SearchInput copy refreshed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: connect pages — hiding off at table level\n\nenableHiding: false moves from every column into each table''s options, so a\ncolumn added later cannot bring the header menu''s \"Hide\" item back. The two\nten-a-page tables (cluster connectors, connector tasks) get their own options\nobject rather than the 50-a-page one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect pages — fourth review round\n\n- The four new tooltips open at the app''s 150 ms (`delayDuration`), not Base UI''s 600.\n- The confirm dialog''s pending button keeps its accessible name (`aria-label`).\n- Heading rungs match the Chakra sizes they replaced (create heading and status card `xl`, \"Connector Properties\" `lg`).\n- The validation warning keeps the `my-4` its sibling alerts have.\n- The logs table shows its pager only with rows, as the legacy table did.\n- The not-configured docs CTA is an anchor again (`buttonVariants` + `rounded-md`).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqodrjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAj8QADGEb8iqN3u40JoFYPKB5dXS\n0zluFTUB/bp7M32dPpabWWQn/oqKm+2aOvmqCJHckuWr68hFxyJCp1rBhXK5j/4v\nUid79p2jALp+sQhR2nJu6zQAv/8s52uoZu8RueGHksdoWOeVK0G76fp5PFpbB6Wx\nSiz9NxBngzP26Gdmve0M3ilDGTCZPCfG4sok+BtPE8jX5cq5yChT52GM1tQGY6MG\n2bPSuVBnomDjiC0xv6haHWw2oueTCEFvESUTsFad3Ws46HnvICFPOtIncn9/Y6Tc\nt6n/ZH2VeCBq9kwpcoNDgTyZt6w1eOIU0EyjtsF9DcBwQw2iEpS7BkslWVoqwBQS\nyLpkb4NTAjAzSZXivSUfmFHeHT+ShRZ7uyDH0gFT6cLceV0gsrGwDWdZm7iIm/EW\nebi+q72Kb6YwVChxMCr3tHVSBJ92GZs3v52DEthA3bMmoQZrrNogw0QEs3vepy+G\nn3XXwQRAoU3g0IDbf70HKszeNLZFC75RXNNpOLhKHIBX7NCRetQcGFeA0UHNtLb+\nBjnP7/gafo9oAcAwiX2BAv55gBk8GWdkgr8cU4P4b4bNaXqw4u4ELjWCmI28IpHb\nTfiibHXwJlG3w08hG5D3s1YAUr///qw3dTI8ia7xNhUoLlOKug4peLdsqD5oKQbC\nio5QtiMquR7T7h0/MkV1\n=jQ4A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T22:17:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKDg1MWRjZTJhOTFlZTJlZDg5YmZjNTYzNWJjNDY5YzZhZDgzMTUzOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/d206252d31fce82011c8e7758cd8fc2ccb4fe5c9","sha":"d206252d31fce82011c8e7758cd8fc2ccb4fe5c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/d206252d31fce82011c8e7758cd8fc2ccb4fe5c9"}],"sha":"851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/851dce2a91ee2ed89bfc5635bc469c6ad831538b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/d206252d31fce82011c8e7758cd8fc2ccb4fe5c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:16:39Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:16:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 10/14] frontend: the Kafka Connect dynamic-ui engine on Registry components (#2637)\n\n* frontend: the Kafka Connect dynamic-ui engine on Registry components\n\nEight files. This is the schema-driven form renderer: a connector''s config\nschema arrives from the backend and `PropertyComponent` picks an input per\n`definition.type`. The schema contract does not change and neither does the\nvalue written back — `updatePropertyValue` still writes `property.value` and\ncalls `notifyChange()`.\n\nOld -> new, by file:\n\n- forms/error-wrapper — Chakra `FormField` -> Field + FieldLabel +\n  FieldDescription + FieldError. This is the shell *every* property renders\n  through, so it is the widest hunk by reach. Its `onClick` stays on the field:\n  a property can carry several validation errors and clicking is what advances\n  `currentErrorIndex` to show the next one.\n- property-component — `NumberInput` -> `Input type=\"number\"`. Chakra''s emitted\n  a number; a native number input emits a string, so this coerces with\n  `valueAsNumber` or the config would carry `\"3\"` where the connector expects\n  `3`. `RadioGroup options={…}` -> composed RadioGroupItem + Label (Base UI has\n  no options prop), `Switch isChecked/onChange` -> `checked/onCheckedChange`.\n- forms/secret-input — the Registry Input already owns the reveal toggle for\n  `type=\"password\"` and disables it while read-only, which is exactly the state\n  an existing secret sits in before Edit, so the hand-rolled InputGroup +\n  InputRightElement + `useBoolean` all go. `key` on the Input is what re-masks\n  on Undo: the toggle''s state lives inside the Input, so leaving editing has to\n  remount it or Undo would leave the restored secret in plain text.\n- forms/topic-input — `Select isMulti` -> SimpleMultiSelect (string-valued, and\n  the property is a comma-joined string either way), FormControl/FormHelperText/\n  FormErrorMessage -> Field/FieldDescription/FieldError, labelled Checkbox.\n- list — the rename hint Tooltip was `isOpen={hasFocus}`, i.e. controlled by\n  focus rather than hover; it stays controlled via `open`.\n- property-group — Chakra''s `Accordion items={…}` -> composed\n  AccordionItem/Trigger/Content. **The sub-group heading rendered its name\n  twice**; that is fixed here rather than carried across.\n- components, connector-step — layout props and `Skeleton noOfLines` ->\n  `SkeletonText lines`.\n\nconnector.spec.ts exercises this end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: drop two dead biome suppressions from the dynamic-ui migration\n\n`ultracite check` reports both as `suppressions/unused`: `onClick` on a\n*component* (Field, FieldError) does not trip the bare-element a11y rules the\nignores named, so they suppressed nothing and only implied a hazard that is not\nthere. `bun run lint` is `ultracite fix` and exits 0 on these, which is why they\nsurvived the first pass — `lint:check` is the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the dynamic-ui engine migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch. The worst two were about the config\nthis form actually submits:\n\n- **Numeric properties changed wire type, and could submit `null`.** The comment\n  had it exactly backwards: Chakra''s `NumberInput.onChange` is\n  `(valueAsString, valueAsNumber)` and the old code took the *first* argument —\n  a string. `getConfigObject` sends `p.value` as-is and compares it `===` against\n  `default_value` to suppress untouched defaults, and `sanitizeDefaultValue`\n  numbers only the INT/LONG/SHORT defaults — so storing a number changed which\n  properties get sent, inconsistently across the numeric types. Clearing a field\n  also stored `NaN`, which `JSON.stringify` turns into `null` in both the JSON\n  tab and the validate/create request. Back to the string.\n- **Every property control was unlabeled.** Chakra''s `FormControl` generated an\n  id and wired `FormLabel htmlFor` to it; the Registry `Field` does not. A\n  derived `property-<name>` id now goes to both the control and the label, so\n  clicking a label focuses its control and a screen reader gets a name instead\n  of a bare \"textbox\" — on every field of the create/edit connector form.\n\nThe rest:\n\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP properties render inline with their label again\n  (Chakra''s FormField special-cased a Switch child), and the control is wrapped\n  so `Field`''s vertical `[&>*]:w-full` cannot stretch a Switch pill to the full\n  row.\n- Property documentation goes back above the control, where FormField had it.\n- **The Registry `Input` discards a caller''s `style`** — it applies its own\n  after the prop spread — so both list inputs had silently lost their flex\n  sizing. Moved to `containerClassName`, which is also what the\n  ui-development rule requires.\n- The numeric steppers are back (`showStepControls`; the Registry needs asking\n  where Chakra shipped them by default), with `step=\"any\"` for DOUBLE/FLOAT,\n  which the Registry otherwise pins to 1 — the browser then marks any\n  non-integer value invalid.\n- **`.ghostInput`''s transparent border needs `!important`** to beat the Registry\n  Input''s `!border-input`; without it the reorderable transform-name inputs\n  rendered permanently bordered on a transparent ground.\n- A selected topic missing from `api.topics` rendered a chip whose × did\n  nothing; the options are the union of the topic list and the current\n  selection, so a deleted topic stays removable.\n- `topics-use-regex` was a fixed id on a component rendered once per property\n  group — `useId()` now.\n- The Edit-secret tooltip gets a `TooltipProvider`; without one it inherited\n  Base UI''s 600ms delay instead of the app''s 150ms.\n- `inputWrapper${cond ? ''hasError'' : ''''}` was missing a space, so\n  `.inputWrapper.hasError` never matched and the new-entry validation message\n  rendered at opacity 0. Pre-existing, one character, inside a function this\n  branch edits.\n- Margins off Registry components, and `mx-4` on a Label dropped — it was a\n  Chakra-only hack to widen a click target inside its own radio label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the per-option `_field` test ids on the connector radio groups\n\nChakra''s RadioGroup rendered a RadioCard per option with\ndata-testid=\"${value}_field\"; the composed RadioGroupItem replacement\ndropped it and broke the kafka-connect e2e JSON-editor test, which\nclicks `json_field`. The dynamic property radio group gets the same\ntreatment for parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): preserve connector input values and labels\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — final review\n\n- Radio-group properties are named: a radiogroup div is not labelable, so the label carries an id and the group points at it with aria-labelledby.\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP fields are vertical again; Chakra''s FormField never inlined them (its Switch check never matched), so the horizontal Field row was a layout change, not parity.\n- The list ghost input''s transparent border is a Tailwind class on the element: an unlayered !important in index.scss lost to the Registry''s layered !border-input, so the field rendered bordered. The new-entry input fits its 29px row.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; the numeric-input comment no longer claims an empty field would render NaN.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — fourth review round\n\n- Heading/description gaps use `mt-*` on the following element: the `mb-*` they replaced is inert until PR 8 moves the margin reset into `@layer base`.\n- Required properties carry `required`/`aria-required` again (Chakra''s FormControl stamped them).\n- The transforms list''s new-entry input takes the property id so its label resolves.\n- The password test reveals the value before Undo, so it fails without the remount `key`.\n- `.stringList` rows and buttons use theme tokens instead of literal greys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b8f6c68390149dcce346282eb8bc4a1d6f93f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/4b8f6c68390149dcce346282eb8bc4a1d6f93f42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/d206252d31fce82011c8e7758cd8fc2ccb4fe5c9","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b8f6c68390149dcce346282eb8bc4a1d6f93f42\nparent f4069cbb4bec6c6b703fe33e038e314bc721f241\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788992199 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788992199 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 10/14] frontend: the Kafka Connect dynamic-ui engine on Registry components (#2637)\n\n* frontend: the Kafka Connect dynamic-ui engine on Registry components\n\nEight files. This is the schema-driven form renderer: a connector''s config\nschema arrives from the backend and `PropertyComponent` picks an input per\n`definition.type`. The schema contract does not change and neither does the\nvalue written back — `updatePropertyValue` still writes `property.value` and\ncalls `notifyChange()`.\n\nOld -> new, by file:\n\n- forms/error-wrapper — Chakra `FormField` -> Field + FieldLabel +\n  FieldDescription + FieldError. This is the shell *every* property renders\n  through, so it is the widest hunk by reach. Its `onClick` stays on the field:\n  a property can carry several validation errors and clicking is what advances\n  `currentErrorIndex` to show the next one.\n- property-component — `NumberInput` -> `Input type=\"number\"`. Chakra''s emitted\n  a number; a native number input emits a string, so this coerces with\n  `valueAsNumber` or the config would carry `\"3\"` where the connector expects\n  `3`. `RadioGroup options={…}` -> composed RadioGroupItem + Label (Base UI has\n  no options prop), `Switch isChecked/onChange` -> `checked/onCheckedChange`.\n- forms/secret-input — the Registry Input already owns the reveal toggle for\n  `type=\"password\"` and disables it while read-only, which is exactly the state\n  an existing secret sits in before Edit, so the hand-rolled InputGroup +\n  InputRightElement + `useBoolean` all go. `key` on the Input is what re-masks\n  on Undo: the toggle''s state lives inside the Input, so leaving editing has to\n  remount it or Undo would leave the restored secret in plain text.\n- forms/topic-input — `Select isMulti` -> SimpleMultiSelect (string-valued, and\n  the property is a comma-joined string either way), FormControl/FormHelperText/\n  FormErrorMessage -> Field/FieldDescription/FieldError, labelled Checkbox.\n- list — the rename hint Tooltip was `isOpen={hasFocus}`, i.e. controlled by\n  focus rather than hover; it stays controlled via `open`.\n- property-group — Chakra''s `Accordion items={…}` -> composed\n  AccordionItem/Trigger/Content. **The sub-group heading rendered its name\n  twice**; that is fixed here rather than carried across.\n- components, connector-step — layout props and `Skeleton noOfLines` ->\n  `SkeletonText lines`.\n\nconnector.spec.ts exercises this end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: drop two dead biome suppressions from the dynamic-ui migration\n\n`ultracite check` reports both as `suppressions/unused`: `onClick` on a\n*component* (Field, FieldError) does not trip the bare-element a11y rules the\nignores named, so they suppressed nothing and only implied a hazard that is not\nthere. `bun run lint` is `ultracite fix` and exits 0 on these, which is why they\nsurvived the first pass — `lint:check` is the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the dynamic-ui engine migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch. The worst two were about the config\nthis form actually submits:\n\n- **Numeric properties changed wire type, and could submit `null`.** The comment\n  had it exactly backwards: Chakra''s `NumberInput.onChange` is\n  `(valueAsString, valueAsNumber)` and the old code took the *first* argument —\n  a string. `getConfigObject` sends `p.value` as-is and compares it `===` against\n  `default_value` to suppress untouched defaults, and `sanitizeDefaultValue`\n  numbers only the INT/LONG/SHORT defaults — so storing a number changed which\n  properties get sent, inconsistently across the numeric types. Clearing a field\n  also stored `NaN`, which `JSON.stringify` turns into `null` in both the JSON\n  tab and the validate/create request. Back to the string.\n- **Every property control was unlabeled.** Chakra''s `FormControl` generated an\n  id and wired `FormLabel htmlFor` to it; the Registry `Field` does not. A\n  derived `property-<name>` id now goes to both the control and the label, so\n  clicking a label focuses its control and a screen reader gets a name instead\n  of a bare \"textbox\" — on every field of the create/edit connector form.\n\nThe rest:\n\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP properties render inline with their label again\n  (Chakra''s FormField special-cased a Switch child), and the control is wrapped\n  so `Field`''s vertical `[&>*]:w-full` cannot stretch a Switch pill to the full\n  row.\n- Property documentation goes back above the control, where FormField had it.\n- **The Registry `Input` discards a caller''s `style`** — it applies its own\n  after the prop spread — so both list inputs had silently lost their flex\n  sizing. Moved to `containerClassName`, which is also what the\n  ui-development rule requires.\n- The numeric steppers are back (`showStepControls`; the Registry needs asking\n  where Chakra shipped them by default), with `step=\"any\"` for DOUBLE/FLOAT,\n  which the Registry otherwise pins to 1 — the browser then marks any\n  non-integer value invalid.\n- **`.ghostInput`''s transparent border needs `!important`** to beat the Registry\n  Input''s `!border-input`; without it the reorderable transform-name inputs\n  rendered permanently bordered on a transparent ground.\n- A selected topic missing from `api.topics` rendered a chip whose × did\n  nothing; the options are the union of the topic list and the current\n  selection, so a deleted topic stays removable.\n- `topics-use-regex` was a fixed id on a component rendered once per property\n  group — `useId()` now.\n- The Edit-secret tooltip gets a `TooltipProvider`; without one it inherited\n  Base UI''s 600ms delay instead of the app''s 150ms.\n- `inputWrapper${cond ? ''hasError'' : ''''}` was missing a space, so\n  `.inputWrapper.hasError` never matched and the new-entry validation message\n  rendered at opacity 0. Pre-existing, one character, inside a function this\n  branch edits.\n- Margins off Registry components, and `mx-4` on a Label dropped — it was a\n  Chakra-only hack to widen a click target inside its own radio label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the per-option `_field` test ids on the connector radio groups\n\nChakra''s RadioGroup rendered a RadioCard per option with\ndata-testid=\"${value}_field\"; the composed RadioGroupItem replacement\ndropped it and broke the kafka-connect e2e JSON-editor test, which\nclicks `json_field`. The dynamic property radio group gets the same\ntreatment for parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): preserve connector input values and labels\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — final review\n\n- Radio-group properties are named: a radiogroup div is not labelable, so the label carries an id and the group points at it with aria-labelledby.\n- BOOLEAN and RADIO_GROUP fields are vertical again; Chakra''s FormField never inlined them (its Switch check never matched), so the horizontal Field row was a layout change, not parity.\n- The list ghost input''s transparent border is a Tailwind class on the element: an unlayered !important in index.scss lost to the Registry''s layered !border-input, so the field rendered bordered. The new-entry input fits its 29px row.\n- Comments trimmed to the constraints; the numeric-input comment no longer claims an empty field would render NaN.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: Kafka Connect dynamic-ui — fourth review round\n\n- Heading/description gaps use `mt-*` on the following element: the `mb-*` they replaced is inert until PR 8 moves the margin reset into `@layer base`.\n- Required properties carry `required`/`aria-required` again (Chakra''s FormControl stamped them).\n- The transforms list''s new-entry input takes the property id so its label resolves.\n- The password test reveals the value before Undo, so it fails without the remount `key`.\n- `.stringList` rows and buttons use theme tokens instead of literal greys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqodrHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2bkQAEfePHdOzAWDdeLiA+7P9PtE\nGB0y5DFb7huogECpvDwN/LxrkgzKdY0ZFRk6dkoeAC7mEs7K4o7lR4lKejsqN4lT\nphnvou3cJ8ORdDaTAXr75EMCvHme2+Sr42fyYPynxKCcS590cbfa6crin/R14YMo\nZFXcCqcW/FfZrX40WMERbCPWR4uRivOsRDNV0ESspyG79jjmBfPEms8VUDliBTph\n8Gvb8DfZeOHV4WNCHmGIAIqa2l8H9PQdvLZ2cmamZf3z/UC6Lr/xV7YXfqglDTU9\nVk2rJWZIceo4jAHCXxIpE/aLQA8xcxf0oU6KDB3pH9rKxQU8LCsi4YJGemw3d7es\nDys/vERTTFW2ti4wkGalPBNu6xkzJeu9E2gEmZe0yPYmjTgW8wBvY/uVMO4GxoDK\njnJj94GTcxiStZNW3FsMvFI9NXNUF41fE7f+5EkAho0oel0E+vaIBnAVlQWf/ned\neEFjKRs7kGFQ/kNQbSBiayqO