 the RP trial license","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobtOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7OkQACKqBfWJsJ9YxQw+xylLtqtj\nHtKL+zNC7JdBrk3YtCnNyLh6BGlcjnnmdtyCtblsOJgMPml7iMFWagFaVs9qPX+x\nwGF3zfeEuQnog1mGk8E/iByxp1UqLMWJ6Fb1RB8yKGCMA90Hf5hO3fS//rD0k2fC\njSZDKpcPZwIJgrug/S3+zULcblaJ3ous48sg0aG6BYi4msGlA3iOybsA+l4e1iw2\nCAb0EEVH6jZ+9X6CjWwAhNGR54nQEVHORl4QcGDkD1wvhKXYsJMxBgjQmcJbprfa\nblEMQy2XChy8B3AI+Z8Rxk9IctRH+rhwNFEKrxiZWNFyK5/JGYXhzJs0+e56mSaI\nWc7ruAoN/8EkW7e5Bf88BzEFu9WcxWhRM/RJCNQ8zZxI3aKRtxUCEN9KJ4LcJO2q\nxBsRwycr2yaD31/Fe3x4KN2omG022NqlEw3szybevpnY/Wb3YSHmdUWbrqeEPVt5\ndxWqYl7sO6SgWiiiUG5tZzoMWg+zOGsXHVO076iXP9VFxuivIt9u9kC8vZYiVP4X\n4Nro7Rx8hHV8OCZLuOuczL1WvtDzlU9k28XXr5mooMVS1ZMh5Oc0AVOqnAdlKM4g\nccj0az3xgUZojNh0NTvL3gpc9x3mfOvg+o8KcEyOJdDeCwg9ypmcHz6GCDYNTDnQ\nOUfSyuSXxwXHaWYPslst\n=VHvZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T20:02:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/f4069cbb4bec6c6b703fe33e038e314bc721f241","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGY0MDY5Y2JiNGJlYzZjNmI3MDNmZTMzZTAzOGUzMTRiYzcyMWYyNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6","sha":"67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69","sha":"efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69"}],"sha":"f4069cbb4bec6c6b703fe33e038e314bc721f241","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/f4069cbb4bec6c6b703fe33e038e314bc721f241"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:32:12Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:32:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 8/14] frontend: mount the Registry ThemeProvider and take the chrome off Chakra (#2636)\n\n* frontend: mount the Registry ThemeProvider and take the chrome off Chakra\n\nThe load-bearing half of this PR is the theme provider. `data-theme` on <html>\nis what theme.css keys its dark palette on and what use-theme-appearance\nwatches to tell Monaco, CodeMirror, react-flow and sonner which ground they\npaint on — and Chakra''s ColorModeSwitch was the only thing setting it. So:\n\n- `components/layout/theme-mode-switch.tsx` replaces ColorModeSwitch on the\n  Registry ThemeProvider''s `useTheme()`, keeping the `ColorModeSwitch` test id\n  and the \"Switch to <next> mode\" label. It reads `resolvedTheme`, not `theme`,\n  because the stored preference can be `system` and the label has to name what\n  the click will produce.\n- The provider is mounted in `app.tsx` only, not in embedded-app or\n  federated-providers as planned. In those modes the Cloud UI host owns\n  `data-theme` on <html>; a second writer inside Console would fight it. It\n  sits outside ChakraProvider so its mount effect lands last while both are up.\n- The `theme={toasterTheme}` plumbing on both sonner mounts stays, contrary to\n  the plan. sonner.tsx reads `useTheme().theme`, which can be `system` — that\n  resolves off prefers-color-scheme and so disagrees with an explicit toggle\n  when the OS says otherwise. `useThemeAppearance()` reads the ground actually\n  painted, which is the answer sonner needs.\n\nThen the misc leftovers, each behind its existing export: no-clipboard-popover\n(hover Popover -> Tooltip), kowl-time-picker, removable-filter, search-bar\n(SearchField -> Input with the search-field-* test ids), kowl-json-view,\nexpandable-text, common (update Modal -> Dialog) and wizard.\n\n`hooks/use-developer-view` loses Chakra''s `useKey` + `useLocalStorage` for a\nkeydown listener and localStorage directly — these non-visual hooks keep the\ndependency alive on their own. The replacement ignores `?` typed into an input\nor held with a modifier, which Chakra''s useKey did not, and its test now\nasserts the toggle flips and persists rather than only that it does not crash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the chrome and app-shell migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The theme provider would have flipped production Console to dark.** Chakra\n  pinned `initialColorMode: ''light''` with `useSystemColorMode: false`; the\n  Registry ThemeProvider defaults to `system`, so every OS-dark standalone user\n  would have got the Registry''s dark palette against a still-light Chakra half —\n  and the only toggle is `IsDev`-gated, so no way back. `defaultTheme=\"light\"`\n  now, with the reasoning and the remaining Chakra colour-mode overlap written\n  down at the mount point. Dark mode stays an opt-in project.\n- **The clipboard-unavailable tooltip could never open.** `render={children}`\n  handed the trigger props to a component that forwards no rest props, and the\n  child in that branch is a *disabled* button — which dispatches no pointer\n  events. It wraps in a span, the same shape the header''s disabled buttons use.\n  This is the only explanation users get for a copy button that silently fails\n  over plain HTTP.\n- **The SearchBar field collapsed from 350px to ~177px.**\n  `containerClassName=\"max-w-[350px]\"` is a cap with no width, and the container\n  is a flex item, so it sized to the input''s intrinsic width. `w-full` added.\n- The clear button stays mounted (`InputEnd` never resets the padding it\n  measured, and unmounting under the click drops focus to `<body>`).\n- `useDeveloperViewProd` read and JSON-parsed localStorage on every render of\n  the app root; it reads once at mount now, mirroring the dev hook.\n- `expandable-text`''s disclosure button gets `aria-expanded` — the point of\n  making it a real button — and drops `border-none bg-transparent`, which\n  Preflight already resets.\n- `removable-filter` drops the `!` on `border-border`: that escape hatch exists\n  for Chakra-classed nodes, and this is a plain div.\n- `wizard` uses `cn()` so a removed CSS-module class cannot stringify into the\n  class list and `px-8` merges against the button''s own size variant.\n- `common`''s dialog passes the setter directly, and `size=\"lg\"` (42rem) is the\n  nearest rung to Chakra''s `minW=\"xl\"` (36rem) rather than `xl` (56rem).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): restore search keyboard shortcuts\n\n* frontend: misc leftovers — error boundary on Tailwind classes, radius on the not-found anchor\n\n- error-boundary.tsx drops its inline style objects for Tailwind classes and design tokens (asked for in the PR 4 review, after that PR had merged).\n- The legacy-AI anchor on the not-found page adds rounded-md; the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: chrome and app shell — second review round\n\n- index.scss: the element margin reset now lives in @layer base, so mb-* utilities on headings and paragraphs apply (it silently beat every one added during the migration).\n- app.tsx pins Chakra''s colour-mode manager to light so a stored chakra-ui-color-mode=dark cannot split the page; bootstrap stamps the theme before first paint via initTheme. Comments trimmed to the constraints.\n- misc/search-bar.tsx composes the new SearchInput (shared with the transforms and Connect pages): clear refocuses the field, the empty right edge is click-through, Escape only stops propagation when it clears; inline styles gone.\n- ? developer-view toggle ignores key repeat, IME composition, handled events and typing targets, and reads its stored flag as a boolean.\n- Misc: tooltip content spacing and dead placement prop on the clipboard notice; ExpandableText renders a span (it sits inside <p>) and a Registry link Button; UpdatePopup Cancel is a plain outline; dead Wizard scss classes and an inert icon size removed; JSON view sizing on utilities.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: chrome and app shell — final review\n\n- Shared SearchInput copy refreshed (advertises its shortcuts); two comments trimmed to their constraints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: drop column hiding and the selection count from single-select tables\n\nEvery Registry table built on useDataTable now passes enableHiding: false and\nenableRowSelection: false where the page has no column-visibility UI and no\nmulti-row selection. enableHiding removes the \"Hide\" item from the column\nheader menus; enableRowSelection removes the \"X of N row(s) selected.\" text\nfrom the pagination footer, which the registry gates on that option.\n\nLog explorer already blanked the selection text with a CSS hack; it now uses\nthe option instead. The secrets store keeps both (it has view options and row\ncheckboxes), and the pipeline list already set them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d0aa06000684e88a83e005119afb5f0b6fe1e23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/6d0aa06000684e88a83e005119afb5f0b6fe1e23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d0aa06000684e88a83e005119afb5f0b6fe1e23\nparent 2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788964332 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788964332 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 8/14] frontend: mount the Registry ThemeProvider and take the chrome off Chakra (#2636)\n\n* frontend: mount the Registry ThemeProvider and take the chrome off Chakra\n\nThe load-bearing half of this PR is the theme provider. `data-theme` on <html>\nis what theme.css keys its dark palette on and what use-theme-appearance\nwatches to tell Monaco, CodeMirror, react-flow and sonner which ground they\npaint on — and Chakra''s ColorModeSwitch was the only thing setting it. So:\n\n- `components/layout/theme-mode-switch.tsx` replaces ColorModeSwitch on the\n  Registry ThemeProvider''s `useTheme()`, keeping the `ColorModeSwitch` test id\n  and the \"Switch to <next> mode\" label. It reads `resolvedTheme`, not `theme`,\n  because the stored preference can be `system` and the label has to name what\n  the click will produce.\n- The provider is mounted in `app.tsx` only, not in embedded-app or\n  federated-providers as planned. In those modes the Cloud UI host owns\n  `data-theme` on <html>; a second writer inside Console would fight it. It\n  sits outside ChakraProvider so its mount effect lands last while both are up.\n- The `theme={toasterTheme}` plumbing on both sonner mounts stays, contrary to\n  the plan. sonner.tsx reads `useTheme().theme`, which can be `system` — that\n  resolves off prefers-color-scheme and so disagrees with an explicit toggle\n  when the OS says otherwise. `useThemeAppearance()` reads the ground actually\n  painted, which is the answer sonner needs.\n\nThen the misc leftovers, each behind its existing export: no-clipboard-popover\n(hover Popover -> Tooltip), kowl-time-picker, removable-filter, search-bar\n(SearchField -> Input with the search-field-* test ids), kowl-json-view,\nexpandable-text, common (update Modal -> Dialog) and wizard.\n\n`hooks/use-developer-view` loses Chakra''s `useKey` + `useLocalStorage` for a\nkeydown listener and localStorage directly — these non-visual hooks keep the\ndependency alive on their own. The replacement ignores `?` typed into an input\nor held with a modifier, which Chakra''s useKey did not, and its test now\nasserts the toggle flips and persists rather than only that it does not crash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the chrome and app-shell migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The theme provider would have flipped production Console to dark.** Chakra\n  pinned `initialColorMode: ''light''` with `useSystemColorMode: false`; the\n  Registry ThemeProvider defaults to `system`, so every OS-dark standalone user\n  would have got the Registry''s dark palette against a still-light Chakra half —\n  and the only toggle is `IsDev`-gated, so no way back. `defaultTheme=\"light\"`\n  now, with the reasoning and the remaining Chakra colour-mode overlap written\n  down at the mount point. Dark mode stays an opt-in project.\n- **The clipboard-unavailable tooltip could never open.** `render={children}`\n  handed the trigger props to a component that forwards no rest props, and the\n  child in that branch is a *disabled* button — which dispatches no pointer\n  events. It wraps in a span, the same shape the header''s disabled buttons use.\n  This is the only explanation users get for a copy button that silently fails\n  over plain HTTP.\n- **The SearchBar field collapsed from 350px to ~177px.**\n  `containerClassName=\"max-w-[350px]\"` is a cap with no width, and the container\n  is a flex item, so it sized to the input''s intrinsic width. `w-full` added.\n- The clear button stays mounted (`InputEnd` never resets the padding it\n  measured, and unmounting under the click drops focus to `<body>`).\n- `useDeveloperViewProd` read and JSON-parsed localStorage on every render of\n  the app root; it reads once at mount now, mirroring the dev hook.\n- `expandable-text`''s disclosure button gets `aria-expanded` — the point of\n  making it a real button — and drops `border-none bg-transparent`, which\n  Preflight already resets.\n- `removable-filter` drops the `!` on `border-border`: that escape hatch exists\n  for Chakra-classed nodes, and this is a plain div.\n- `wizard` uses `cn()` so a removed CSS-module class cannot stringify into the\n  class list and `px-8` merges against the button''s own size variant.\n- `common`''s dialog passes the setter directly, and `size=\"lg\"` (42rem) is the\n  nearest rung to Chakra''s `minW=\"xl\"` (36rem) rather than `xl` (56rem).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): restore search keyboard shortcuts\n\n* frontend: misc leftovers — error boundary on Tailwind classes, radius on the not-found anchor\n\n- error-boundary.tsx drops its inline style objects for Tailwind classes and design tokens (asked for in the PR 4 review, after that PR had merged).\n- The legacy-AI anchor on the not-found page adds rounded-md; the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: chrome and app shell — second review round\n\n- index.scss: the element margin reset now lives in @layer base, so mb-* utilities on headings and paragraphs apply (it silently beat every one added during the migration).\n- app.tsx pins Chakra''s colour-mode manager to light so a stored chakra-ui-color-mode=dark cannot split the page; bootstrap stamps the theme before first paint via initTheme. Comments trimmed to the constraints.\n- misc/search-bar.tsx composes the new SearchInput (shared with the transforms and Connect pages): clear refocuses the field, the empty right edge is click-through, Escape only stops propagation when it clears; inline styles gone.\n- ? developer-view toggle ignores key repeat, IME composition, handled events and typing targets, and reads its stored flag as a boolean.\n- Misc: tooltip content spacing and dead placement prop on the clipboard notice; ExpandableText renders a span (it sits inside <p>) and a Registry link Button; UpdatePopup Cancel is a plain outline; dead Wizard scss classes and an inert icon size removed; JSON view sizing on utilities.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: chrome and app shell — final review\n\n- Shared SearchInput copy refreshed (advertises its shortcuts); two comments trimmed to their constraints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: drop column hiding and the selection count from single-select tables\n\nEvery Registry table built on useDataTable now passes enableHiding: false and\nenableRowSelection: false where the page has no column-visibility UI and no\nmulti-row selection. enableHiding removes the \"Hide\" item from the column\nheader menus; enableRowSelection removes the \"X of N row(s) selected.\" text\nfrom the pagination footer, which the registry gates on that option.\n\nLog explorer already blanked the selection text with a CSS hack; it now uses\nthe option instead. The secrets store keeps both (it has view options and row\ncheckboxes), and the pipeline list already set them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoW3sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHVYQAI2clCK/kH07OAtwXhe4F23P\nEz88j4k6mBMHsLiM3ceisgPpTP4bneFCwKnmdcy4SuwqGJVhQKweWuwAsdRI3vWw\nEo1BciuTmZQPYlqHQFcrnTSSVPEDoBbzPJscpAgDIR+rJStiAf4cos9PSwak54g9\nur3w2k3T89v+12EMDPPo7ly8YDPJkN3ak5aCfY8DjL7vHs0MaNMSK7Q3sAF2bKMO\nHxqJPkvjDzoG4qkz9Gxp23atBjr2fT11LFBR7ohdx681N7an6vE+v7GbVkAUgi99\nAlsDczcghYvZhQW5tAgIOf6QdXKGtCEXslk6KX9fE2GRIN8LHR6XUCNmNzkwPJxb\nLd5iqt6+otij9fvJmWW0ptxJ+QWKlY25cWzUjZT/LmNBhe8IS14DOH/muRCt54Fj\nmWXQ3pnfoYYZ/X+G6v7d18TF/O48+h7Fm8+nMxp/jMMqjCeJgrYOm2qCOCWABlwh\nUKpXGz1sMuCF6t4EF3BC4AFu89eH4KRMoWtQmOEJqsUxtW0/S2wMPpdLOWzqbOec\ndE92rl0s+clJr6Q1Y98LfH+aMmoyoMc/Jxl+0jZlXfd2RpnoSkoYpa8o7HHX0eZ0\ni6xVTHid+CNcNvm70jbSkOZgn0r6vnFGdLHfWh1AReOeCIttsaqi8PcQK9QdgNgk\nQcb8jn8wMd2Diwbe4+8/\n=9Gdn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T14:32:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKDY3ZGI1NDU0NzAyMmJlODk3MjU3M2IyNDRlOTE1NWRlZjY5ZjdmZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","sha":"2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2"}],"sha":"67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/67db54547022be8972573b244e9155def69f7fd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1083817?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jvorcak","id":1083817,"login":"jvorcak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODM4MTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/e2ce0db84b4efda844f500a2743c9a016dd832be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:39:25Z","email":"jan.vorcak@redpanda.com","name":"Ján Vorčák"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:39:25Z","email":"jan.vorcak@redpanda.com","name":"Ján Vorčák"},"message":"UX-1469: fix breadcrumb navigation while topic messages are loading\n\nClicking the current topic''s own breadcrumb re-navigated to its bare\npath, dropping query params (filters, pagination, active tab); it now\nrenders as non-navigable text instead. Clicking the \"Topics\" breadcrumb\nwhile a message search is in flight could race a queued nuqs URL\nupdate and land on /topics/undefined; the topic details route now\nredirects that back to /topics. Also hardens error-message handling\nin the message search and the default route error boundary so a\nnon-Error rejection never renders the literal text \"undefined\".","tree":{"sha":"9c3bcba50961667b4dd835d6251299f40fa21df7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/9c3bcba50961667b4dd835d6251299f40fa21df7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/e2ce0db84b4efda844f500a2743c9a016dd832be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1083817?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jvorcak","id":1083817,"login":"jvorcak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODM4MTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/e2ce0db84b4efda844f500a2743c9a016dd832be","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGUyY2UwZGI4NGI0ZWZkYTg0NGY1MDBhMjc0M2M5YTAxNmRkODMyYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","sha":"2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2"}],"sha":"e2ce0db84b4efda844f500a2743c9a016dd832be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/e2ce0db84b4efda844f500a2743c9a016dd832be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59714880?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/r-vasquez","id":59714880,"login":"r-vasquez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzE0ODgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:21:30Z","email":"rvasque3@gmail.com","name":"Rogger Vasquez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:21:30Z","email":"rvasque3@gmail.com","name":"Rogger Vasquez"},"message":"fe/e2e: run entrp variant on the RP trial license\n\nThe enterprise variant mounted a Console license\nfile into the backend container, sourced in CI\nfrom a GitHub secret. Once that license expired,\nthe backend exited at startup (expired license\nwith enterprise features enabled) before the\nharness could capture its logs, and every run\nfailed with \"container ... is not running\".\n\nThe e2e brokers never had a license installed.\nThey run on the built-in 30-day trial that every\nfresh Redpanda cluster starts with (24.3+), and\nConsole Enterprise falls back to the cluster''s\nlicense when its own config has none. Drop\n`licenseFilepath` from both enterprise configs so\nConsole picks up that trial, and remove the\nlicense mount and the \"skip variant when no\nlicense\" plumbing that existed only for it.\n\nREDPANDA_LICENSE_PATH stays as an explicit\noverride for license-specific work, e.g. against\na long-lived local cluster whose trial expired.\nIts contents reach the container as\nREDPANDA_LICENSE, which the backend reads at\nstartup.","tree":{"sha":"d74b34bec8113fc228b467367e76529d021ac0dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/d74b34bec8113fc228b467367e76529d021ac0dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59714880?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/r-vasquez","id":59714880,"login":"r-vasquez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzE0ODgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/r-vasquez","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGVmZTljZGM1MDQwZjIyOGVhMjQ0N2JmZjMxYzFhNTA0Nzc3ZTRlNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","sha":"a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77"}],"sha":"efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/efe9cdc5040f228ea2447bff31c1a504777e4e69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:02:14Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:02:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 7/14] frontend: overview, broker and login surfaces on Registry components, plus two smoke specs (#2635)\n\n* frontend: smoke specs for overview and login\n\nOverview is the largest route with no Playwright coverage and the first screen\nanyone sees. The specs assert the panels are present and populated, not their\nvalues, which depend on whichever cluster the suite runs against.\n\nFor login, the OSS variant has no auth configured, so /login redirects to\n/overview — that redirect is the contract worth guarding. The credential form\nis already exercised by the enterprise variant''s auth.setup.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login surfaces on Registry components\n\nEight files. Mostly Chakra layout props to Tailwind classes; the parts that\ncarry judgement:\n\n- Chakra''s DataTable injected an expander column whenever `subComponent` was\n  set. The Registry one does not, so config-list''s synonym sub-rows had no way\n  to open — it now carries the same expander column the new topic messages page\n  uses. Its nested table also needs `pagination={false} sorting={false}`\n  explicitly: those default to false in Chakra and true in the Registry.\n- Login''s error modal was a Chakra Modal, so auth.setup.ts waited on\n  `.chakra-modal__overlay` — a class that no longer exists. It now waits on\n  `[data-slot=\"dialog-overlay\"]`. The wait was already inside a `.catch`, so\n  this was a silent 5s stall rather than a failure, but auth.setup.ts gates\n  every enterprise spec and deserves to be right.\n- \"Log in with OIDC\" navigates to a backend endpoint, so it is an anchor with\n  `buttonVariants()`, not a Button. Same for the debug-bundle links in\n  cluster-health-overview, which debug-bundle-page.ts reads via\n  `getByRole(''link'')`.\n- Chakra''s TextDivider is inlined as a three-column grid — the only place it\n  was used.\n- The waving-panda SVG only existed as a data URI inside the Chakra bundle, so\n  it is vendored to assets/redpanda/WavingPanda.svg.\n- Two literal colours become tokens: the cluster-details hairline was `#ddd`\n  (invisible in the dark theme) and the controller crown was `#0008`. The login\n  gradient and the Redpanda logo stay literal — both are fixed art.\n- `Skeleton noOfLines={13}` maps onto `SkeletonText lines={13}`; the\n  Statistic, Section and OptionGroup wrappers from PR 3 are untouched.\n\nEvery `data-testid` is preserved, including `overview-license-name` and the\nfour the login flow depends on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the overview, broker and login migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **Both new specs would have failed every run.** \"Topics\", \"Security\" and\n  \"Schema Registry\" are also sidebar nav items, so\n  `getByText(..., { exact: true })` resolved to two elements and tripped\n  Playwright strict mode. The locators are scoped now — stat labels by\n  `[data-slot=\"stat-label\"]`, the details panel by an id on its Section — and\n  the detail rows are asserted as headings rather than free text.\n- **The login-callback spec was a race, not a contract.** `login-complete`\n  navigates away as soon as its own fetch settles, so \"Completing login...\"\n  exists for a round-trip. Dropped rather than left to flake.\n- **`whitespace-break-spaces` was inert on config values.** `.value` in\n  ConfigList.module.scss is unlayered, so it beats any `@layer utilities` rule —\n  where Chakra''s emotion class (injected after the bundle) used to win. It was\n  silently downgrading `break-spaces` to `pre-line`, collapsing runs of spaces\n  in config values. Fixed at the module rule, which is where it has to live.\n  Same reason `flex` next to `styles.nameText` was dead code: `.name .nameText`\n  is unlayered `display: inline-block`.\n- **`.nameText` had literal `#d1d1d1`/`#f5f5f5`**, unreadable in the dark\n  theme; now `var(--color-border)` / `var(--color-surface-subtle)`.\n- **An unmapped `UnhealthyReason` took down the health panel.**\n  `MAP[x].toLowerCase() ?? x` dereferences before the guard, so a reason the\n  6-entry map does not cover threw in render. Pre-existing, but this diff\n  rewrites the enclosing JSX.\n- **The in-progress debug-bundle link could route nowhere.**\n  `isDebugBundleInProgress` and `debugBundleStatus` are derived separately, so an\n  empty job id gave `/debug-bundle/progress/`, which matches no route.\n- **The login button was not disabled in flight** — the inputs were, the button\n  was not, so a double click fired `loginSaslScram` twice and raced two\n  `historyPush(''/overview'')`.\n- `<h3>Cluster Details</h3>` was the one heading the migration missed;\n  `text-[10px] … tracking-[0.8px]` is the named `text-caption` rung; the\n  hand-rolled TextDivider is the Registry''s `FieldSeparator`; the broker table''s\n  `tableOptions` restated the DataTable''s own default and cost a fresh object\n  per render.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: login surfaces — registry text style for the login-complete splash, radius on the OIDC anchor\n\n- text-[1.5em] (flagged by the lookout audit) becomes text-heading-lg, the rung the login page heading already uses.\n- The OIDC anchor keeps buttonVariants and adds rounded-md; the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login — second review round\n\n- Overview: the four section headings carried a dead text class while Overview.scss painted them a hard-coded near-black; the scss now uses the foreground token. The Cluster Status stripe never rendered because its selector still targeted .ant-statistic; it targets the Registry Stat and uses semantic tokens. Statistic wrapper replaced by Stat here and on broker details. Broker table paginates like the legacy one (50, pager only past that); column size hints the Registry ignores are gone; a 0-byte broker shows ''0 B''; the footer''s non-existent font-sm class is text-body-sm.\n- Cluster health: link-styled anchors drop the button height; unknown health reasons read ''Unknown reason'' instead of an enum number. The store''s debugBundleStatus getter prefers the RUNNING broker status, so the in-progress link gets its job id.\n- Config list: the three remaining literal colours in ConfigList.module.scss are tokens.\n- Login: Button isLoading instead of a hand-rolled spinner; the logo takes the foreground colour; the OR separator''s label chip matches the page ground in dark; heading rung is text-heading-xl (the original 1.5em), also on login-complete.\n- auth.setup.ts waits on the dialog''s own button disappearing instead of a swallowed overlay selector.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login — final review\n\n- Broker table stays at ten a page with the pager only past that (it had defaultPageSize 10, not 50).\n- Cluster-details headings keep a legible rung (text-heading-sm / text-body-sm) instead of shrinking to caption sizes; the docs footer inherits its size.\n- Config list: column size hints the Registry never reads are gone, the chevrons no longer carry an inert size class, and the two stylesheets drop orphaned selectors and history comments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login — reviewer round\n\nCluster Status stat: the left stripe (clipped on self-hosted and with the\nnew-overview flag off) becomes a Registry StatusDot in the value; the\nstripe SCSS goes. OptionGroup renders its ToggleGroup as `outline`, so the\nFormatting/Sort segments on broker details sit in a track. The login\nerror Alert carries `auth-error`, asserted by a new enterprise spec for\nthe wrong-password path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: login — rejected-password path under JSDOM\n\nThe enterprise e2e spec needs a backend; this drives the same form with a\nstubbed authentication client: one request in flight with the button\ndisabled, then the inline error and a re-enabled form.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00fcaf6f6f8ab8e8b33e813dfa2e921f9ed18456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/00fcaf6f6f8ab8e8b33e813dfa2e921f9ed18456"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 00fcaf6f6f8ab8e8b33e813dfa2e921f9ed18456\nparent a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788908534 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788908534 -0600\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 7/14] frontend: overview, broker and login surfaces on Registry components, plus two smoke specs (#2635)\n\n* frontend: smoke specs for overview and login\n\nOverview is the largest route with no Playwright coverage and the first screen\nanyone sees. The specs assert the panels are present and populated, not their\nvalues, which depend on whichever cluster the suite runs against.\n\nFor login, the OSS variant has no auth configured, so /login redirects to\n/overview — that redirect is the contract worth guarding. The credential form\nis already exercised by the enterprise variant''s auth.setup.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login surfaces on Registry components\n\nEight files. Mostly Chakra layout props to Tailwind classes; the parts that\ncarry judgement:\n\n- Chakra''s DataTable injected an expander column whenever `subComponent` was\n  set. The Registry one does not, so config-list''s synonym sub-rows had no way\n  to open — it now carries the same expander column the new topic messages page\n  uses. Its nested table also needs `pagination={false} sorting={false}`\n  explicitly: those default to false in Chakra and true in the Registry.\n- Login''s error modal was a Chakra Modal, so auth.setup.ts waited on\n  `.chakra-modal__overlay` — a class that no longer exists. It now waits on\n  `[data-slot=\"dialog-overlay\"]`. The wait was already inside a `.catch`, so\n  this was a silent 5s stall rather than a failure, but auth.setup.ts gates\n  every enterprise spec and deserves to be right.\n- \"Log in with OIDC\" navigates to a backend endpoint, so it is an anchor with\n  `buttonVariants()`, not a Button. Same for the debug-bundle links in\n  cluster-health-overview, which debug-bundle-page.ts reads via\n  `getByRole(''link'')`.\n- Chakra''s TextDivider is inlined as a three-column grid — the only place it\n  was used.\n- The waving-panda SVG only existed as a data URI inside the Chakra bundle, so\n  it is vendored to assets/redpanda/WavingPanda.svg.\n- Two literal colours become tokens: the cluster-details hairline was `#ddd`\n  (invisible in the dark theme) and the controller crown was `#0008`. The login\n  gradient and the Redpanda logo stay literal — both are fixed art.\n- `Skeleton noOfLines={13}` maps onto `SkeletonText lines={13}`; the\n  Statistic, Section and OptionGroup wrappers from PR 3 are untouched.\n\nEvery `data-testid` is preserved, including `overview-license-name` and the\nfour the login flow depends on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the overview, broker and login migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **Both new specs would have failed every run.** \"Topics\", \"Security\" and\n  \"Schema Registry\" are also sidebar nav items, so\n  `getByText(..., { exact: true })` resolved to two elements and tripped\n  Playwright strict mode. The locators are scoped now — stat labels by\n  `[data-slot=\"stat-label\"]`, the details panel by an id on its Section — and\n  the detail rows are asserted as headings rather than free text.\n- **The login-callback spec was a race, not a contract.** `login-complete`\n  navigates away as soon as its own fetch settles, so \"Completing login...\"\n  exists for a round-trip. Dropped rather than left to flake.\n- **`whitespace-break-spaces` was inert on config values.** `.value` in\n  ConfigList.module.scss is unlayered, so it beats any `@layer utilities` rule —\n  where Chakra''s emotion class (injected after the bundle) used to win. It was\n  silently downgrading `break-spaces` to `pre-line`, collapsing runs of spaces\n  in config values. Fixed at the module rule, which is where it has to live.\n  Same reason `flex` next to `styles.nameText` was dead code: `.name .nameText`\n  is unlayered `display: inline-block`.\n- **`.nameText` had literal `#d1d1d1`/`#f5f5f5`**, unreadable in the dark\n  theme; now `var(--color-border)` / `var(--color-surface-subtle)`.\n- **An unmapped `UnhealthyReason` took down the health panel.**\n  `MAP[x].toLowerCase() ?? x` dereferences before the guard, so a reason the\n  6-entry map does not cover threw in render. Pre-existing, but this diff\n  rewrites the enclosing JSX.\n- **The in-progress debug-bundle link could route nowhere.**\n  `isDebugBundleInProgress` and `debugBundleStatus` are derived separately, so an\n  empty job id gave `/debug-bundle/progress/`, which matches no route.\n- **The login button was not disabled in flight** — the inputs were, the button\n  was not, so a double click fired `loginSaslScram` twice and raced two\n  `historyPush(''/overview'')`.\n- `<h3>Cluster Details</h3>` was the one heading the migration missed;\n  `text-[10px] … tracking-[0.8px]` is the named `text-caption` rung; the\n  hand-rolled TextDivider is the Registry''s `FieldSeparator`; the broker table''s\n  `tableOptions` restated the DataTable''s own default and cost a fresh object\n  per render.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: login surfaces — registry text style for the login-complete splash, radius on the OIDC anchor\n\n- text-[1.5em] (flagged by the lookout audit) becomes text-heading-lg, the rung the login page heading already uses.\n- The OIDC anchor keeps buttonVariants and adds rounded-md; the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login — second review round\n\n- Overview: the four section headings carried a dead text class while Overview.scss painted them a hard-coded near-black; the scss now uses the foreground token. The Cluster Status stripe never rendered because its selector still targeted .ant-statistic; it targets the Registry Stat and uses semantic tokens. Statistic wrapper replaced by Stat here and on broker details. Broker table paginates like the legacy one (50, pager only past that); column size hints the Registry ignores are gone; a 0-byte broker shows ''0 B''; the footer''s non-existent font-sm class is text-body-sm.\n- Cluster health: link-styled anchors drop the button height; unknown health reasons read ''Unknown reason'' instead of an enum number. The store''s debugBundleStatus getter prefers the RUNNING broker status, so the in-progress link gets its job id.\n- Config list: the three remaining literal colours in ConfigList.module.scss are tokens.\n- Login: Button isLoading instead of a hand-rolled spinner; the logo takes the foreground colour; the OR separator''s label chip matches the page ground in dark; heading rung is text-heading-xl (the original 1.5em), also on login-complete.\n- auth.setup.ts waits on the dialog''s own button disappearing instead of a swallowed overlay selector.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login — final review\n\n- Broker table stays at ten a page with the pager only past that (it had defaultPageSize 10, not 50).\n- Cluster-details headings keep a legible rung (text-heading-sm / text-body-sm) instead of shrinking to caption sizes; the docs footer inherits its size.\n- Config list: column size hints the Registry never reads are gone, the chevrons no longer carry an inert size class, and the two stylesheets drop orphaned selectors and history comments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: overview, broker and login — reviewer round\n\nCluster Status stat: the left stripe (clipped on self-hosted and with the\nnew-overview flag off) becomes a Registry StatusDot in the value; the\nstripe SCSS goes. OptionGroup renders its ToggleGroup as `outline`, so the\nFormatting/Sort segments on broker details sit in a track. The login\nerror Alert carries `auth-error`, asserted by a new enterprise spec for\nthe wrong-password path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: login — rejected-password path under JSDOM\n\nThe enterprise e2e spec needs a backend; this drives the same form with a\nstubbed authentication client: one request in flight with the button\ndisabled, then the inline error and a re-enabled form.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoJP2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASbEQABBEbPqD0ztS3jYu78xyeEw7\nLYcLucqQxqLhlnFcO7KDYBXgpN9X8UEPyD1yQ/Z6acmxx7GnfqcTHABByo1PfKY0\nICfp5idqET6FuAI6t1WB1sG9Y2Iqx8lVxfezrh3QPGkRIVe4smcM6yJiveXAdiky\niGmsUVITVui7j8iXSenWyNLH/VitQA5EiRME8fAz0KqphwFp/W5ScGtJ+x7qW5fk\nfuxp3uV8hhzPnQBLlSrVkafagXvc/xXsPeyqzcbxFcUJYvko9oSjaL25NA0J+AIN\nZLzJav0oUhB3j4d7qfC9/NuUmRb9tdq9My/cPjlp0m2X7Z0OlEmxlfiaZvcm5SLB\npxrCxselGbsLOnisfb8EAespfvPJw7jQmSsfzEFsdgxnbpOEtkmS36EWr3yoBwjm\nphd/w3mG2q6WP5MyldhgiYyzUtdhhRkdd8bgXfVYH4rVEouFqRlAokiVxCNc5CuO\nLGIUm+t3snpuZGygYd6zQue3w1O7C5Ew2Yz3C2unKt/dQaaSmJASdeKRYGIONjVB\nB0ypJqdZYbbzfm/0hWPW92XNJJGXiB4znNR2wVf5L43jvkCAjXSoZErlWW//z2B1\nBpC5xkbwW9WtFRIhIf0UwQGrh/edTkgjDrjy7LPc0tWuVQKow50R3m8lsBjcpRyS\nhFuI75mw61MXIgkxtC+e\n=ZMe9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T23:02:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKDIyMDdiOWQwM2I4NjZiNDBkM2EyOTQwNTZmN2Y0NmE2ZjZlN2U1ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","sha":"a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77"}],"sha":"2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/2207b9d03b866b40d3a294056f7f46a6f6e7e5f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:37:08Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:37:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 6/14] frontend: admin, debug bundle and license pages on Registry components (#2634)\n\n* frontend: admin, debug bundle and license pages on Registry components\n\nNine files. The mechanical bulk is Chakra layout props to Tailwind classes and\nChakra Alert to the Registry one (which paints its own icon, so AlertIcon goes\nand the tone picks the icon). The parts that carry judgement:\n\n- Navigation dressed as a button stays an anchor. The Registry Button forces\n  role=\"button\" even through `as={Link}`, which loses link semantics and breaks\n  `getByRole(''link'')` — debug-bundle-page.ts looks up \"Bundle generation in\n  progress\" that way, and license-utils.test.tsx reads both license CTAs as\n  links. All three now use `<Link className={buttonVariants(...)}>`, the shape\n  not-found-page already uses.\n- Chakra''s FormField becomes Field + FieldLabel + FieldDescription +\n  FieldError, with an id on every control so `getByLabel(/cpu profiler/i)` and\n  friends keep resolving. Label selector inputs, which had no label, get\n  aria-label.\n- `Select isMulti` -> SimpleMultiSelect (string-valued, so broker IDs round-trip\n  through Number); the unit dropdowns -> SingleSelect<number>; PasswordInput ->\n  `Input type=\"password\"`, which already has the eye toggle; ConfirmModal ->\n  AlertDialog with Cancel/Confirm.\n- Chakra''s Result rendered its title as an h1 and its subtitle as an h2;\n  license.spec.ts asserts on the h1, so that stays and the subtitle becomes body\n  text, which is what it always was.\n- The dev-panda SVG only existed as a data URI inside the Chakra bundle, so it\n  is vendored to assets/redpanda/DevPandaFrontView.svg.\n- The license-expired scrim was a literal `bg=\"white\"`, unreadable in the dark\n  theme; it now takes bg-background.\n\nlicense-utils.test.tsx asserted Chakra''s `data-status` attribute; the Registry\nAlert carries its tone in the variant classes, so the assertion follows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the admin, debug bundle and license migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The Register button lost its accessible name while submitting.** `isLoading`\n  hides the label with `visibility: hidden`, which also removes it from the\n  accessibility tree — so the comment claiming the name stayed \"Register\" was\n  wrong. It is now set explicitly.\n- **Both license CTAs rendered underlined.** `AlertDescription` puts\n  `[&_a]:link-inline` on every descendant anchor, which outranks the button\n  styling on the two anchors that replaced `Button as={Link}`. The CTA row opts\n  out.\n- **The advanced-feature alert stacked as fragments.** `AlertDescription` is\n  `display: grid`, so a loose text run becomes its own row; it is one `<p>` now.\n- **A rejected file drop was silent.** The Registry Dropzone reports rejections\n  only through `onError` and then skips `onDrop` entirely, where Chakra''s took\n  the first file regardless — so dropping two files, or one over the size limit,\n  changed nothing on screen and Upload then posted `undefined`. `onError` is\n  wired, and `droppedFiles` is only set once the read resolves, so the dropzone\n  can no longer show a filename for a file that failed to read. `errorMessage`\n  is also cleared on a new drop and on submit instead of persisting.\n- **The two multi-selects had no accessible label.** `SimpleMultiSelect`\n  forwards neither `aria-label` nor `aria-labelledby` and its trigger is a\n  `<div>` carrying a hardcoded `aria-label=\"Multi-select trigger\"`, so\n  `<FieldLabel htmlFor>` associated nothing. One local `LabelledMultiSelect`\n  composes the parts so `aria-labelledby` gets through — which is what Chakra''s\n  `FormField label` did — and carries `aria-invalid`/`aria-describedby` too.\n- **The in-progress link could point at `/debug-bundle/progress/`**, which\n  matches no route, when the job id was empty; it renders only with an id now.\n  `debug-bundle-page.ts` clicks exactly this link.\n- The four \"number + unit\" fields were four hand-written copies of one control;\n  they are now one `NumberWithUnitField` (−108/+175 including the two helpers,\n  so the four call sites drop from ~88 lines to ~40). It also stops the input\n  from displaying \"NaN\" mid-retype — the stored value is unchanged, which is\n  what the pre-migration code did.\n- Debug-bundle body copy gets `text-body`, matching the license surfaces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: keep the admin and license migration under the complexity budget\n\n`bun run lint` is `ultracite fix`, which exits 0 while leaving errors — the real\ngate is `lint:check`, and it showed two net-new\n`noExcessiveCognitiveComplexity` errors this branch introduced:\n\n- register-modal: `{err ? <FieldError>{err}</FieldError> : null}` three times.\n  `FieldError` already returns null with no content, so the guards were both\n  redundant and three branches against the budget.\n- admin-debug-bundle: `data-invalid={Boolean(x) || undefined}` seven times. The\n  coercion is needed (`data-invalid={false}` renders the string \"false\"), so it\n  moves to a module-level `invalidFlag` helper instead of seven inline branches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for admin and license — Link buttons keep their radius, label-selector rows keep focus\n\n- Try again/Done on the debug-bundle progress page go back to a Button (as={Link}); the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants, so the plain Link rendered square.\n- License CTAs stay anchors (link role is asserted) and add rounded-md for the same reason.\n- Label-selector rows were keyed by key+value, so every keystroke remounted the row and dropped focus; rows now carry a stable id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: admin and license — second review round\n\n- License banner: the enterprise-features sentence sat directly in the grid AlertDescription, so its <strong> became its own row; one block child. Overview banner: button-styled CTAs rendered as anchors were underlined by the description''s anchor rule.\n- Debug bundle: Cancel in the confirm dialog rendered outlined because AlertDialogCancel merges its own variant classes — use its variant prop. The number-with-unit rows had the unit select taking the row and the input squeezed. The in-progress link now derives from the RUNNING broker status, not the first one. ''Skip TLS verification'' and ''Metrics samples'' were never sent; wire both.\n- Upload license: Textarea rows is inert under content sizing (resize=vertical restores it); a rejected re-drop clears the stale file instead of submitting it under the error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: admin and license — comments trimmed to their constraints\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"08c2cccc6b058c3ce004cdbd8f52240c878a26b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/08c2cccc6b058c3ce004cdbd8f52240c878a26b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","verification":{"payload":"tree 08c2cccc6b058c3ce004cdbd8f52240c878a26b6\nparent 0b2f23ff4b5211c162f002cc2587a0aebc43237e\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788907028 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788907028 -070