laude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the admin, debug bundle and license migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The Register button lost its accessible name while submitting.** `isLoading`\n  hides the label with `visibility: hidden`, which also removes it from the\n  accessibility tree — so the comment claiming the name stayed \"Register\" was\n  wrong. It is now set explicitly.\n- **Both license CTAs rendered underlined.** `AlertDescription` puts\n  `[&_a]:link-inline` on every descendant anchor, which outranks the button\n  styling on the two anchors that replaced `Button as={Link}`. The CTA row opts\n  out.\n- **The advanced-feature alert stacked as fragments.** `AlertDescription` is\n  `display: grid`, so a loose text run becomes its own row; it is one `<p>` now.\n- **A rejected file drop was silent.** The Registry Dropzone reports rejections\n  only through `onError` and then skips `onDrop` entirely, where Chakra''s took\n  the first file regardless — so dropping two files, or one over the size limit,\n  changed nothing on screen and Upload then posted `undefined`. `onError` is\n  wired, and `droppedFiles` is only set once the read resolves, so the dropzone\n  can no longer show a filename for a file that failed to read. `errorMessage`\n  is also cleared on a new drop and on submit instead of persisting.\n- **The two multi-selects had no accessible label.** `SimpleMultiSelect`\n  forwards neither `aria-label` nor `aria-labelledby` and its trigger is a\n  `<div>` carrying a hardcoded `aria-label=\"Multi-select trigger\"`, so\n  `<FieldLabel htmlFor>` associated nothing. One local `LabelledMultiSelect`\n  composes the parts so `aria-labelledby` gets through — which is what Chakra''s\n  `FormField label` did — and carries `aria-invalid`/`aria-describedby` too.\n- **The in-progress link could point at `/debug-bundle/progress/`**, which\n  matches no route, when the job id was empty; it renders only with an id now.\n  `debug-bundle-page.ts` clicks exactly this link.\n- The four \"number + unit\" fields were four hand-written copies of one control;\n  they are now one `NumberWithUnitField` (−108/+175 including the two helpers,\n  so the four call sites drop from ~88 lines to ~40). It also stops the input\n  from displaying \"NaN\" mid-retype — the stored value is unchanged, which is\n  what the pre-migration code did.\n- Debug-bundle body copy gets `text-body`, matching the license surfaces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: keep the admin and license migration under the complexity budget\n\n`bun run lint` is `ultracite fix`, which exits 0 while leaving errors — the real\ngate is `lint:check`, and it showed two net-new\n`noExcessiveCognitiveComplexity` errors this branch introduced:\n\n- register-modal: `{err ? <FieldError>{err}</FieldError> : null}` three times.\n  `FieldError` already returns null with no content, so the guards were both\n  redundant and three branches against the budget.\n- admin-debug-bundle: `data-invalid={Boolean(x) || undefined}` seven times. The\n  coercion is needed (`data-invalid={false}` renders the string \"false\"), so it\n  moves to a module-level `invalidFlag` helper instead of seven inline branches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for admin and license — Link buttons keep their radius, label-selector rows keep focus\n\n- Try again/Done on the debug-bundle progress page go back to a Button (as={Link}); the radius lives on the Button component, not in buttonVariants, so the plain Link rendered square.\n- License CTAs stay anchors (link role is asserted) and add rounded-md for the same reason.\n- Label-selector rows were keyed by key+value, so every keystroke remounted the row and dropped focus; rows now carry a stable id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: admin and license — second review round\n\n- License banner: the enterprise-features sentence sat directly in the grid AlertDescription, so its <strong> became its own row; one block child. Overview banner: button-styled CTAs rendered as anchors were underlined by the description''s anchor rule.\n- Debug bundle: Cancel in the confirm dialog rendered outlined because AlertDialogCancel merges its own variant classes — use its variant prop. The number-with-unit rows had the unit select taking the row and the input squeezed. The in-progress link now derives from the RUNNING broker status, not the first one. ''Skip TLS verification'' and ''Metrics samples'' were never sent; wire both.\n- Upload license: Textarea rows is inert under content sizing (resize=vertical restores it); a rejected re-drop clears the stale file instead of submitting it under the error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: admin and license — comments trimmed to their constraints\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoI4UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATXgQAAMajHdL9IqWVLCBZ62W65xw\nH8Rd3MqHspF5f1nP+GGk8Bm/6juSTtca8li1nh22R2019cCSV67RD3rIOCogA1Vv\nwzFvOjx6G4SlLduo2jcVpcObIUKUvMGLWA2J8Y8hFoC4OLhnIj4QQg/SUlzOfvxv\nj2d2DEmZHV0W71AVa7SEyagM2LziYEgiGAlNYD0DOAkiI9DQmOuM17+cHZxdJEVF\n1734zX6t33Fl+gwAIrCT/6CirwRIYId1IQWrObXPxpXD/rPRcKze7b+Xf0xFRh1R\nfWYqyH9Nq8VnqpYaO+8ZzhJ5yzZdws4pIgwDfUFf3Ovx7RGZfQ2GjTRkhXH6bPZZ\nw9S2l1rDQ8LvOTquLM90tpFuHZgUxgIDIeSRTfYH/LAqamPL8jwKFwl+AqOC2+RF\nW/W3sxgJQcUHfL0GbS/X09Ka1eYqJEsE/ttUqCRZNZ/0DQ/Z9L/lMBdPoP+aKbL/\n+Td9fAFPOMqKvAIWg5hgWtTcmXVFYmALZDLbPAJLJLwu1WrWomDgoeH438Z/leEq\nRRXn5lVFj1TjKixejDyKXuAQhzPtCNBAxgg3aK1J5+OQx3jnvoRKbXYcMNXfR3gi\n6bhWhKp41XtxeDW3TNQZcRhs5JA/67vlYLI1HA0/WF4yd/NkfVIs0a47ODAn9YL0\nzorW280WPPmQdd14jF+/\n=4w4D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T22:37:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGEzZDU1MGZjMzJhODBjY2RiNmIyMzYxZDM1MjhkNDVjZjNlZDlkNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/0b2f23ff4b5211c162f002cc2587a0aebc43237e","sha":"0b2f23ff4b5211c162f002cc2587a0aebc43237e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/0b2f23ff4b5211c162f002cc2587a0aebc43237e"}],"sha":"a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/a3d550fc32a80ccdb6b2361d3528d45cf3ed9d77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/0b2f23ff4b5211c162f002cc2587a0aebc43237e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:23:43Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:23:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 5/14] frontend: transforms pages on Registry components (#2633)\n\n* frontend: smoke spec for the transforms setup page\n\ntransforms.spec.ts is commented out end to end because it needs transforms\nseeded through the backend API. The setup page has no such dependency, so it\ncan carry coverage for the re-skin that follows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: transforms pages on Registry components\n\nFour files, no behaviour changes:\n\n- transforms-list: Chakra DataTable -> Registry DataTable with\n  DataTableColumnHeader on the two sortable columns; SearchField -> Input with\n  the search-field-* test ids; Section and the delete modal kept.\n- transform-details: same table swap, drops the LegacyColumnDef import and the\n  controlled SortingState (nothing else read it). Chakra took the URL-derived\n  pagination as an initial value with no writer, so it moves to\n  tableOptions.initialState.\n- transforms-setup: Alert paints its own icon now, so AlertIcon goes; CodeBlock\n  takes its code as a child.\n- modals: Chakra Modal -> Registry Dialog, open through utils/modal-container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the expander column on the transform logs table\n\nChakra''s DataTable injected an expander column whenever `subComponent` was\nset; the Registry one does not, so the expanded-message panel had no way to\nopen. Same column shape the new topic messages page already uses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: review fixes for the transforms migration\n\nFound by a review pass over the branch:\n\n- **The Hint alert rendered as five stacked fragments.** The Registry\n  `AlertDescription` is `display: grid`, so each loose text run and each\n  `<InlineCode>` became its own row. Its content is now one `<p>`.\n- **Both code blocks lost syntax highlighting.** `<CodeBlock><Pre>{text}</Pre>`\n  emits a bare text node with no `<code>` and no language. They now use\n  `DynamicCodeBlock`, which is what the migrated schema pages use.\n- **The logs table lost click-to-sort.** Chakra''s DataTable painted the sort\n  affordance on every header itself; the Registry only sorts through\n  `DataTableColumnHeader`. Timestamp gets one; Value is explicitly\n  `enableSorting: false`, since its cell renders a decoded preview and sorting\n  the raw value was never meaningful.\n- **`DataTableColumnHeader` offers a \"Hide\" item with no way back** — these\n  pages have no `DataTableViewOptions` toolbar, so every column using it is\n  `enableHiding: false`.\n- **The clear button unmounted itself.** `InputEnd` reports its width but never\n  resets it on unmount, so clearing the search left the input padded for a\n  button that was gone — and the click landed on the element being removed,\n  dropping focus to `<body>`. It stays mounted and the button goes invisible.\n- The expander button gets `aria-expanded`: the Registry sets it on the row,\n  and only for `expandRowByClick`, which these tables do not use.\n- The log column model was rebuilt five times a second by the 200ms poll;\n  it and the table options are memoized now.\n- The quick-search regex was compiled once per row per render; hoisted.\n- Icons come from `components/icons` where it aliases them — `XIcon` and\n  `CloseIcon` were the same lucide glyph imported twice under two names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(review): restore transform partition sorting\n\n* frontend: transforms — shared SearchInput, table parity with the legacy DataTable, logs column layout\n\n- New misc/search-input.tsx: leading icon, clear button that refocuses the field, click-through while empty, / to focus and Escape to clear — the Chakra SearchField contract the raw Input dropped. Used by both transforms search boxes.\n- Tables: the legacy DataTable paginated at 50 and hid the pager under 50 rows; restore that on the list and partition tables instead of 10-a-page with a permanent footer, or no pagination at all.\n- Logs table: the Registry ignores column sizes, so the Value column collapsed; hand it the slack and keep timestamps on one line. Rows are keyed by partition+offset so an expanded row follows its message; the URL page hook only fed an initialState TanStack reads once.\n- Dialog title clears the absolute close button; static snippets use SimpleCodeBlock instead of the async highlighter; the partition test resets the store inside act().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: transforms — final review\n\n- Setup page keeps the terminal look: SyncCodeBlock for the bash command (highlighted synchronously), DynamicCodeBlock for the listing; SimpleCodeBlock had dropped the highlighting.\n- Logs table shows no pager under its loading or empty row, as the legacy table.\n- SearchInput advertises its shortcuts (aria-keyshortcuts on the field, a title on the clear button).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: transforms — lint formatting\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: transforms — hiding off at table level\n\nenableHiding: false moves from every column into the tables'' shared options, so\na column added later cannot bring the header menu''s \"Hide\" item back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Beniamin Malinski <malinskibeniamin@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a7bf76faa04339d8cf15497e44a08ebc6960965","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/0a7bf76faa04339d8cf15497e44a08ebc6960965"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/0b2f23ff4b5211c162f002cc2587a0aebc43237e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a7bf76faa04339d8cf15497e44a08ebc6960965\nparent 2c35c7061dace5b0abc99a1362965f2a1ba36f0b\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788906223 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788906223 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 2 · PR 5/14] frontend: transforms pages on Registry components (#2633)\n\n* frontend: smoke spec for the transforms setup page\n\ntransforms.spec.ts is commented out end to end because it needs transforms\nseeded through the backend API. The setup page has no such dependency, so it\ncan carry coverage for the re-skin that follows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: transforms pages on Registry components\n\nFour files, no behaviour changes:\n\n- transforms-list: Chakra DataTable -> Registry DataTable with\n  DataTableColumnHeader on the two sortable columns; SearchField -> Input with\n  the search-field-* test ids; Section and the delete modal kept.\n- transform-details: same table swap, drops the LegacyColumnDef import and the\n  controlled SortingState (nothing else read it). Chakra took the URL-derived\n  pagination as an initial value with no writer,