te_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/cf1c420f372c11854aafac360ca4de97765ed15b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:21:33Z","email":"jan.vorcak@redpanda.com","name":"Ján Vorčák"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:21:33Z","email":"jan.vorcak@redpanda.com","name":"Ján Vorčák"},"message":"frontend: address review findings on continuous mode and live tail\n\n- display window follows the loading frontier: keep the tail of the\n  ordered array so continuous \"Newest\" pagination advances past the cap\n  instead of fetching pages it silently discards; footer reports which\n  side was trimmed (\"newer\" for that scope)\n- bound the paged/continuous backing buffer (PAGED_BUFFER_MAX 5000) so\n  \"Load more\" cannot grow memory without limit\n- live tail loop exposes status (running/retrying/exhausted) and\n  restart(); Retry and toolbar refresh restart an exhausted loop with a\n  fresh failure budget, and the \"streaming\" UI derives from the actual\n  loop status rather than the URL toggle\n- message-flash animation becomes a Tailwind v4 @theme token instead of\n  a hand-rolled class; selected table row uses bg-selected-wash\n- regression tests for the frontier window, exhausted status and restart","tree":{"sha":"af8ac38552e8b52259683dc63d146e6ce3bcb48e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/af8ac38552e8b52259683dc63d146e6ce3bcb48e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/cf1c420f372c11854aafac360ca4de97765ed15b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1083817?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jvorcak","id":1083817,"login":"jvorcak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODM4MTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/cf1c420f372c11854aafac360ca4de97765ed15b","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGNmMWM0MjBmMzcyYzExODU0YWFmYWMzNjBjYTRkZTk3NzY1ZWQxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/cb8f85b599ca81b37c9b2b7ef2f9c86078f72bdd","sha":"cb8f85b599ca81b37c9b2b7ef2f9c86078f72bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/cb8f85b599ca81b37c9b2b7ef2f9c86078f72bdd"}],"sha":"cf1c420f372c11854aafac360ca4de97765ed15b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/cf1c420f372c11854aafac360ca4de97765ed15b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/9c834fd91637a27492c195f3338f4cf9c243c0cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:56:11Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:56:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 1 · PR 4/14] frontend: SingleSelect and the error/not-found surfaces on Registry components, plus two guard tests (#2629)\n\n* frontend: Registry internals for the shared display wrappers, drop Chakra type seams\n\nFive app-owned wrappers keep their exports and get Registry internals, so\ntheir importers do not change:\n\n- tsx-utils: DefaultSkeleton -> SkeletonText; InfoText -> one Tooltip /\n  TooltipTrigger / TooltipContent tree (placement narrows to top|bottom|\n  left|right, no caller passed one); OptionGroup -> RadioGroup +\n  RadioGroupItem nested in the Registry Label. The file no longer imports\n  @redpanda-data/ui.\n- misc/section: Chakra Section -> Card size=\"full\" kept in block flow with\n  Section''s px-6; props are children, id, className and a grid-area-only\n  style. The 17 call sites that passed py / my / minWidth / gridArea /\n  overflowY / borderColor move them to a class, a wrapper or gridArea;\n  flexDirection on a block Box was a no-op. Overview''s <hr> keeps the\n  margins the Chakra Section injected. LogsTab loses a `variant` no caller\n  passed.\n- misc/tabs: Chakra Tabs items= -> Registry Tabs, uncontrolled with\n  defaultValue, underline variant, activateOnFocus so arrow keys still\n  select; panels keep Chakra''s 1rem padding; isFitted -> layout=\"full\".\n  Its six tests pass unchanged.\n- misc/statistic: Chakra Stat -> Registry Stat label/value (title, value,\n  className; hint and SpaceProps had no callers). Spacing moves to the\n  rows that lay stats out (Flex gap={8} / flex gap-8).\n- misc/small-stat: Flex + Text -> a flex div.\n\nType seams: state/ui.ts takes SortingState from @tanstack/react-table (same\nshape as the v8 one Chakra re-exported) and defines ConnectTabKeys itself\ninstead of importing it from pages/connect/overview. TopicTabId stays an\n`import type` from topic-details until the #2588 stream lands.\nutils/legacy-data-table.ts is untouched on purpose: it derives its types\nfrom the legacy DataTable because the v9 ColumnDef is the wrong shape for\nit, and deletes with the last legacy table.\n\nImporters of @redpanda-data/ui: 95 -> 89.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: paint .codeBox with theme tokens\n\n`Code` in tsx-utils and nine raw call sites render `.codeBox`, which\nhardcoded a light grey background with no text colour, so in the dark\ntheme the inherited light foreground sat on a light box and the text was\nunreadable (seen on the topic-messages \"Backend Error\" alert). Background\nand border now come from the surface and border tokens, which resolve in\nboth themes and match the registry''s inline code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the segmented OptionGroup, large stat values, user-only tab changes\n\nSecond review pass on the display wrappers:\n- OptionGroup renders a segmented ToggleGroup, which is what the Chakra\n  RadioCard group looked like; radio circles were an undisclosed change.\n- Statistic uses Stat size=\"lg\" so headline numbers keep their weight and\n  size instead of dropping to body text.\n- Tabs forwards onChange only for user activation; Base UI also reports\n  its own initial/fallback selection, which the Chakra wrapper never did.\n- Overview drops a gridArea on a Section whose parent is a flex column.\n- .codeBox paints with surface-recess and border-subtle, the tokens the\n  theme documents for a code block; its dead .noPadding tint goes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: SingleSelect and the error/not-found surfaces on Registry components, plus two guard tests\n\nLast Phase 1 PR of the Chakra exit. Every wrapper keeps its export.\n\n- misc/select: SingleSelect<T> on the Registry Select; values round-trip\n  through a string key so enum/number callers keep their types, an unset\n  value selects nothing (no collision with an empty-string option), and an\n  `id` lands on the trigger for <label htmlFor>. The one `creatable`\n  caller (preview-settings) goes to the Registry Combobox with the old\n  cannot-clear behaviour kept. `data-testid` still wraps the control in a\n  div, which is the e2e page object''s contract. login.tsx drops a no-op\n  chakraStyles prop and labels the SASL select through FormControl''s id.\n  tests/mock-react-select.tsx and its two setup imports are gone; nothing\n  rendered react-select under test.\n- Tab.Messages column-settings and preview-fields-modal: the two Chakra\n  modals that host SingleSelect provide a PortalContainer, so Base UI\n  popups render inside the modal''s focus and scroll lock.\n- misc/error-result: flex divs + text-heading-lg/text-body-lg, Registry\n  SimpleCodeBlock, the local ErrorBananaSlip.svg instead of Chakra Avatars.\n- misc/error-display: Chakra Result -> Registry Empty + Button; Chakra\n  Section -> the app Section wrapper; List -> a plain ul.\n- misc/error-modal: Chakra Modal -> Registry Dialog size=\"xl\" (keeps the\n  old 3xl footprint); Base UI''s onOpenChangeComplete(false) replaces\n  onCloseComplete for the queue.\n- misc/error-boundary: Box/Flex/Icon -> divs; Registry Button size=\"lg\"\n  with leading icons and isLoading.\n- misc/not-found-page, not-found-content: divs + h1.text-heading-xl (keeps\n  the level-1 heading the test asserts); the test''s Chakra mock is deleted.\n- utils/modal-container: Box -> div.\n- src/components/registry-guards/: app-owned tests for two registry\n  contracts the registry ships untested - an expanded DataTable row\n  survives a data swap (fails with autoResetExpanded: true), and Alert\n  paints exactly one icon by default, replaces it for `icon`, and paints\n  none for `icon={null}`. Not under components/ui/ because Biome ignores\n  that directory.\n\nImporters of @redpanda-data/ui: 89 -> 81.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: SingleSelect shows out-of-list values, coherent clearing, and parity fixes for the error surfaces\n\nSecond review pass on the interactive and error surfaces:\n- SingleSelect passes the current value through even when it is not in\n  `options`, so a connector property or schema version outside the\n  suggested list still shows as text, as the old select did. The creatable\n  field forwards the Combobox''s clear signals instead of swallowing them,\n  so the field never shows empty while a pattern still applies. One option\n  array feeds both Registry controls; labels are strings, which every\n  caller passes.\n- Hero and error headings keep their weight (font-semibold) and the\n  error-result title stays at the 24px rung.\n- error-result keeps a text fallback when its illustration fails to load,\n  and the detail code block keeps the old geometry (no outer margin, no\n  height cap).\n- error-modal sizes its icon directly instead of a 70px wrapper.\n- error-display collapses identical messages, so list keys are unique.\n- The two registry guard tests move to src/__tests__/, beside the existing\n  consumer-side guard, and drain TanStack''s microtask reset with act().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aec0adecfbd345c0d39f41d393984d9945e21391","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/aec0adecfbd345c0d39f41d393984d9945e21391"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/9c834fd91637a27492c195f3338f4cf9c243c0cd","verification":{"payload":"tree aec0adecfbd345c0d39f41d393984d9945e21391\nparent 60125eca37bcb422818c4a8d663a1bac1ad568ea\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788875771 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788875771 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 1 · PR 4/14] frontend: SingleSelect and the error/not-found surfaces on Registry components, plus two guard tests (#2629)\n\n* frontend: Registry internals for the shared display wrappers, drop Chakra type seams\n\nFive app-owned wrappers keep their exports and get Registry internals, so\ntheir importers do not change:\n\n- tsx-utils: DefaultSkeleton -> SkeletonText; InfoText -> one Tooltip /\n  TooltipTrigger / TooltipContent tree (placement narrows to top|bottom|\n  left|right, no caller passed one); OptionGroup -> RadioGroup +\n  RadioGroupItem nested in the Registry Label. The file no longer imports\n  @redpanda-data/ui.\n- misc/section: Chakra Section -> Card size=\"full\" kept in block flow with\n  Section''s px-6; props are children, id, className and a grid-area-only\n  style. The 17 call sites that passed py / my / minWidth / gridArea /\n  overflowY / borderColor move them to a class, a wrapper or gridArea;\n  flexDirection on a block Box was a no-op. Overview''s <hr> keeps the\n  margins the Chakra Section injected. LogsTab loses a `variant` no caller\n  passed.\n- misc/tabs: Chakra Tabs items= -> Registry Tabs, uncontrolled with\n  defaultValue, underline variant, activateOnFocus so arrow keys still\n  select; panels keep Chakra''s 1rem padding; isFitted -> layout=\"full\".\n  Its six tests pass unchanged.\n- misc/statistic: Chakra Stat -> Registry Stat label/value (title, value,\n  className; hint and SpaceProps had no callers). Spacing moves to the\n  rows that lay stats out (Flex gap={8} / flex gap-8).\n- misc/small-stat: Flex + Text -> a flex div.\n\nType seams: state/ui.ts takes SortingState from @tanstack/react-table (same\nshape as the v8 one Chakra re-exported) and defines ConnectTabKeys itself\ninstead of importing it from pages/connect/overview. TopicTabId stays an\n`import type` from topic-details until the #2588 stream lands.\nutils/legacy-data-table.ts is untouched on purpose: it derives its types\nfrom the legacy DataTable because the v9 ColumnDef is the wrong shape for\nit, and deletes with the last legacy table.\n\nImporters of @redpanda-data/ui: 95 -> 89.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: paint .codeBox with theme tokens\n\n`Code` in tsx-utils and nine raw call sites render `.codeBox`, which\nhardcoded a light grey background with no text colour, so in the dark\ntheme the inherited light foreground sat on a light box and the text was\nunreadable (seen on the topic-messages \"Backend Error\" alert). Background\nand border now come from the surface and border tokens, which resolve in\nboth themes and match the registry''s inline code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the segmented OptionGroup, large stat values, user-only tab changes\n\nSecond review pass on the display wrappers:\n- OptionGroup renders a segmented ToggleGroup, which is what the Chakra\n  RadioCard group looked like; radio circles were an undisclosed change.\n- Statistic uses Stat size=\"lg\" so headline numbers keep their weight and\n  size instead of dropping to body text.\n- Tabs forwards onChange only for user activation; Base UI also reports\n  its own initial/fallback selection, which the Chakra wrapper never did.\n- Overview drops a gridArea on a Section whose parent is a flex column.\n- .codeBox paints with surface-recess and border-subtle, the tokens the\n  theme documents for a code block; its dead .noPadding tint goes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: SingleSelect and the error/not-found surfaces on Registry components, plus two guard tests\n\nLast Phase 1 PR of the Chakra exit. Every wrapper keeps its export.\n\n- misc/select: SingleSelect<T> on the Registry Select; values round-trip\n  through a string key so enum/number callers keep their types, an unset\n  value selects nothing (no collision with an empty-string option), and an\n  `id` lands on the trigger for <label htmlFor>. The one `creatable`\n  caller (preview-settings) goes to the Registry Combobox with the old\n  cannot-clear behaviour kept. `data-testid` still wraps the control in a\n  div, which is the e2e page object''s contract. login.tsx drops a no-op\n  chakraStyles prop and labels the SASL select through FormControl''s id.\n  tests/mock-react-select.tsx and its two setup imports are gone; nothing\n  rendered react-select under test.\n- Tab.Messages column-settings and preview-fields-modal: the two Chakra\n  modals that host SingleSelect provide a PortalContainer, so Base UI\n  popups render inside the modal''s focus and scroll lock.\n- misc/error-result: flex divs + text-heading-lg/text-body-lg, Registry\n  SimpleCodeBlock, the local ErrorBananaSlip.svg instead of Chakra Avatars.\n- misc/error-display: Chakra Result -> Registry Empty + Button; Chakra\n  Section -> the app Section wrapper; List -> a plain ul.\n- misc/error-modal: Chakra Modal -> Registry Dialog size=\"xl\" (keeps the\n  old 3xl footprint); Base UI''s onOpenChangeComplete(false) replaces\n  onCloseComplete for the queue.\n- misc/error-boundary: Box/Flex/Icon -> divs; Registry Button size=\"lg\"\n  with leading icons and isLoading.\n- misc/not-found-page, not-found-content: divs + h1.text-heading-xl (keeps\n  the level-1 heading the test asserts); the test''s Chakra mock is deleted.\n- utils/modal-container: Box -> div.\n- src/components/registry-guards/: app-owned tests for two registry\n  contracts the registry ships untested - an expanded DataTable row\n  survives a data swap (fails with autoResetExpanded: true), and Alert\n  paints exactly one icon by default, replaces it for `icon`, and paints\n  none for `icon={null}`. Not under components/ui/ because Biome ignores\n  that directory.\n\nImporters of @redpanda-data/ui: 89 -> 81.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: SingleSelect shows out-of-list values, coherent clearing, and parity fixes for the error surfaces\n\nSecond review pass on the interactive and error surfaces:\n- SingleSelect passes the current value through even when it is not in\n  `options`, so a connector property or schema version outside the\n  suggested list still shows as text, as the old select did. The creatable\n  field forwards the Combobox''s clear signals instead of swallowing them,\n  so the field never shows empty while a pattern still applies. One option\n  array feeds both Registry controls; labels are strings, which every\n  caller passes.\n- Hero and error headings keep their weight (font-semibold) and the\n  error-result title stays at the 24px rung.\n- error-result keeps a text fallback when its illustration fails to load,\n  and the detail code block keeps the old geometry (no outer margin, no\n  height cap).\n- error-modal sizes its icon directly instead of a 70px wrapper.\n- error-display collapses identical messages, so list keys are unique.\n- The two registry guard tests move to src/__tests__/, beside the existing\n  consumer-side guard, and drain TanStack''s microtask reset with act().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoBP7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8UgQAKvhdwebQFkItFknoFCALQQK\nQyrW4iAfQd0SLeYtGiARTKXbPPoX3zFTjvfXItEYpjTfDSJ4X/4kujsLpInbDEF/\nMdAYzRlLkh3xooxXBXNDF8qIALWlTFbvNzQzOfSGl3a0IPyWwLL