st_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jvorcak","id":1083817,"login":"jvorcak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODM4MTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvorcak","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/e50dc5d9fa244f474765dd7dbf30acd16f680130","node_id":"C_kwDODJ1vatoAKGU1MGRjNWQ5ZmEyNDRmNDc0NzY1ZGQ3ZGJmMzBhY2QxNmY2ODAxMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/b0cb01260165e78c00085db0e728c8bcffc81d33","sha":"b0cb01260165e78c00085db0e728c8bcffc81d33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/b0cb01260165e78c00085db0e728c8bcffc81d33"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/redpanda-data/console/commit/60125eca37bcb422818c4a8d663a1bac1ad568ea","sha":"60125eca37bcb422818c4a8d663a1bac1ad568ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/60125eca37bcb422818c4a8d663a1bac1ad568ea"}],"sha":"e50dc5d9fa244f474765dd7dbf30acd16f680130","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/e50dc5d9fa244f474765dd7dbf30acd16f680130"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/60125eca37bcb422818c4a8d663a1bac1ad568ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T14:02:59Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T14:02:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 1 · PR 3/14] frontend: Registry internals for the shared display wrappers, drop Chakra type seams (#2628)\n\n* frontend: Registry internals for the shared display wrappers, drop Chakra type seams\n\nFive app-owned wrappers keep their exports and get Registry internals, so\ntheir importers do not change:\n\n- tsx-utils: DefaultSkeleton -> SkeletonText; InfoText -> one Tooltip /\n  TooltipTrigger / TooltipContent tree (placement narrows to top|bottom|\n  left|right, no caller passed one); OptionGroup -> RadioGroup +\n  RadioGroupItem nested in the Registry Label. The file no longer imports\n  @redpanda-data/ui.\n- misc/section: Chakra Section -> Card size=\"full\" kept in block flow with\n  Section''s px-6; props are children, id, className and a grid-area-only\n  style. The 17 call sites that passed py / my / minWidth / gridArea /\n  overflowY / borderColor move them to a class, a wrapper or gridArea;\n  flexDirection on a block Box was a no-op. Overview''s <hr> keeps the\n  margins the Chakra Section injected. LogsTab loses a `variant` no caller\n  passed.\n- misc/tabs: Chakra Tabs items= -> Registry Tabs, uncontrolled with\n  defaultValue, underline variant, activateOnFocus so arrow keys still\n  select; panels keep Chakra''s 1rem padding; isFitted -> layout=\"full\".\n  Its six tests pass unchanged.\n- misc/statistic: Chakra Stat -> Registry Stat label/value (title, value,\n  className; hint and SpaceProps had no callers). Spacing moves to the\n  rows that lay stats out (Flex gap={8} / flex gap-8).\n- misc/small-stat: Flex + Text -> a flex div.\n\nType seams: state/ui.ts takes SortingState from @tanstack/react-table (same\nshape as the v8 one Chakra re-exported) and defines ConnectTabKeys itself\ninstead of importing it from pages/connect/overview. TopicTabId stays an\n`import type` from topic-details until the #2588 stream lands.\nutils/legacy-data-table.ts is untouched on purpose: it derives its types\nfrom the legacy DataTable because the v9 ColumnDef is the wrong shape for\nit, and deletes with the last legacy table.\n\nImporters of @redpanda-data/ui: 95 -> 89.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: paint .codeBox with theme tokens\n\n`Code` in tsx-utils and nine raw call sites render `.codeBox`, which\nhardcoded a light grey background with no text colour, so in the dark\ntheme the inherited light foreground sat on a light box and the text was\nunreadable (seen on the topic-messages \"Backend Error\" alert). Background\nand border now come from the surface and border tokens, which resolve in\nboth themes and match the registry''s inline code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the segmented OptionGroup, large stat values, user-only tab changes\n\nSecond review pass on the display wrappers:\n- OptionGroup renders a segmented ToggleGroup, which is what the Chakra\n  RadioCard group looked like; radio circles were an undisclosed change.\n- Statistic uses Stat size=\"lg\" so headline numbers keep their weight and\n  size instead of dropping to body text.\n- Tabs forwards onChange only for user activation; Base UI also reports\n  its own initial/fallback selection, which the Chakra wrapper never did.\n- Overview drops a gridArea on a Section whose parent is a flex column.\n- .codeBox paints with surface-recess and border-subtle, the tokens the\n  theme documents for a code block; its dead .noPadding tint goes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbdb8a6362c0326f9e6c9d9b37f20a4131f60b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/cbdb8a6362c0326f9e6c9d9b37f20a4131f60b01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/60125eca37bcb422818c4a8d663a1bac1ad568ea","verification":{"payload":"tree cbdb8a6362c0326f9e6c9d9b37f20a4131f60b01\nparent e332531dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788789779 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788789779 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 1 · PR 3/14] frontend: Registry internals for the shared display wrappers, drop Chakra type seams (#2628)\n\n* frontend: Registry internals for the shared display wrappers, drop Chakra type seams\n\nFive app-owned wrappers keep their exports and get Registry internals, so\ntheir importers do not change:\n\n- tsx-utils: DefaultSkeleton -> SkeletonText; InfoText -> one Tooltip /\n  TooltipTrigger / TooltipContent tree (placement narrows to top|bottom|\n  left|right, no caller passed one); OptionGroup -> RadioGroup +\n  RadioGroupItem nested in the Registry Label. The file no longer imports\n  @redpanda-data/ui.\n- misc/section: Chakra Section -> Card size=\"full\" kept in block flow with\n  Section''s px-6; props are children, id, className and a grid-area-only\n  style. The 17 call sites that passed py / my / minWidth / gridArea /\n  overflowY / borderColor move them to a class, a wrapper or gridArea;\n  flexDirection on a block Box was a no-op. Overview''s <hr> keeps the\n  margins the Chakra Section injected. LogsTab loses a `variant` no caller\n  passed.\n- misc/tabs: Chakra Tabs items= -> Registry Tabs, uncontrolled with\n  defaultValue, underline variant, activateOnFocus so arrow keys still\n  select; panels keep Chakra''s 1rem padding; isFitted -> layout=\"full\".\n  Its six tests pass unchanged.\n- misc/statistic: Chakra Stat -> Registry Stat label/value (title, value,\n  className; hint and SpaceProps had no callers). Spacing moves to the\n  rows that lay stats out (Flex gap={8} / flex gap-8).\n- misc/small-stat: Flex + Text -> a flex div.\n\nType seams: state/ui.ts takes SortingState from @tanstack/react-table (same\nshape as the v8 one Chakra re-exported) and defines ConnectTabKeys itself\ninstead of importing it from pages/connect/overview. TopicTabId stays an\n`import type` from topic-details until the #2588 stream lands.\nutils/legacy-data-table.ts is untouched on purpose: it derives its types\nfrom the legacy DataTable because the v9 ColumnDef is the wrong shape for\nit, and deletes with the last legacy table.\n\nImporters of @redpanda-data/ui: 95 -> 89.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: paint .codeBox with theme tokens\n\n`Code` in tsx-utils and nine raw call sites render `.codeBox`, which\nhardcoded a light grey background with no text colour, so in the dark\ntheme the inherited light foreground sat on a light box and the text was\nunreadable (seen on the topic-messages \"Backend Error\" alert). Background\nand border now come from the surface and border tokens, which resolve in\nboth themes and match the registry''s inline code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: restore the segmented OptionGroup, large stat values, user-only tab changes\n\nSecond review pass on the display wrappers:\n- OptionGroup renders a segmented ToggleGroup, which is what the Chakra\n  RadioCard group looked like; radio circles were an undisclosed change.\n- Statistic uses Stat size=\"lg\" so headline numbers keep their weight and\n  size instead of dropping to body text.\n- Tabs forwards onChange only for user activation; Base UI also reports\n  its own initial/fallback selection, which the Chakra wrapper never did.\n- Overview drops a gridArea on a Section whose parent is a flex column.\n- .codeBox paints with surface-recess and border-subtle, the tokens the\n  theme documents for a code block; its dead .noPadding tint goes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnsQTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3zYQAGJJMknjHYf/E9JZZw9ZrKSp\nfT09P6/L8CNXxQ57I6fFxIgZTcEVPFuskGLJMnunMs0SsQlo2xK6FAH7r2glpLQv\nnAEVgtvH1THqbTxNR9nJP5TH8uwq5sdGZ9GHs7p422r+AsyWh5JWT30gKnRXy9X+\nDisb4y6c89nZ9PwIw8XLMqc4tpG1CG5W6Pe91YlyCnUv8l64//r+W8cBxbpGC1rC\nluZLdhNKHKrJSFVYvQWHeJw1+9Q1K0AHlUvJluoGAbAxZOB+/+j05pDHMhmIJ0/e\n10AxLD0XAOD7t9xOYloNzmOSs6y1oA6NzZZBsZF9+PVPyF5aOLafCgUyOSz/jY3T\nNoLOMcRNSBbd92IodsawLFZjgtwyaukwEhS7ZjZTuidBGcjBTEpMFp4QRbSjJFWV\nu8MUmNbSHWvbv+KY+IciKy7UHu0a3ATfUUGXM4XE0736wV30FhjUIsfqXI9pEpQa\neQSckO0k+YhTiLF0u+LFC25h7hE7zopVSwUBkgiSuwYk80+fvsah3HHZVAvEGKQR\n7cGQbxY3yrouS/P4QigY9vCkuYpdm6q2QeKbxk7KX+AWPvvjuzJxMtat8KXzcu37\nkHGOZY0iV61WeDaEMCGmoGgWqJeS5eIKB0Y1JAef9WizCVSPohrxR7z+AqGQ5k5/\n8Kl8RyTZlgVYdS2Hw3lg\n=tA9u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T14:03:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_