9","sha":"e332531dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/e332531dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09"}],"sha":"57d5bab3d64665676a0c603d6011545261ccc375","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/57d5bab3d64665676a0c603d6011545261ccc375"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/e332531dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T16:49:04Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T16:49:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): disable route-level HMR when the dev server is proxied (#2631)\n\nrouter-plugin''s route HMR shim resolves its router through the window\nglobal __TSR_ROUTER__. When Console is embedded in cloud-ui''s dev server\n(console-hmr sets PROXY_TARGET) that global is the host''s router: on\nfirst evaluation the shim sees a colliding `__root__`, rewrites the host\nroute and calls _replaceRouteChunk on a router-core that may not have it,\nso Console fails to load.\n\nKeep addHmr on for the standalone dev server and turn it off whenever\nPROXY_TARGET is set. Component edits still hot-swap through React Fast\nRefresh; only route-option edits need a page reload in the embedded case.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb10f629d3e24c96e041d1e67a23094cdc500a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/fb10f629d3e24c96e041d1e67a23094cdc500a63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/e332531dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09","verification":{"payload":"tree fb10f629d3e24c96e041d1e67a23094cdc500a63\nparent 69062ef05464bfbeebd6ca3709e6a74d3dd3bffd\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788540544 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788540544 -0600\n\nfix(frontend): disable route-level HMR when the dev server is proxied (#2631)\n\nrouter-plugin''s route HMR shim resolves its router through the window\nglobal __TSR_ROUTER__. When Console is embedded in cloud-ui''s dev server\n(console-hmr sets PROXY_TARGET) that global is the host''s router: on\nfirst evaluation the shim sees a colliding `__root__`, rewrites the host\nroute and calls _replaceRouteChunk on a router-core that may not have it,\nso Console fails to load.\n\nKeep addHmr on for the standalone dev server and turn it off whenever\nPROXY_TARGET is set. Component edits still hot-swap through React Fast\nRefresh; only route-option edits need a page reload in the embedded case.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmvaACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOvwQAJp0jCwiDVDc780PsYiRRy20\nLHAggtKD0bh79hO6OP+5FVbDQk6JUX+/I2VffLcBEFmcHCBLzZ4l8rqzlJ35WIIo\nWGI4xCG8AMMNoDNS+sQQS4Y9HsCyA20D23HAue5eN2M/HeCGCtwFj/gnD+llbkUQ\n7UZUwsixJ+Tpq+SLLntFBD8u3ynsUrnaR8nQYMjHT5Nlm0E0NLRNWP/a0AH