1dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/e332531dd37f545c7bb0c464aa4b312c9e455f09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/879913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyPete","id":879913,"login":"SpicyPete","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTkxMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyPete","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/commits/69062ef05464bfbeebd6ca3709e6a74d3dd3bffd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T15:54:22Z","email":"879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pete."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T15:54:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Chakra exit · Phase 1 · PR 2/14] frontend: move showToast onto the Registry toast, drop Chakra''s toast (#2627)\n\n* frontend: move showToast onto the Registry toast, drop Chakra''s toast\n\nChakra''s toast is gone. `showToast` in utils/toast.utils.tsx is the one\napp-level entry point, re-implemented on the Registry `toast` (Base UI)\nvendored in the registry 3.4.1 pull, plus `updateToast` / `closeToast` for\nthe loading -> result flows. The 14 files that called Chakra''s\ncreateStandaloneToast / useToast directly now go through it; only their\ntoast calls change.\n\nContract kept from the Chakra version: non-errors dismiss after 5s, errors\nstay until closed, `duration: null` is sticky, `id` + `resourceName`\ncompose the toast id. A status change on update re-applies that status''s\ndefault unless a duration is given, so an error never inherits a loading\ntoast''s timer. The id dedupe only works now: the old code created a fresh\nstandalone instance per call, so `isActive` never saw an earlier toast;\nBase UI upserts on a duplicate id.\n\n- The Registry <Toaster> mounts at the provider layer (app.tsx,\n  embedded-app.tsx, federated-providers.tsx) where Chakra''s toastOptions\n  lived, so the root error boundary and the login route can toast too.\n  index.scss lifts its viewport above Chakra''s modals (z 1400) until\n  Chakra leaves. Sonner stays the second live toast until its callers are\n  re-pointed at showToast (follow-up, not Chakra work).\n- backend-api.ts: standalone instance + redpandaTheme -> showToast, keeping\n  its 5s auto-dismiss.\n- tsx-utils StatusIndicator: showToast once, updateToast after; render()\n  returns null (no ToastContainer). The progress body is spans only\n  (Base UI renders the description as a <p>) with progressbar semantics,\n  and a closed progress toast stays closed for that search.\n- error-boundary, reassign-partitions x2, transforms x2, rp-connect x6,\n  connect x2: routed through the facade; reassign''s 2s instance default is\n  written onto each non-error call, so nothing gets faster or slower.\n  Errors there without an explicit duration now stay until closed.\n- app.tsx / embedded-app.tsx / federated-providers.tsx: toastOptions prop\n  removed from ChakraProvider (the provider itself leaves in PR 13).\n- tests/mocks/redpanda-ui.ts: toast stubs removed; facade unit tests.\n\nreassign-partitions.tsx shows ~470 changed lines; `git diff -w` shows 48.\nRemoving the <><ToastContainer/>...</> wrapper de-indented render().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: place Console''s Registry toasts top-right\n\nThe Registry toast viewport is bottom-anchored and its Toaster has no\nposition prop. Console''s toasts belong top-right, where Chakra''s and\nsonner''s were, so index.scss anchors the viewport and the stack at the\ntop with the registry''s offset math mirrored and the vertical signs\nflipped. The rules are keyed on the viewport''s console test id so they\ncannot reach a host app''s Registry toasts when embedded; the z-index\nlift above Chakra''s modals moves into the same block. Drop it once the\nregistry grows a position prop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6322b397f116913457ecf9484268aeee728a2f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/trees/6322b397f116913457ecf9484268aeee728a2f0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redpanda-data/console/git/commits/69062ef05464bfbeebd6ca3709e6a74d3dd3bffd","verification":{"payload":"tree 6322b397f116913457ecf9484268aeee728a2f0d\nparent 40ff0cb8848c7bdfa28cfd14d010884374b86298\nauthor Pete. <879913+SpicyPete@users.noreply.github.com> 1788537262 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788537262 -0700\n\n[Chakra exit · Phase 1 · PR 2/14] frontend: move showToast onto the Registry toast, drop Chakra''s toast (#2627)\n\n* frontend: move showToast onto the Registry toast, drop Chakra''s toast\n\nChakra''s toast is gone. `showToast` in utils/toast.utils.tsx is the one\napp-level entry point, re-implemented on the Registry `toast` (Base UI)\nvendored in the registry 3.4.1 pull, plus `updateToast` / `closeToast` for\nthe loading -> result flows. The 14 files that called Chakra''s\ncreateStandaloneToast / useToast directly now go through it; only their\ntoast calls change.\n\nContract kept from the Chakra version: non-errors dismiss after 5s, errors\nstay until closed, `duration: null` is sticky, `id` + `resourceName`\ncompose the toast id. A status change on update re-applies that status''s\ndefault unless a duration is given, so an error never inherits a loading\ntoast''s timer. The id dedupe only works now: the old code created a fresh\nstandalone instance per call, so `isActive` never saw an earlier toast;\nBase UI upserts on a duplicate id.\n\n- The Registry <Toaster> mounts at the provider layer (app.tsx,\n  embedded-app.tsx, federated-providers.tsx) where Chakra''s toastOptions\n  lived, so the root error boundary and the login route can toast too.\n  index.scss lifts its viewport above Chakra''s modals (z 1400) until\n  Chakra leaves. Sonner stays the second live toast until its callers are\n  re-pointed at showToast (follow-up, not Chakra work).\n- backend-api.ts: standalone instance + redpandaTheme -> showToast, keeping\n  its 5s auto-dismiss.\n- tsx-utils StatusIndicator: showToast once, updateToast after; render()\n  returns null (no ToastContainer). The progress body is spans only\n  (Base UI renders the description as a <p>) with progressbar semantics,\n  and a closed progress toast stays closed for that search.\n- error-boundary, reassign-partitions x2, transforms x2, rp-connect x6,\n  connect x2: routed through the facade; reassign''s 2s instance default is\n  written onto each non-error call, so nothing gets faster or slower.\n  Errors there without an explicit duration now stay until closed.\n- app.tsx / embedded-app.tsx / federated-providers.tsx: toastOptions prop\n  removed from ChakraProvider (the provider itself leaves in PR 13).\n- tests/mocks/redpanda-ui.ts: toast stubs removed; facade unit tests.\n\nreassign-partitions.tsx shows ~470 changed lines; `git diff -w` shows 48.\nRemoving the <><ToastContainer/>...</> wrapper de-indented render().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* frontend: place Console''s Registry toasts top-right\n\nThe Registry toast viewport is bottom-anchored and its Toaster has no\nposition prop. Console''s toasts belong top-right, where Chakra''s and\nsonner''s were, so index.scss anchors the viewport and the stack at the\ntop with the registry''s offset math mirrored and the vertical signs\nflipped. The rules are keyed on the viewport''s console test id so they\ncannot reach a host app''s Registry toasts when embedded; the z-index\nlift above Chakra''s modals moves into the same block. Drop it once the\nregistry grows a position prop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmumuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9UYQAA8HKj7+T7XGwQOsjAIVoyzi\nM4/E+bwXJW7+Q5pxd3JrVBINlV9ZdTmV3Zn9jK9XcDGrIaZxbqndoqkHo4flMIXW\n4Mqnqwdrfe9K594MVJtvTrd9t4ji9ZIAk26p3zDxaFmwbtLufeaXaWKjVJYdtfQ6\nurUVoRmNs5xecDzi9QMp0jVVOIHSAnLosfV7xGENIv1i2qe2lQEjX2dYzgMIXTmA\nMern7/QeRTIRa7p1R15eHthWYkER6b0/bu8wJLoovHw4fVdOsvv8yhOEjv/7QGG3\nV663dZLdlNuCtN6270gzNxy8+pmMTuaXjI0RDf/uHk9p2y5rSepFhtqeSmv+AyF9\nGP5dgnf3It2eF/7GnXhZ/kcQhZWHE2/jrRtiTjXl+phIFmGBRBYpSWlTpMlnWO2S\n75y+0AoEWqAHYyne+H7HBOoVxI0tAMvZoauEVOpyAs53HGxaGbjPbfPb4aFNInaw\nbLQk5ICbM69D+tSod0QpgOKA7P9P2kIVbhmoGdLKRfLSOraku9Wnnh0webYqow+H\ndFOJN8o8eHpeRvn41Kou+SsIuOxs/rFWQACC17LSe0g0I36mObeyQIHIiTwihtsS\n6iRZGuvuDxgPGIinfK8Q0/GJahpcTnyQa5GWQqkJmB6iQ4dAGEsM00Sizimv6cP2\n2Bk6HA/r4XGnZFiIiUQR\n=L+e1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T15:54:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https: