m config is also user-controlled).\nS5 RootLoginListener: skip+warn when no recipient available instead of sending\n   to an empty address; null-safe body/subject token substitution.\nR1 RootLoginListener: extract resolveRemoteAddress/resolveSite helpers; magic\n   numbers (0x20/0x7F, default site) -> named constants.\nR2 pom.xml: add JUnit4/AssertJ/Mockito test deps (parent pins surefire-junit4).\nR3 add RootLoginListenerTest (11 tests, JUnit4) covering sanitization, null\n   safety, error swallowing, and recipient skip.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb56391f6a65ffbd1efff0296d47fa6044c8d1df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/root-login-notification/git/trees/eb56391f6a65ffbd1efff0296d47fa6044c8d1df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/root-login-notification/git/commits/1039c3b76de592740d1e9d41111b1c0aa9d192cf","verification":{"payload":"tree eb56391f6a65ffbd1efff0296d47fa6044c8d1df\nparent a13eefe657460e5c82941f32b99ec1b07d62ec2f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781071491 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781071491 +0200\n\nfix: harden root login notification listener (error handling, null safety, CRLF)\n\nS1 RootLoginListener: wrap notification in try/catch + SLF4J logger so a\n   send/SMTP failure is logged and never breaks the login flow (was unguarded).\nS2 RootLoginListener: null-safety for getJahiaUser()/getAuthValveContext()/\n   getRequest() (programmatic logins); guard null mailService/config.\nS3 RootLoginListener: sanitize recipient/sender for CR/LF (sanitizeAddress) as\n   defense-in-depth — the OSGi .cfg bypasses the GraphQL email validation.\nS4 RootLoginListener: sanitize the fully-assembled subject header for CR/LF\n   (the subject template from config is also user-controlled).\nS5 RootLoginListener: skip+warn when no recipient available instead of sending\n   to an empty address; null-safe body/subject token substitution.\nR1 RootLoginListener: extract 