2dfd5d459c1715736c107d908471894f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/1f6a0f7a02be4e7deb3267ad9d8a62b2aaa162f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:21:19Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:21:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js): stop using Array.prototype.at in the error handler (#3263)\n\n* fix(analytics-js): drop Array.prototype.at use\n\ngetDirectoryName called `paths.at(-2)`. Babel transpiles syntax, not\nmethods, and `at` is not on the runtime polyfill list, so it ships as-is\nin both the modern and legacy bundles. On Chrome < 92, Firefox < 90 and\nSafari < 15.4 (about 0.2% of browsers that receive the modern build, plus\nevery legacy browser) isSDKError and getErrorCategory throw inside the\nerror handler''s own try/catch, so those SDK errors are never reported.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): resolve sonar smells\n\n- Suppress S7755 on the index access: `.at()` is the bug this PR removes.\n- Parameterize the three identical URL extraction tests (S5976).\n- Move the empty-stacktrace assertion into its own test (S8784).\n- Drop an unused `no-extend-native` disable directive.\n\n* test(analytics-js): restore at() descriptor\n\nDeleting Array.prototype.at and assigning it back made it enumerable, so for...in listed \"at\" on arrays for the rest of the suite. The helper now restores the original property descriptor, and a test pins it.","tree":{"sha":"2f1cccac0ed4857e9d669896baafbb4aeff28d21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/2f1cccac0ed4857e9d669896baafbb4aeff28d21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/1f6a0f7a02be4e7deb3267ad9d8a62b2aaa162f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f1cccac0ed4857e9d669896baafbb4aeff28d21\nparent ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790864479 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790864479 +0530\n\nfix(analytics-js): stop using Array.prototype.at in the error handler (#3263)\n\n* fix(analytics-js): drop Array.prototype.at use\n\ngetDirectoryName called `paths.at(-2)`. Babel transpiles syntax, not\nmethods, and `at` is not on the runtime polyfill list, so it ships as-is\nin both the modern and legacy bundles. On Chrome < 92, Firefox < 90 and\nSafari < 15.4 (about 0.2% of browsers that receive the modern build, plus\nevery legacy browser) isSDKError and getErrorCategory throw inside the\nerror handler''s own try/catch, so those SDK errors are never reported.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): resolve sonar smells\n\n- Suppress S7755 on the index access: `.at()` is the bug this PR removes.\n- Parameterize the three identical URL extraction tests (S5976).\n- Move the empty-stacktrace assertion into its own test (S8784).\n- Drop an unused `no-extend-native` disable directive.\n\n* test(analytics-js): restore at() descriptor\n\nDeleting Array.prototype.at and assigning it back made it enumerable, so for...in listed \"at\" on arrays for the rest of the suite. The helper now restores the original property descriptor, and a test pins it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmxfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABTgQALCP3m00qbqvtP/r97JiBvxh\n5C75jYn2P/n2DwTFe2qL9J9HQal083dDpc09y+/1L5GDu6B3/GOivVgdBADK3x/H\niwqSesTjBI+/RYn6WgP/ddepSBZae+a0ztS9bEdD4l7meNHiDtvggAFlIIuAtWqb\n6c8TVnbyUwfQxjbALvrRFJcq96GDno6jgQHpcYODntYRvJCOcQ9zqvyAJj4OfSfG\nhKsRcx738oTtg15wGiysD915VmZbQE6SxqBi48QY0ggPwn9LDoCj88G5XuG/bv5q\nKFCubc2SQr7TM45OBdD3QuhCbj19CbwQi2MXZFp2cVkYdam/B4GN9DUMBewP7fsB\nm6ZHtYCi6BZWDjKg0JH9t/Hey/m0xKQN2ayaJgvJ+7Dr7rdmw/uiqNoacx5Qot63\ndWNwPfi/TGyFNsSZ2H8AHxMqVy+MEINlfy/kqeAPE6wCKWL61rvUpGwdAaYLtweB\n/+/se1IlPrJwI0vVBeE/f5Rl7UfrHWmF3yZY1W9g6r7lIlacJuiOAkkNu955me91\nNTl0LamX72eiyygnPb9n5T1pXa06H+CW8XIZtoNykqV8ms2FTHBKAqMC/I7BJi6f\n1C3O3EzsL+93/Js4TeY5syY4aXxR0DPK412w30M59/QFFKtwIqEAzD4XB0TmNOdE\nlzBiEJlpUJEG4H5P3sdF\n=mrdA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T14:21:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/1f6a0f7a02be4e7deb3267ad9d8a62b2aaa162f7","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDFmNmEwZjdhMDJiZTRlN2RlYjMyNjdhZDlkOGE2MmIyYWFhMTYyZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe","sha":"ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe"}],"sha":"1f6a0f7a02be4e7deb3267ad9d8a62b2aaa162f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/1f6a0f7a02be4e7deb3267ad9d8a62b2aaa162f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:18:02Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:18:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js-loading-scripts): pick the modern build under strict CSP (#3262)\n\n* fix(analytics-js-loading-scripts): CSP-safe probe\n\nThe loading snippet picks the modern build only if `new Function(...)`\nparses a probe of modern syntax. A CSP without ''unsafe-eval'' (or Trusted\nTypes) rejects that call before parsing, so every browser on such pages\nloads the legacy build: ~75% more bytes and all plugins bundled.\n\nOnly a SyntaxError now means the engine is too old. Any other error\nfalls back to Promise.any and Element.prototype.replaceChildren. Their\ncombined floor (Chrome 86, Firefox 79, Safari/iOS 14) is at or above the\nprobe''s own floor (Chrome 80, Firefox 74, Safari/iOS 14 for instance\nclass fields), so the fallback never admits an engine that cannot run\nthe modern build. Requiring a DOM method as well as Promise.any keeps a\npage''s own Promise.any polyfill from flipping the decision.\n\n* test(analytics-js-loading-scripts): cover eval guards\n\nRun the blocked-eval case for both CSP (EvalError) and Trusted Types (TypeError), and add a case where Promise.any exists but replaceChildren does not.","tree":{"sha":"2e8df6204cfeb613482637b6a48c7a7e2af627c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/2e8df6204cfeb613482637b6a48c7a7e2af627c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e8df6204cfeb613482637b6a48c7a7e2af627c9\nparent 1ccc2c58701c44e5b25042267bc855326977cfde\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790864282 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790864282 +0530\n\nfix(analytics-js-loading-scripts): pick the modern build under strict CSP (#3262)\n\n* fix(analytics-js-loading-scripts): CSP-safe probe\n\nThe loading snippet picks the modern build only if `new Function(...)`\nparses a probe of modern syntax. A CSP without ''unsafe-eval'' (or Trusted\nTypes) rejects that call before parsing, so every browser on such pages\nloads the legacy build: ~75% more bytes and all plugins bundled.\n\nOnly a SyntaxError now means the engine is too old. Any other error\nfalls back to Promise.any and Element.prototype.replaceChildren. Their\ncombined floor (Chrome 86, Firefox 79, Safari/iOS 14) is at or above the\nprobe''s own floor (Chrome 80, Firefox 74, Safari/iOS 14 for instance\nclass fields), so the fallback never admits an engine that cannot run\nthe modern build. Requiring a DOM method as well as Promise.any keeps a\npage''s own Promise.any polyfill from flipping the decision.\n\n* test(analytics-js-loading-scripts): cover eval guards\n\nRun the blocked-eval case for both CSP (EvalError) and Trusted Types (TypeError), and add a case where Promise.any exists but replaceChildren does not.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmuaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASC4QABed8KIxepqE0fSdfjLizKgW\nmncpClfF1cGXXEdd4FivzDKjYwgCqOUL7Diy0QsA+6o0eE8bcBY6nix1l6eXA8IG\nE+YmldszhrLxIMLljiue/jt4YzTdop65EOajANFE4guqQ68w2xQPCwustPkeMole\na8vfsduABNhSZml78ESNxcPuoBNDE00UGP1BjiSdgYT1YDUevysAY0CI1Tcrxzkp\n5iDOiVjHCNbFqCEiS/do5sPfb40klMBBeyNSWiUb4wtfzs44PatPFwoN8ZYkb2KF\nRFiQHMrvvT1jQp1UyGaULWuGYkIrp0urI2eFOHkJD2tSVOsKSDgtK4EXfqD5m2Jx\nZiriweRcRMy7YSy04uEEV48WrzpBKvwW6gOaAuA9APWV/lB3grNdkYKdWc6YPJi/\nLatniRv0sZ5BDNVmqxqhgdDKIsu4m06YaqnTXL/CLz04CbzIUciUq247zdQVLfD0\nUQch3lVfuHNlDsPEaMtW18PYy9f2Kbz7H/ZKiNaKzhnOhlAA2P4x12sWvwTDccLm\nEY2/RK0UwUPh26QDd4SNj0YsqrOU41PfBOnZu7WlocPN1smqRKMoR7n02uF4dVd0\nbFzx3hXLDoamHSorWoT2KKmH0v5rZfuO9kKVTbQ3Eini2CaJ9Xsk2j4mFDoLdmIT\nVNt67yyEYuTEB+hFK3aD\n=BSCx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T14:18:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKGVkOTU1ODI0YjdjOTI5ZDJlYmNjN2I3ZDlhNDA2ZDJmZmQ5MGZiZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/1ccc2c58701c44e5b25042267bc855326977cfde","sha":"1ccc2c58701c44e5b25042267bc855326977cfde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/1ccc2c58701c44e5b25042267bc855326977cfde"}],"sha":"ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/ed955824b7c929d2ebcc7b7d9a406d2ffd90fbfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/1ccc2c58701c44e5b25042267bc855326977cfde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:17:18Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:17:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js): skip polyfill detection and loading in the modern build (#3265)\n\n* perf(analytics-js): skip polyfills in modern build\n\nThe loading snippet only hands the modern build to engines that parse\nclass fields, optional chaining and nullish coalescing (Chrome/Edge 80,\nFirefox 74, Safari/iOS 14). Every API on the runtime polyfill list ships\nin those engines except String.prototype.replaceAll (Chrome/Edge 85),\nwhich the core does not call. Checked against 30 days of CDN user agents,\nthe detection never fires for traffic that loads the modern build.\n\nPolyfill detection and loading now run only in the legacy build. The\nPOLYFILL_URL expression is marked pure so the modern build also drops the\ndetection list. polyfillIfRequired and polyfillURL have no effect in the\nmodern build.\n\nModern CDN core: 36.5 KB -> 35.7 KB gzip. npm modern ESM: 80.2 KB ->\n78.7 KB gzip. Legacy CDN bundle unchanged.\n\n* docs(analytics-js): correct modern polyfill comment\n\n* fix(analytics-js): mark error report promise as void\n\nClears SonarCloud S9383 on CapabilitiesManager.onError.\n\n* docs(analytics-js-common): scope polyfill options\n\npolyfillIfRequired and polyfillURL have no effect in the modern build, which no longer detects or loads polyfills.","tree":{"sha":"0af8e11890a03c9fb937351ebc9ab99252d3c6c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/0af8e11890a03c9fb937351ebc9ab99252d3c6c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/1ccc2c58701c44e5b25042267bc855326977cfde","verification":{"payload":"tree 0af8e11890a03c9fb937351ebc9ab99252d3c6c1\nparent 4f8fa5c9c59f0f321b4c476877fb51e236680bb7\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790864238 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790864238 +0530\n\nfix(analytics-js): skip polyfill detection and loading in the modern build (#3265)\n\n* perf(analytics-js): skip polyfills in modern build\n\nThe loading snippet only hands the modern build to engines that parse\nclass fields, optional chaining and nullish coalescing (Chrome/Edge 80,\nFirefox 74, Safari/iOS 14). Every API on the runtime polyfill list ships\nin those engines except String.prototype.replaceAll (Chrome/Edge 85),\nwhich the core does not call. Checked against 30 days of CDN user agents,\nthe detection never fires for traffic that loads the modern build.\n\nPolyfill detection and loading now run only in the legacy build. The\nPOLYFILL_URL expression is marked pure so the modern build also drops the\ndetection list. polyfillIfRequired and polyfillURL have no effect in the\nmodern build.\n\nModern CDN core: 36.5 KB -> 35.7 KB gzip. npm modern ESM: 80.2 KB ->\n78.7 KB gzip. Legacy CDN bundle unchanged.\n\n* docs(analytics-js): correct modern polyfill comment\n\n* fix(analytics-js): mark error report promise as void\n\nClears SonarCloud S9383 on CapabilitiesManager.onError.\n\n* docs(analytics-js-common): scope polyfill options\n\npolyfillIfRequired and polyfillURL have no effect in the modern build, which no longer detects or loads polyfills.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmtuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFwEQAIu8PFb+wyd2SyxiyNDd/KSi\nSuU/TQLjIvKH3jdjI4wz512Q1rwE85FujQ+nzcNhGYUVRS2Ty