te-browserslist-db@latest` (lockfile only;\nbaseline-browser-mapping follows). Resolved targets move with the\nnewer usage data, but IE 11 stays in the production query, so legacy\noutput remains ES5: modern CDN core is byte-identical, legacy CDN is\n0.1 KB gzip smaller.","tree":{"sha":"07448d4950e73a2f70fc3b257f876ddd47a11836","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/07448d4950e73a2f70fc3b257f876ddd47a11836"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/4f8fa5c9c59f0f321b4c476877fb51e236680bb7","verification":{"payload":"tree 07448d4950e73a2f70fc3b257f876ddd47a11836\nparent 711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790859642 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790859642 +0530\n\nchore(deps): update caniuse-lite to 1.0.30001814 (#3266)\n\ncaniuse-lite 1.0.30001790 crossed six months old, so every build now\nprints \"Browserslist: browsers data (caniuse-lite) is 6 months old\".\nThe bundle size check parses `check:size:json:ci` output as JSON and\nfails on that line, which breaks the job on every PR.\n\nUpdated with `npx update-browserslist-db@latest` (lockfile only;\nbaseline-browser-mapping follows). Resolved targets move with the\nnewer usage data, but IE 11 stays in the production query, so legacy\noutput remains ES5: modern CDN core is byte-identical, legacy CDN is\n0.1 KB gzip smaller.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvll6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJNsQAIPWNrOceecWyfEUK2P+vNzY\nyj4+eof0tgo1tK6QZEWRF8lY6wFHpToWgXsXVlrXdp47pHTMq0rYM2Q2FQ77qp/Q\n2FbVKP6xYoeqp4m7+HpZ2HOD8VkMOvVjagVAxe2+8Vvl0LwnUs1mEoWtuaCpbDpZ\n1bxdv5wAnxOwCPzPC7rGpyeJZDTkx0yQvEHDNWdmjG+KGkEUBEa6ZdiGrQy7bm0F\n2JEJLA4neb+6XdBUSVrlgHjXwdhOVouMH9OrmGiD9m8robWKSrJl2JHHrrsUsJEC\ni2aOQOf9oa9/ry5lU3d48CaKLZYbcM1fMggrf57EGQLMGgzZfUqPiscWFBnI3HGj\nryjFAGJtGQrPu0NKDCDVMqmwe/jneZs8KEZzJxd253AZZNmksPDYXC+eoIFml+QO\nKhs3Msh8jftWVcMNx28DqQ9wOo/AkEIyV0dPsGPXD8+FnTD7V8OiYA1tjRdx+6Su\ncOAKA8NDZle7nWC6oNssGAr2vsgy/TP/7JySpZemiM5FBFHjqFWE6OanlNd50Gox\nSuxCHC5vr/4g+DBnEMaLUQAixZDKiLcyTau/AQYfa+/sLLA+uoxLWU9Gt/NrCHaI\n63ORcq9HCLDS65J0Aa/VPt+gqZ33SR16Cr3HbimA+v1eB47CQJ1PftkBMaf1Gdjm\noBQ1sMfIv7iennvCln4S\n=BfkP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T13:00:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/4f8fa5c9c59f0f321b4c476877fb51e236680bb7","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDRmOGZhNWM5YzU5ZjBmMzIxYjRjNDc2ODc3ZmI1MWUyMzY2ODBiYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41","sha":"711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41"}],"sha":"4f8fa5c9c59f0f321b4c476877fb51e236680bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/4f8fa5c9c59f0f321b4c476877fb51e236680bb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:53:46Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:53:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(monorepo): deliver polyfills to every user agent (#3229)\n\n* fix(monorepo): avoid String.prototype.replaceAll\n\nreplaceAll is ES2021 and is never transpiled or bundled. Where it is missing,\ngetDestinationUserFriendlyId throws inside ConfigManager.processConfig before\nthe lifecycle reaches ''configured'', so load aborts entirely: no plugins, no\ndestinations, zero events. stackTraceParser hits it on every V8 frame, so the\nerror reporter throws while reporting, which is why these reports carry an\nempty stacktrace.\n\nFour call sites move to .replace(/ /g, ...). The eval-branch replace is also\nsplit into two passes, each with a single unambiguous pattern, so it no longer\nbacktracks super-linearly.\n\nThe same id builder is also guarded against a non-string displayName. It is\ntyped string but comes from the source config response, and production shows\n`HttpClient:: i.replaceAll is not a function` on current Chrome, which has had\nreplaceAll since 85 - so the receiver is not a string. 52 users since 3.34.0\nand still firing. A rewrite to .replace alone does not help, because .replace\nis missing on a non-string too.\n\ncompat/compat goes from warn to error and String.prototype.replaceAll comes out\nof settings.polyfills, so the class fails CI rather than depending on a\nUA-sniffing service. That promotion surfaced Object.hasOwn (ES2022) in\nanalytics-js-integrations, which no polyfill list can close - the service\nimplements it at no version - so it is exempted in lint and recorded as a known\ngap.\n\nSDK-5492\n\n* fix(monorepo): deliver polyfills to every user agent\n\nThe polyfill service decides per feature from the User-Agent alone and never\nfeature-detects, so a client whose UA claims a modern browser gets a 104 B\nbanner comment and zero executable code. UA-spoofing webviews, hardened\nbrowsers and extensions that remove an API the UA implies is present are left\nwith no polyfills at all, and nothing in the load path can tell.\n\nflags=always ships the code regardless of UA; flags=gated wraps each polyfill\nin a runtime feature detect so natives are never clobbered. Measured against\nthe live service with an Edge 122 UA: 104 B unflagged, 89,928 B flagged.\n\nBoth entry points are fixed. The snippet requests Symbol and Promise when\nPromise or globalThis is missing; unflagged it got 172 B carrying no Promise\nand still invoked rudderAnalyticsMount, so the SDK started without Promise and\ncould not reach the CapabilitiesManager URL at all. It is copied verbatim into\nexamples, sanity pages and the dev harness, so all 22 tracked copies move\ntogether.\n\nThe feature list drops requestAnimationFrame and navigator.sendBeacon - unused\nor already feature-detected with a fallback - and adds Map, which RetryQueue\nuses.\n\nTwo further load path defects. The failure path never reported anything:\nExternalSrcLoader calls back with a truthy script id alongside the error, so\n`if (!scriptId)` never fired. It is `if (!scriptId || err)` now, and the load\nstops there rather than running on an engine still missing the APIs. A timed\nout script stays in the DOM, so the load settles once and the callback global\nis dropped on failure too, by identity. Separately, nothing re-checked any\ncapability after the script ran; the post-load path now reports what is still\nmissing.\n\nanalytics-v1.1 is out of scope and keeps its unflagged URL, as do the nine v1.1\nsanity pages.\n\nSDK-5491","tree":{"sha":"9294cb68321755dd91676f5e7614d8bfd4800590","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/9294cb68321755dd91676f5e7614d8bfd4800590"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41","verification":{"payload":"tree 9294cb68321755dd91676f5e7614d8bfd4800590\nparent 0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790758426 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790758426 +0530\n\nfix(monorepo): deliver polyfills to every user agent (#3229)\n\n* fix(monorepo): avoid String.prototype.replaceAll\n\nreplaceAll is ES2021 and is never transpiled or bundled. Where it is missing,\ngetDestinationUserFriendlyId throws inside ConfigManager.processConfig before\nthe lifecycle reaches ''configured'', so load aborts entirely: no plugins, no\ndestinations, zero events. stackTraceParser hits it on every V8 frame, so the\nerror reporter throws while reporting, which is why these reports carry an\nempty stacktrace.\n\nFour call sites move to .replace(/ /g, ...). The eval-branch replace is also\nsplit into two passes, each with a single unambiguous pattern, so it no longer\nbacktracks super-linearly.\n\nThe same id builder is also guarded against a non-string displayName. It is\ntyped string but comes from the source config response, and production shows\n`HttpClient:: i.replaceAll is not a function` on current Chrome, which has had\nreplaceAll since 85 - so the receiver is not a string. 52 users since 3.34.0\nand still firing. A rewrite to .replace alone does not help, because .replace\nis missing on a non-string too.\n\ncompat/compat goes from warn to error and String.prototype.replaceAll comes out\nof settings.polyfills, so the class fails CI rather than depending on a\nUA-sniffing service. That promotion surfaced Object.hasOwn (ES2022) in\nanalytics-js-integrations, which no polyfill list can close - the service\nimplements it at no version - so it is exempted in lint and recorded as a known\ngap.\n\nSDK-5492\n\n* fix(monorepo): deliver polyfills to every user agent\n\nThe polyfill service decides per feature from the User-Agent alone and never\nfeature-detects, so a client whose UA claims a modern browser gets a 104 B\nbanner comment and zero executable code. UA-spoofing webviews, hardened\nbrowsers and extensions that remove an API the UA implies is present are left\nwith no polyfills at all, and nothing in the load path can tell.\n\nflags=always ships the code regardless of UA; flags=gated wraps each polyfill\nin a runtime feature detect so natives are never clobbered. Measured against\nthe live service with an Edge 122 UA: 104 B unflagged, 89,928 B flagged.\n\nBoth entry points are fixed. The snippet requests Symbol and Promise when\nPromise or globalThis is missing; unflagged it got 172 B carrying no Promise\nand still invoked rudderAnalyticsMount, so the SDK started without Promise and\ncould not reach the CapabilitiesManager URL at all. It is copied verbatim into\nexamples, sanity pages and the dev harness, so all 22 tracked copies move\ntogether.\n\nThe feature list drops requestAnimationFrame and navigator.sendBeacon - unused\nor already feature-detected with a fallback - and adds Map, which RetryQueue\nuses.\n\nTwo further load path defects. The failure path never reported anything:\nExternalSrcLoader calls back with a truthy script id alongside the error, so\n`if (!scriptId)` never fired. It is `if (!scriptId || err)` now, and the load\nstops there rather than running on an engine still missing the APIs. A timed\nout script stays in the DOM, so the load settles once and the callback global\nis dropped on failure too, by identity. Separately, nothing re-checked any\ncapability after the script ran; the post-load path now reports what is still\nmissing.\n\nanalytics-v1.1 is out of scope and keeps its unflagged URL, as do the nine v1.1\nsanity pages.\n\nSDK-5491","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvM4aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFFkQAEwaztcQ1CCkQ6jI0V1mYSWy\nfFWu/KP5gKd7v2VqOWIEMi/rWnw12xBuhYbgynRAKKUCOKkT0wH6jQT0fnkalwNk\nblQ+z7fqRjVTXiWA5q1YTmNiJgP+enr3r3B6odJkLT/0qv/62fTcqfS09IeP7pWd\nZH9wdy/iBzv171pq4xbrcJfcNlDlyjTuhRzfoLkkStuafuhUiyW2h7epq17kd6l+\nF7vwm+LWdk0adMp5t2x8lD1lOJCcuDE+VWoU0T4olPA0rje7ULrWZCXriYrZN2W1\n+ibjZNrLHeK357l3BZ8yzQZq6gnpHKhEiNLDByKfTwOF9nbuGVyE4VxYv7QKmAdz\nRMn/vVnDA7O1KAhcpPw9qOY3Ij7I05S5TVv2KYBsdkOY0W+oUQz5yiHBbRAsisNt\nKIbBlYek0hYE27HBXygpyjA6cmnrr7E6YXd2NneHV2MFQWlOMEn7+kDLDVl6Gjr1\ng9u9Td5hSmEg7KBHPtp6qfS2bxXiIn2+SD/bmYUnCSS8hkxLJZD8SIEJuVD5ibz9\nmywhUuhrFXG8wZhm2oLrCtgALfWhzOJTb6abK9jBnYeIEwhXCOdBBFghNHJ5JGfT\nzgd1eePYr6rjoQof0sMSwICPmAvkYGZ+zHa2fX1b31N24YA/MI9CIcti7mSbzyvl\nlKyeF1CwUmlaNyzzyhFO\n=7su2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:53:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDcxMTAzNmRmMzA4NTAzMjQzZDgwZWM1MjY0YzcwMzQ0MjNiYmJjNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59","sha":"0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59"}],"sha":"711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/711036df308503243d80ec5264c7034423bbbc41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:15:46Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:15:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js): group remote plugin failures (#3232)\n\n* fix(monorepo): lower the modern browserslist floor\n\nThe modern query was `defaults and supports es6-module-dynamic-import and not\ndead`. `defaults` is a popularity filter - `> 0.5%`, last 2 versions, Firefox\nESR - so it excluded browsers that do support dynamic import but have fallen\nbelow half a percent of global usage. The query resolves to 29 browsers where\nthe capability alone resolves to 429, dropping everything from Chrome 100 to\nChrome 120 among many others.\n\nThe loading snippet routes clients to the modern build on a feature test, not\non popularity, so those clients were handed an artifact compiled with syntax\nnewer than the test that admitted them.\n\nDropping `defaults` leaves exactly the capability the snippet tests for. It is\napplied to analytics-js as well as analytics-js-plugins, so the core bundle and\nthe plugin chunks target the same set rather than the core being compiled for a\nnarrower one than the chunks it loads.\n\nSDK-5495\n\n* fix(analytics-js): group remote plugin failures\n\nA failed remote plugin load was reported with the federation runtime''s own\nmessage, which names its local variable - \"lK.init is not a function\". The host\nbundler renames that local per build and the report grouped on the message, so\none bug arrived as 24 separate groups differing only by the identifier: lK, a,\ns, lB, t8, ur, ne, u5, u3 and more, 474 users across the first ten alone. WebKit\nphrases it differently again, appending \"(In ''a.init(l)'', ''a.init'' is\nundefined)\", which fragments it further still.\n\nThe aggregated report now carries the remote entry URL as its grouping hash. It\nis stable per release and independent of how any engine phrases the failure, so\nevery shape lands in one group. That is the same mechanism deviceModeDestinations\nalready uses for the readiness check, and it needs no regex over error messages.\n\nThe module shape is also checked before the factory is called. An intercepted\nchunk can parse as a valid module and export nothing, in which case the\nfederation runtime hands back undefined, and calling that blind was one of the\nshapes producing a minified identifier in the first place.\n\nSDK-5496","tree":{"sha":"19637e0901aa779cc387f510e8b4412559eaf0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/19637e0901aa779cc387f510e8b4412559eaf0fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59","verification":{"payload":"tree 19637e0901aa779cc387f510e8b4412559eaf0fe\nparent 96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790756146 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790756146 +0530\n\nfix(analytics-js): group remote plugin failures (#3232)\n\n* fix(monorepo): lower the modern browserslist floor\n\nThe modern query was `defaults and supports es6-module-dynamic-import and not\ndead`. `defaults` is a popularity filter - `> 0.5%`, last 2 versions, Firefox\nESR - so it excluded browsers that do support dynamic import but have fallen\nbelow half a percent of global usage. The query resolves to 29 browsers where\nthe capability alone resolves to 429, dropping everything from Chrome 100 to\nChrome 120 among many others.\n\nThe loading snippet routes clients to the modern build on a feature test, not\non popularity, so those clients were handed an artifact compiled with syntax\nnewer than the test that admitted them.\n\nDropping `defaults` leaves exactly the capability the snippet tests for. It is\napplied to analytics-js as well as analytics-js-plugins, so the core bundle and\nthe plugin chunks target the same set rather than the core being compiled for a\nnarrower one than the chunks it loads.\n\nSDK-5495\n\n* fix(analytics-js): group remote plugin failures\n\nA failed remote plugin load was reported with the federation runtime''s own\nmessage, which names its local variable - \"lK.init is not a function\". The host\nbundler renames that local per build and the report grouped on the message, so\none bug arrived as 24 separate groups differing only by the identifier: lK, a,\ns, lB, t8, ur, ne, u5, u3 and more, 474 users across the first ten alone. WebKit\nphrases it differently again, appending \"(In ''a.init(l)'', ''a.init'' is\nundefined)\", which fragments it further still.\n\nThe aggregated report now carries the remote entry URL as its grouping hash. It\nis stable per release and independent of how any engine phrases the failure, so\nevery shape lands in one group. That is the same mechanism deviceModeDestinations\nalready uses for the readiness check, and it needs no regex over error messages.\n\nThe module shape is also checked before the factory is called. An intercepted\nchunk can parse as a valid module and export nothing, in which case the\nfederation runtime hands back undefined, and calling that blind was one of the\nshapes producing a minified identifier in the first place.\n\nSDK-5496","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMUyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZPgQAEGigscd0ZKsWUQCgeU8irjB\njR+kQp6GlH2BbGQwozOStb9YqbD7q5HkXYZ1Lxh6fyzy9vk4L31Qtke2nDrXqXab\nq3JeqZfjjy82ofzEfeUeMFSvqRKyEiCM14Lbw5HJsqprQWHACB+UkPfi37XGN7Im\nQcATpzuYSIHmxsXdXQCkZD/aGTQjQekq6sjAXWPxYprow/nOfdXrre3sw8mPqrCh\ndbKAgj/pk/9Xd22IMgPxSZl9GErPDYdRAGTVxkfmmhP1kG4oEnD2Ao0vFq+zT0nr\nNNSO43eaKuTkzaP8EO/DXoeK0k9uFuoeOHO6OY+Lp+g55DIRVdCqOB5F43CyBaEL\nOB2Jzv4t495s3vEifLkQbhuInZeLDy8cWRwrvUDvoMuocYIEgAMzqAQBi4J7FoQ8\nVpMbHBjv7hPMrcshXbuWB417GQ05xl1s6wOhsT1UOFcIKeyJRkCVfV44e2nv0+/3\nfuq+okozKTeQVnFdSppNsqHxRxtObIlVNemthzv2BD29HYUGmT1aVZkt2QeReTbp\nHobbsgOlJVWGTGPU9ro27dIrEkeoELDNHU7biaZoeoOfeUihshMy6cghd9/Pfkg8\nKoXYLOs0K2fw8fKz/jwWQ87MNOShc9IN9xfrgUNp/qp2sKiByAIWWj8w5TM1sRsQ\nS2nzLOIyrXiyT53AzCxx\n=YSRl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:15:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDBkNmE4MWU3OGU2ZWY5MzhhZjVlYzA0OWVkNzBiMmM3NjZiNmRjNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880","sha":"96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880"}],"sha":"0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0d6a81e78e6ef938af5ec049ed70b2c766b6dc59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:02:22Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:02:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js-plugins): guard beacon payload (#3237)\n\n* fix(analytics-js): drop corrupt store entries\n\n`Store.get` reported a parse failure, returned null and left the unreadable\nvalue in storage. `checkReclaim` re-reads `reclaimStart` on every timer tick, so\none poisoned entry reported forever while the reclaim handshake stayed blocked\nand the donor queue''s events were never reclaimed or cleaned up.\n\nRemove the entry inside the catch so a later read is a clean miss. Nothing is\nlost - the value was already unreadable, and the removal is itself guarded since\nan engine can refuse it and a later read retries.\n\nThe removal is deliberately narrow. Only a parse failure qualifies: a retrieval\nor decryption failure leaves a value that may still be recoverable. On an\nencrypted store it also requires decryption to have changed the value, because\n`crypto` and both encryption plugins return an unrecognised format untouched, so\na missing, still-loading or other-version plugin would otherwise cost a value it\ncould still read. And `get` re-reads the entry and removes it only while it is\nunchanged. That compare is on the serialized form, since storejs deserializes on\nevery read and a reference check would never match an object or an array.\n\nWeb Storage has no conditional delete, so the re-read narrows rather than closes\nthe window in which another tab''s newer `reclaimStart` is dropped. The cost\nthere is a restarted reclaim handshake: `RetryQueue` writes queued events only\nto the store it owns, and a peer writes nothing but the reclaim markers and the\nack into someone else''s store.\n\n* fix(analytics-js-plugins): guard beacon payload\n\ngetBatchDeliveryPayload returns undefined when Blob construction throws, and the\nqueue''s size callback read `.size` off it directly behind a type cast, so the\nwhole enqueue threw instead of the batch being skipped. It is optional chained\nnow, matching the XhrQueue precedent.\n\nSDK-5499","tree":{"sha":"11974a5933b85b6afdf47c19d2c681b691c7cf01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/11974a5933b85b6afdf47c19d2c681b691c7cf01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880","verification":{"payload":"tree 11974a5933b85b6afdf47c19d2c681b691c7cf01\nparent 3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790755342 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790755342 +0530\n\nfix(analytics-js-plugins): guard beacon payload (#3237)\n\n* fix(analytics-js): drop corrupt store entries\n\n`Store.get` reported a parse failure, returned null and left the unreadable\nvalue in storage. `checkReclaim` re-reads `reclaimStart` on every timer tick, so\none poisoned entry reported forever while the reclaim handshake stayed blocked\nand the donor queue''s events were never reclaimed or cleaned up.\n\nRemove the entry inside the catch so a later read is a clean miss. Nothing is\nlost - the value was already unreadable, and the removal is itself guarded since\nan engine can refuse it and a later read retries.\n\nThe removal is deliberately narrow. Only a parse failure qualifies: a retrieval\nor decryption failure leaves a value that may still be recoverable. On an\nencrypted store it also requires decryption to have changed the value, because\n`crypto` and both encryption plugins return an unrecognised format untouched, so\na missing, still-loading or other-version plugin would otherwise cost a value it\ncould still read. And `get` re-reads the entry and removes it only while it is\nunchanged. That compare is on the serialized form, since storejs deserializes on\nevery read and a reference check would never match an object or an array.\n\nWeb Storage has no conditional delete, so the re-read narrows rather than closes\nthe window in which another tab''s newer `reclaimStart` is dropped. The cost\nthere is a restarted reclaim handshake: `RetryQueue` writes queued events only\nto the store it owns, and a peer writes nothing but the reclaim markers and the\nack into someone else''s store.\n\n* fix(analytics-js-plugins): guard beacon payload\n\ngetBatchDeliveryPayload returns undefined when Blob construction throws, and the\nqueue''s size callback read `.size` off it directly behind a type cast, so the\nwhole enqueue threw instead of the batch being skipped. It is optional chained\nnow, matching the XhrQueue precedent.\n\nSDK-5499","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMIOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj3cQAGmCFpuYIW9ht12yADwzd2wM\nxmf97L7YaeRJPpHaVjUoOlyo8uqYtZTJSLV4HGat00nDw2TY6SM+xbs1JiwzDUhc\nEbRfQstHULhetNbUGbjCAryWphzjl2nyXEuNtfo8+WUPQ4KiX+Zn6kQTBaBnykz1\n7bYFd9SU8uaRD58ALjpCBGyDFQqEIHQlGBcbKpMvTUxrKP6JSQjLnWpF+wJojMIm\nPk1HcjQEiIw0hD9ZBYZNxh7EBecbJjES6J6fZ209b0sk1vBGtXO7EVsohryvy912\nk5Kk5Ei2NnHIzFM9ikPHCc4Q6hZOUTSEt8ZRMkQXH97bdQ5Y7vfkibSgukKVknt7\nyILLEHvWjPEcrcapHwKq7mKdGgIMhO4JhZ+f5G/WaT6YmGqXF1vKJ+sLBAZVNKpY\n82UM2w3MUNgM6WtvdNfehnKyoaulUeJrDkJI4V40SZLYE98i1020RfEr1YpNoMzP\nqqWdaHhTIm/plO7vIpTM0enuqcijtKKXFJtZoG9lKf1U2Aq6QNxH6q7omQIuCK6X\nR7t+v6RQ/6r0ZLXTY7OfZbjymZYJ62T2q1PfVqctWRpNdhsFEsX0si5Trk4BxBhx\nCQ1Z4n8ISMeMwTD6RTqiiOH+zs5v5rVBqGKO93lzDchh+O+a6sdcL3alL6JYUmzE\n2Eid/aXRHUuBtVuYdx/L\n=nfEE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:02:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDk2ZGI2NTEyY2FhYTEyYTQ5NDlmNTY5OGIxMDg5N2VmMjM1OWY4ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552","sha":"3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552"}],"sha":"96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/96db6512caaa12a4949f5698b10897ef2359f880"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T07:27:10Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T07:27:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(monorepo): lower the modern browserslist floor (#3231)\n\nThe modern query was `defaults and supports es6-module-dynamic-import and not\ndead`. `defaults` is a popularity filter - `> 0.5%`, last 2 versions, Firefox\nESR - so it excluded browsers that do support dynamic import but have fallen\nbelow half a percent of global usage. The query resolves to 29 browsers where\nthe capability alone resolves to 429, dropping everything from Chrome 100 to\nChrome 120 among many others.\n\nThe loading snippet routes clients to the modern build on a feature test, not\non popularity, so those clients were handed an artifact compiled with syntax\nnewer than the test that admitted them.\n\nDropping `defaults` leaves exactly the capability the snippet tests for. It is\napplied to analytics-js as well as analytics-js-plugins, so the core bundle and\nthe plugin chunks target the same set rather than the core being compiled for a\nnarrower one than the chunks it loads.\n\nSDK-5495","tree":{"sha":"0315a3137d126ce52a61e0551b48dd32b11b6abf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/0315a3137d126ce52a61e0551b48dd32b11b6abf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552","verification":{"payload":"tree 0315a3137d126ce52a61e0551b48dd32b11b6abf\nparent bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790753230 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790753230 +0530\n\nfix(monorepo): lower the modern browserslist floor (#3231)\n\nThe modern query was `defaults and supports es6-module-dynamic-import and not\ndead`. `defaults` is a popularity filter - `> 0.5%`, last 2 versions, Firefox\nESR - so it excluded browsers that do support dynamic import but have fallen\nbelow half a percent of global usage. The query resolves to 29 browsers where\nthe capability alone resolves to 429, dropping everything from Chrome 100 to\nChrome 120 among many others.\n\nThe loading snippet routes clients to the modern build on a feature test, not\non popularity, so those clients were handed an artifact compiled with syntax\nnewer than the test that admitted them.\n\nDropping `defaults` leaves exactly the capability the snippet tests for. It is\napplied to analytics-js as well as analytics-js-plugins, so the core bundle and\nthe plugin chunks target the same set rather than the core being compiled for a\nnarrower one than the chunks it loads.\n\nSDK-5495","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvLnOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABjEQAGlldjXZaDIN4s9McyxXGQG1\nhUVPeMJR+yjURTZ5cfDjBtpYQ/bPvWtYztWNxcE5vVltTwsIcRGkqNRQB1TNWpzT\n1yjGbAzuN1AMcc60vcVIBcg7LGx7TWhOPzFHzQ/7ayV78CPI2lD76TItMH59vkwP\np6VieTWjek6HJJCaEtl3l/HxJd9mq0N0nXDkBSedM5ukunui5gBhnKlA2vPuZO8j\nRnn2jHm/qVgoxnzSkloV/r9ouDn1TPC7yFZZK1KNQjtioXBhkcvkOWwaw+0cfR/w\nD6cHoY1rjxKJfpKD0OEidMaRP62SdFUvTGG4rWUT8AK0sLo4ga+MAo4DLTOClNUK\njqhXjkxdhXKJFd+1lIB92pauI302EMOI2MP3xFbMAYXk48syKdgE2Wg7pYUZXbIA\nFoGIJhJhWpcs64xTS+XwRA9OKLNPkoYoRkxv9ysnJJOTxSB6kyOQ5ooE17Yy5Gk4\neJLPiWDlF5eoKxyGy/9p5HL91eS+ehlm/q/Q+Bs/h94KTdtHldN1ybs6qkqC9QRS\nLS1U2oKGUY/6oCVT1mst8IKpp6G3n160THeKxkmQYVP6ZQ/2F3w4NTIbdSRAUAfj\n72MY5Mu/V874/ikebnGpWBwRwgnB6OI8LP8DYhM43Mw/rgzeVnkFmcX4b+AYrUUJ\nexhEQ0nLCW23XEwq254u\n=jWy/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T07:27:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDM1NTViYjU1YjNhMmJlZDRlODE1NzM5OWUyMWFhMjRlYzY0YTc1NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71","sha":"bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71"}],"sha":"3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/3555bb55b3a2bed4e8157399e21aa24ec64a7552"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:24:20Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:24:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js): drop corrupt store entries on parse failure (#3236)\n\nfix(analytics-js): drop corrupt store entries\n\n`Store.get` reported a parse failure, returned null and left the unreadable\nvalue in storage. `checkReclaim` re-reads `reclaimStart` on every timer tick, so\none poisoned entry reported forever while the reclaim handshake stayed blocked\nand the donor queue''s events were never reclaimed or cleaned up.\n\nRemove the entry inside the catch so a later read is a clean miss. Nothing is\nlost - the value was already unreadable, and the removal is itself guarded since\nan engine can refuse it and a later read retries.\n\nThe removal is deliberately narrow. Only a parse failure qualifies: a retrieval\nor decryption failure leaves a value that may still be recoverable. On an\nencrypted store it also requires decryption to have changed the value, because\n`crypto` and both encryption plugins return an unrecognised format untouched, so\na missing, still-loading or other-version plugin would otherwise cost a value it\ncould still read. And `get` re-reads the entry and removes it only while it is\nunchanged. That compare is on the serialized form, since storejs deserializes on\nevery read and a reference check would never match an object or an array.\n\nWeb Storage has no conditional delete, so the re-read narrows rather than closes\nthe window in which another tab''s newer `reclaimStart` is dropped. The cost\nthere is a restarted reclaim handshake: `RetryQueue` writes queued events only\nto the store it owns, and a peer writes nothing but the reclaim markers and the\nack into someone else''s store.","tree":{"sha":"768704352c91d6bc627e4be3a9034c7bb8c1d2b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/768704352c91d6bc627e4be3a9034c7bb8c1d2b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71","verification":{"payload":"tree 768704352c91d6bc627e4be3a9034c7bb8c1d2b0\nparent e985e8276c240aab370d9863be661a49da749262\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790695460 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790695460 +0530\n\nfix(analytics-js): drop corrupt store entries on parse failure (#3236)\n\nfix(analytics-js): drop corrupt store entries\n\n`Store.get` reported a parse failure, returned null and left the unreadable\nvalue in storage. `checkReclaim` re-reads `reclaimStart` on every timer tick, so\none poisoned entry reported forever while the reclaim handshake stayed blocked\nand the donor queue''s events were never reclaimed or cleaned up.\n\nRemove the entry inside the catch so a later read is a clean miss. Nothing is\nlost - the value was already unreadable, and the removal is itself guarded since\nan engine can refuse it and a later read retries.\n\nThe removal is deliberately narrow. Only a parse failure qualifies: a retrieval\nor decryption failure leaves a value that may still be recoverable. On an\nencrypted store it also requires decryption to have changed the value, because\n`crypto` and both encryption plugins return an unrecognised format untouched, so\na missing, still-loading or other-version plugin would otherwise cost a value it\ncould still read. And `get` re-reads the entry and removes it only while it is\nunchanged. That compare is on the serialized form, since storejs deserializes on\nevery read and a reference check would never match an object or an array.\n\nWeb Storage has no conditional delete, so the re-read narrows rather than closes\nthe window in which another tab''s newer `reclaimStart` is dropped. The cost\nthere is a restarted reclaim handshake: `RetryQueue` writes queued events only\nto the store it owns, and a peer writes nothing but the reclaim markers and the\nack into someone else''s store.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu9gkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzxAQAHW6Cc4X5alLLcLjpEmd4HXZ\nXjJzPzhPQV8xQ5qfr+a7S/jhlRoNnSsrYcYncNtjZTs6CTEqnm0bNveWDRvdWHN7\nqEPcQ8UJeALuclkr7SSb9UfWdef6he7eLaEhbNoKGArYbGaMRIFfjMHP5yyTxpHJ\nbMoOUjBad4J+tPI3f2x8RhIkQIDSE31s1CJNxxT9UpmE+JBWS9MTnXvLIpK+A9DW\nb9aXVRShO6sIiiD2xMALm5V5K/dQhBojx8k5jPvR9Jvqwi0doak4lgTTZAGbHMZ0\nMkJhRCKk/WoX30gf+IZm5BHpJb22Fwuwpq1JqrDkl9M+19II8LnrsQUku1nzRZbG\nwGosFdLiWZ4qTh/YFJL5Kvx33DNp3fom4a/P5knJWMLc0cI4vppaUiC+3RJ623Fh\nNdID0iev5A0tpjMsDnbwfnZx89bOi72goukweZC79qf6jKOPhm6sJxC8k34pKtFW\nnYzikL2pP0S1Wby9JhAklNEWxK/S+r3Mcumhe4GdvbDk+iNukJG6oJu9RcZzi3/N\nruN7yoNaoU0ojtXOUx57WGbm0YGFT3eVjBtVqzZfQHoa4gp1riPzvm1YPU8p9LTt\n9bVmZPMFyJ/QGxbsMbXB/j/2i49DbgWwiYd6cb5rb57zLgrk5ad/fafEdcGQaVBS\nF1VmLFYMdw3RoZCMEjI2\n=DJLJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:24:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKGJhY2I1ODE2OWI4ZWY4MzkzYzJlOGViYmRjZGRhMjgzMzI0MDhmNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/e985e8276c240aab370d9863be661a49da749262","sha":"e985e8276c240aab370d9863be661a49da749262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/e985e8276c240aab370d9863be661a49da749262"}],"sha":"bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/bacb58169b8ef8393c2e8ebbdcdda28332408f71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/e985e8276c240aab370d9863be661a49da749262/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:23:00Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:23:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(monorepo): avoid String.prototype.replaceAll (#3228)\n\nreplaceAll is ES2021 and is never transpiled or bundled. Where it is missing,\ngetDestinationUserFriendlyId throws inside ConfigManager.processConfig before\nthe lifecycle reaches ''configured'', so load aborts entirely: no plugins, no\ndestinations, zero events. stackTraceParser hits it on every V8 frame, so the\nerror reporter throws while reporting, which is why these reports carry an\nempty stacktrace.\n\nFour call sites move to .replace(/ /g, ...). The eval-branch replace is also\nsplit into two passes, each with a single unambiguous pattern, so it no longer\nbacktracks super-linearly.\n\nThe same id builder is also guarded against a non-string displayName. It is\ntyped string but comes from the source config response, and production shows\n`HttpClient:: i.replaceAll is not a function` on current Chrome, which has had\nreplaceAll since 85 - so the receiver is not a string. 52 users since 3.34.0\nand still firing. A rewrite to .replace alone does not help, because .replace\nis missing on a non-string too.\n\ncompat/compat goes from warn to error and String.prototype.replaceAll comes out\nof settings.polyfills, so the class fails CI rather than depending on a\nUA-sniffing service. That promotion surfaced Object.hasOwn (ES2022) in\nanalytics-js-integrations, which no polyfill list can close - the service\nimplements it at no version - so it is exempted in lint and recorded as a known\ngap.\n\nSDK-5492","tree":{"sha":"41eb4f492ac35c98b2b244683a9eb2532bb4b990","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/41eb4f492ac35c98b2b244683a9eb2532bb4b990"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/e985e8276c240aab370d9863be661a49da749262","verification":{"payload":"tree 41eb4f492ac35c98b2b244683a9eb2532bb4b990\nparent 7b759d16caf53510d6ac0782b3827d4563ce9d88\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790688180 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790688180 +0530\n\nfix(monorepo): avoid String.prototype.replaceAll (#3228)\n\nreplaceAll is ES2021 and is never transpiled or bundled. Where it is missing,\ngetDestinationUserFriendlyId throws inside ConfigManager.processConfig before\nthe lifecycle reaches ''configured'', so load aborts entirely: no plugins, no\ndestinations, zero events. stackTraceParser hits it on every V8 frame, so the\nerror reporter throws while reporting, which is why these reports carry an\nempty stacktrace.\n\nFour call sites move to .replace(/ /g, ...). The eval-branch replace is also\nsplit into two passes, each with a single unambiguous pattern, so it no longer\nbacktracks super-linearly.\n\nThe same id builder is also guarded against a non-string displayName. It is\ntyped string but comes from the source config response, and production shows\n`HttpClient:: i.replaceAll is not a function` on current Chrome, which has had\nreplaceAll since 85 - so the receiver is not a string. 52 users since 3.34.0\nand still firing. A rewrite to .replace alone does not help, because .replace\nis missing on a non-string too.\n\ncompat/compat goes from warn to error and String.prototype.replaceAll comes out\nof settings.polyfills, so the class fails CI rather than depending on a\nUA-sniffing service. That promotion surfaced Object.hasOwn (ES2022) in\nanalytics-js-integrations, which no polyfill list can close - the service\nimplements it at no version - so it is exempted in lint and recorded as a known\ngap.\n\nSDK-5492","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu7u0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzVQQAJlk3n7CA51E/LiuwB+9v1E5\nNbL6so7w3HSLrKNm4sQa6XleMTn+8K+iO09+ogZ8vtgDdHpHmMQ03IXaM3M4U+Un\nVh3doJZxB1Vq4vjkjwLBztmrXZnZYUlpOl4COEgXM/78v0SxPbQ0I+zwY+qCxTqS\nVHhhw/PQ9yzvF1lXQlOzQ6W4WzlH71T3skjQkfyLdeyWK8AUjo7CVFuzlv7nEtVz\nKcpkoKvSL93T9htEjcyl/O7Fgf1c1H0E5/4fs5+WfGapdj7ZAuo/1YH6cJObhxDX\nOh8JekalA6+gtHtVsXWMMxaKpMHlm/z41m1PfaPrE12udYpODcDrUfMX4iRXW/Qm\n/h7jrMMR7zTEU13Az98/xVZX3N99ZXmRsKuz4QPNW8lz0Dmu0Q6eVjM2i00Z792s\ndSx7Czx/jvoQY3uzbzOEBv5szdpVTgwVPufvblmSgix0Ea4VJ09MMdlHBZbuMuUC\njfAAOESg4u7ToDGJ+HO2YGi/ONUObAftPph03sFSJOmga+puEmH4uhUsKjHsZv6u\n+1t50D44w2Vv63R8Y