ents{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0ddf4d4b9b5cfc58de151b20a16c52ffe03872e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:06:49Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:06:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): report plugin load failures once (#3225)\n\n* ci(monorepo): give every bundle limit 10% headroom (#3224)\n\nTwenty of the 56 entries sat under 1% headroom, the tightest being\nService Worker - Modern - NPM (UMD) at 4 bytes. At that margin any\nunrelated change fails the size check, and the limit gets nudged up just\npast the new size, so the bundle grows one bump at a time and the trend\nis never reviewed.\n\nRaised 47 entries to at least 10% above their measured size, rounded up\nto the next half KiB. The other 9 already had more room and are\nunchanged; no limit is lowered.\n\nThe rule is recorded in every .size-limit header and in CONTRIBUTING.md\nso the next person to hit a failure has it in front of them.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js-common): match FF module errors\n\nPLUGINS_LOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGES carried only the Chromium wording, so a\nFirefox dynamic-import failure (\"error loading dynamically imported\nmodule\") never matched and was reported as an unrecognised SDK error\nrather than filtered with the rest of the plugin load failures.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): report plugin failures once\n\nA failed federation remote entry rejects every plugin import at once, so\none incident produced one BugSnag report per plugin. Collapse the fan-out\ninto a single report naming every plugin that failed.\n\nThe report is scheduled as a task, not a microtask. The siblings resolve\nthrough several awaits of the federation runtime, so a microtask queued\nby the first rejection runs before the others have landed and the report\nwould name only that one plugin. A task drains the whole cascade first.\n\nIt also does not wait on Promise.all: a dynamic import has no timeout of\nits own, so one import that never settles would otherwise suppress the\nreport for the siblings that already failed.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): name only the remote failures\n\nThe report joined state.plugins.failedPlugins, which setActivePlugins,\nregisterLocalPlugins and register() have already written to by the time\nany remote import settles. A config with one unknown or unavailable local\nplugin plus a remote load failure produced a message blaming the local\nplugin on the remote incident.\n\nRemote failures are now collected locally and only those are named.\n\nThe log reason also falls back to String(err): the `err as Error`\nassertion only silences the compiler, so a non-Error rejection rendered\n\"- undefined\".\n\n* test(@rudderstack/analytics-js-common): cover FF import wording\n\nThe Firefox pattern went in without a test, so nothing would catch it\nbeing dropped or its wording drifting. Covers both browser wordings, a\nnon-matching message, and that both reach SCRIPT_LOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGES.\n\n* test(@rudderstack/analytics-js): type the plugin name fixtures\n\nThe fixtures were cast with `as any`, which suppressed validation of the\nplugin names themselves. Typing them as PluginName[] means a typo in a\nfixture fails rather than silently exercising a plugin that does not\nexist.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): report after every import settles\n\nReporting on the first failure named only the plugins that had rejected\nby then: a sibling rejecting from a later task arrived after the report\nand the once-guard blocked the correction.\n\nWaiting on Promise.all gives the complete list, and since each import\nalready catches its own rejection the promise never rejects, so this is\nallSettled semantics without the extra API. The once-guard, the task hop\nand the reporter closure all go away with it.\n\nAn import that never settles now means no report at all. That is the\ndeliberate side of the trade: a dynamic import has no timeout of its own,\nand holding a timer open to salvage a partial report would spend page\nresources on error reporting, which is the lowest priority thing the SDK\ndoes. The failures are still logged and still recorded in state.","tree":{"sha":"c0532600fb3afe5b87cfaf23eb7deea2bf7e8062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/c0532600fb3afe5b87cfaf23eb7deea2bf7e8062"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/0ddf4d4b9b5cfc58de151b20a16c52ffe03872e4","verification":{"payload":"tree c0532600fb3afe5b87cfaf23eb7deea2bf7e8062\nparent 179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1790053609 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790053609 +0530\n\nfix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): report plugin load failures once (#3225)\n\n* ci(monorepo): give every bundle limit 10% headroom (#3224)\n\nTwenty of the 56 entries sat under 1% headroom, the tightest being\nService Worker - Modern - NPM (UMD) at 4 bytes. At that margin any\nunrelated change fails the size check, and the limit gets nudged up just\npast the new size, so the bundle grows one bump at a time and the trend\nis never reviewed.\n\nRaised 47 entries to at least 10% above their measured size, rounded up\nto the next half KiB. The other 9 already had more room and are\nunchanged; no limit is lowered.\n\nThe rule is recorded in every .size-limit header and in CONTRIBUTING.md\nso the next person to hit a failure has it in front of them.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js-common): match FF module errors\n\nPLUGINS_LOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGES carried only the Chromium wording, so a\nFirefox dynamic-import failure (\"error loading dynamically imported\nmodule\") never matched and was reported as an unrecognised SDK error\nrather than filtered with the rest of the plugin load failures.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): report plugin failures once\n\nA failed federation remote entry rejects every plugin import at once, so\none incident produced one BugSnag report per plugin. Collapse the fan-out\ninto a single report naming every plugin that failed.\n\nThe report is scheduled as a task, not a microtask. The siblings resolve\nthrough several awaits of the federation runtime, so a microtask queued\nby the first rejection runs before the others have landed and the report\nwould name only that one plugin. A task drains the whole cascade first.\n\nIt also does not wait on Promise.all: a dynamic import has no timeout of\nits own, so one import that never settles would otherwise suppress the\nreport for the siblings that already failed.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): name only the remote failures\n\nThe report joined state.plugins.failedPlugins, which setActivePlugins,\nregisterLocalPlugins and register() have already written to by the time\nany remote import settles. A config with one unknown or unavailable local\nplugin plus a remote load failure produced a message blaming the local\nplugin on the remote incident.\n\nRemote failures are now collected locally and only those are named.\n\nThe log reason also falls back to String(err): the `err as Error`\nassertion only silences the compiler, so a non-Error rejection rendered\n\"- undefined\".\n\n* test(@rudderstack/analytics-js-common): cover FF import wording\n\nThe Firefox pattern went in without a test, so nothing would catch it\nbeing dropped or its wording drifting. Covers both browser wordings, a\nnon-matching message, and that both reach SCRIPT_LOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGES.\n\n* test(@rudderstack/analytics-js): type the plugin name fixtures\n\nThe fixtures were cast with `as any`, which suppressed validation of the\nplugin names themselves. Typing them as PluginName[] means a typo in a\nfixture fails rather than silently exercising a plugin that does not\nexist.\n\n* fix(@rudderstack/analytics-js): report after every import settles\n\nReporting on the first failure named only the plugins that had rejected\nby then: a sibling rejecting from a later task arrived after the report\nand the once-guard blocked the correction.\n\nWaiting on Promise.all gives the complete list, and since each import\nalready catches its own rejection the promise never rejects, so this is\nallSettled semantics without the extra API. The once-guard, the task hop\nand the reporter closure all go away with it.\n\nAn import that never settles now means no report at all. That is the\ndeliberate side of the trade: a dynamic import has no timeout of its own,\nand holding a timer open to salvage a partial report would spend page\nresources on error reporting, which is the lowest priority thing the SDK\ndoes. The failures are still logged and still recorded in state.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsgzpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvU0QAJ1Xw1q0ixCSXOttQCwYRxv4\n2zSvDmIxQgF8bKcUz4/8GS5NGQsvyp6IB3IrZn93GC5UL1h2U+N5kmXi++p2cAyS\nbxfp/oMbvmRqV1oz66OHAsGdzjr1YUju70xElIfBFu5r7YNCNg3D5BQ0z//f5DtQ\n9PT9JwzYY2D+VqY8pDij5vt2rpYDPiMIxl6PflhNvLi3zs3LNw2Z14/TM00WjM9x\nWZc8xNjs4QaQjZdKSqg5WN+8ekDDUS/pQ1lSu1rG2yoSGMJhQ9BzgOfszlXXkwXq\nXKgBn1GTN/W5AsXsfjJqgqiyEXvs672/gompWXZCSPyonvKz3N2KW8Wpvd09B7gH\nH14AkGAYDZmYaS8+Y42iT02Z8D4L7gGrtd+aDI2jhSswdo/yOIcAVeywzoa6+7jO\nK0AXCNXZWvP6ysOnoOToEaNUqHZFJrgwoWBw1tmirkL9dgwWek3542ardmOkjSKE\n6lmYuQ5oUOV8h8sgHBTs5sCsUQnN4sUN47pbWIVzxwU+LKQLLHI1T1sSEllllCLh\njay4bFA7cuNXscUzmKjKrmBUdU5fAcERzbewbNsi0QgNZMF+uBN4PFOP7pVKYIGS\nAfRM7lf9caRW7nx01Kq8zII4eoKXUL2McVBl3WsNifCHTENBf1BnuR0W/vM8x4yR\nVDUmkob/3/jRr8Caj/ID\n=lxWp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T05:06:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/0ddf4d4b9b5cfc58de151b20a16c52ffe03872e4","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDBkZGY0ZDRiOWI1Y2ZjNThkZTE1MWIyMGExNmM1MmZmZTAzODcyZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8","sha":"179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8"}],"sha":"0ddf4d4b9b5cfc58de151b20a16c52ffe03872e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0ddf4d4b9b5cfc58de151b20a16c52ffe03872e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:02:59Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:02:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(monorepo): give every bundle limit 10% headroom (#3224)\n\nTwenty of the 56 entries sat under 1% headroom, the tightest being\nService Worker - Modern - NPM (UMD) at 4 bytes. At that margin any\nunrelated change fails the size check, and the limit gets nudged up just\npast the new size, so the bundle grows one bump at a time and the trend\nis never reviewed.\n\nRaised 47 entries to at least 10% above their measured size, rounded up\nto the next half KiB. The other 9 already had more room and are\nunchanged; no limit is lowered.\n\nThe rule is recorded in every .size-limit header and in CONTRIBUTING.md\nso the next person to hit a failure has it in front of them.","tree":{"sha":"654059b8158f5f41bcec1186f2e921193581a6b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/654059b8158f5f41bcec1186f2e921193581a6b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 654059b8158f5f41bcec1186f2e921193581a6b3\nparent 9be2791b311777411d0cc55862ca83277d606b20\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1789992179 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789992179 +0530\n\nci(monorepo): give every bundle limit 10% headroom (#3224)\n\nTwenty of the 56 entries sat under 1% headroom, the tightest being\nService Worker - Modern - NPM (UMD) at 4 bytes. At that margin any\nunrelated change fails the size check, and the limit gets nudged up just\npast the new size, so the bundle grows one bump at a time and the trend\nis never reviewed.\n\nRaised 47 entries to at least 10% above their measured size, rounded up\nto the next half KiB. The other 9 already had more room and are\nunchanged; no limit is lowered.\n\nThe rule is recorded in every .size-limit header and in CONTRIBUTING.md\nso the next person to hit a failure has it in front of them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsRzzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFLoQAJkZSx2eOUT92KkvTAWR7r2r\ntISX3haTqlAkVOIMR2dwTg0crUlEsLjLtuvfbs5rP+z2NFldQIgTSqRXhGeQ2hDa\n2aEZ6W32o9d4nusOlHEfxJf0vEhU8xQ/eyh4bpdSrQcd36wHT68s0+HzFdS71QiL\nnRzqZ19qZj/tUCR6gu5j+AXY7DIk9Rs923v52tuviQSj66/aGmdjGiOvnunnTPM7\nU/RoARr7yGdI0yD/CjGQ8sW3XMQFGf8d5p+0fFB4Ep1zrBT8Z8xkJW794HTVungY\neu7J9f590tOnJgmcGyDBG2tcAJo+JcTOf5mMiuSkrE6ohbkpO19PjP0M98J+OxHe\nawtjMXhXj8JfUpoYxUQfRpWyHZHPsypn58ROT8H57gZ2xGdCnlRnVAChzYsChfXA\n1U2ER3iNYjlHwuZFhq5f4K7uLPelRLCqRV/n9yQWm4Et+kqcixUEO+okE1P76YC3\nTw+KG+ZS31ClPUTDvFTNUOfD34kgBMaBjKOV7BqAhUlhCmllJY93bg2kTKenDcrv\nll84bfxj9s7oK4rs+T6NNdBBknmm2yu5gFr2EArPy3sFH+w+VlEp8dxttsKoXMe2\nseIkVwj05dsFQQfORRRzSekW1XDe+ePUVWz5TKKXqb8E2eF5dfrCFHsuYgR9gP9M\nfR8bTYtfk9wzEE18BOjn\n=sjzL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T12:02:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDE3OWQ1MWUwMzUxMGIxMmNkNTMzNzBiMTZlMzdmMDdhOWM5NzM2Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/9be2791b311777411d0cc55862ca83277d606b20","sha":"9be2791b311777411d0cc55862ca83277d606b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/9be2791b311777411d0cc55862ca83277d606b20"}],"sha":"179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/179d51e03510b12cd53370b16e37f07a9c9736b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/9be2791b311777411d0cc55862ca83277d606b20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:59:16Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:59:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(monorepo): verify CDN artifacts and gate the npm publish (#3223)\n\n* ci(monorepo): verify published CDN artifacts\n\nNothing in the pipeline ever fetched a published URL, so a partial\nupload could not be detected: `aws s3 cp` exiting 0 and the invalidation\nreaching Completed were the only success signals.\n\nAdd two smoke steps that fail the deploy on any non-200:\n\n- every built plugin entry point and chunk under\n  /<version>/modern/plugins, asserted right after the pinned-prefix\n  invalidation and deliberately before the core is copied to the common\n  production path, which is the ordering the versioned-first upload was\n  written to preserve\n- /<s3_dir_path>/modern/rsa.min.js, the URL the deployment Slack message\n  advertises\n\nThe plugin check covers all *.js in the built directory rather than only\nthe rsa-plugins-remote-* chunks: a missing shared chunk breaks the remote\nplugins that import it just as effectively.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): gate npm publish on CDN deploy\n\ndeploy-prod.yml and publish-new-release.yml are triggered independently\nby the same `pull_request: closed` event, with no `needs:`, no\n`workflow_run` and no shared concurrency group. Nothing orders them.\n\nThe CDN has won every time so far, but the margin is shrinking: 5m37s on\n3.33.1, 5m43s on 3.34.0, 2m34s on 3.34.1. The npm build pins\nREMOTE_MODULES_BASE_PATH at the new version''s CDN directory, so if npm\never wins, every consumer upgrading in that window gets 403s on\n/<version>/modern/plugins/*.\n\nAdd a wait-for-cdn-deploy job that polls the production deploy run for\nthe same head SHA and blocks publish-npm-packages until its deploy job\nconcludes successfully. An unpublished npm version is recoverable; a\npublished one pointing at a missing CDN directory is not.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): never cancel in-flight prod deploy\n\n`cancel-in-progress: true` let a newer run kill an in-flight production\ndeploy mid-sequence. That is the one mechanism that can genuinely leave a\nlive core at /v3 pointing at an incomplete pinned plugin directory: the\njob uploads the versioned plugin directory before it overwrites the core,\nand no invalidation repairs a truncated upload.\n\nA queued duplicate run is strictly safer than a truncated one.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): block on sanity suite invalidation\n\nThis was the only fire-and-forget invalidation in the repo: no id\ncaptured, no wait. Every other invalidation blocks on\n`aws cloudfront wait invalidation-completed`.\n\nE2E jobs `needs:` this job in five places (deploy-prod, deploy-staging,\ndeploy-dev, deploy-beta, rollback), so they could start against the\npreviously cached suite pages and flake in ways that read as SDK bugs.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* fix(monorepo): match deploy run by merge commit sha\n\nFor a pull_request event the workflow run''s head_sha is the PR merge\ncommit, not the source branch tip, so filtering runs by\npull_request.head.sha found no deploy run and the gate timed out after\n45 minutes, skipping npm publish on every release.\n\nBoth workflows run off the same pull_request: closed event and share\ngithub.sha, so the lookup now matches.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): share the CDN artifact verification\n\nExtract the smoke checks inlined in deploy.yml into a\n.github/actions/verify-cdn-artifacts composite action and call it from\nboth deploy.yml and publish-new-release.yml.\n\nThe npm publish gate now asks whether the artifacts are on the CDN\nrather than whether the deploy-prod.yml run for a given SHA succeeded,\nwhich drops the job-name suffix matching and the merge-commit SHA\nplumbing that the run-status poll needed. It keeps a bounded retry so\nit waits for the deploy to land instead of failing on the first miss.\n\nThe action is a composite action rather than a workflow_call workflow\nbecause a reusable workflow can only be invoked at the job level, and\ndeploy.yml verifies the pinned plugin directory mid-job -- deliberately\nbefore the core is copied to the floating production path.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): verify integrations on the CDN too\n\nverify-cdn-artifacts now takes verify_core, verify_plugins and\nverify_integrations flags and reads as \"verify plugins and integrations\nfor version X\". Previously it inferred what to check from which of\nsdk_version / s3_dir_path / plugins_src / plugin_artifacts happened to\nbe non-empty, so a caller could not state its intent and a typo in a\npath silently narrowed the check. The remaining inputs are the values\nthose checks need, and each flag validates its own: verify_core needs\ns3_dir_path, the other two need sdk_version.\n\nIntegrations were never verified. deploy.yml uploads legacy and modern\njs-integrations to the versioned prefix alongside the plugins, and both\nare loaded by name at runtime, so both listings are now asserted -- on\nthe production deploy and again on the npm publish gate.\n\nEach directory''s generated listing is uploaded after the recursive\nupload of that directory returns, so it is the completion marker for\nall three prefixes. That replaces the ad hoc all_plugins.tar.gz and\nlist.html pair the publish gate spelled out by hand.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): check every artifact a listing names\n\nThe listing was standing in for the directory behind it, so the npm\npublish gate passed while a plugin entry point or a shared chunk was\nmissing -- the listing is uploaded before deploy.yml''s own per-file\ncheck runs. It is generated from `aws s3 ls` and carries an anchor per\nobject, so fetch it and verify every .js it names. That gives the\npublish gate a per-file check without a local build to enumerate, and\ncovers the integrations the same way. Source maps are skipped.\n\nverify_core now also checks the core under the versioned prefix. The\nfloating path answers 200 with the previous release whether or not this\ndeploy got that far, so on its own it could not tell the two apart. The\nversioned copy is the last object written to that prefix.\n\nplugins_src stays: the listing only reports what S3 has, so enumerating\nthe build output is still what catches an artifact that was built and\nnever uploaded.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): bound the CDN gate and the deploy group\n\ntimeout_seconds only bounded the gap between passes. A pass consulted\nthe deadline once it had finished, and each unreachable URL could hold\na curl for ~90s with retries, so a directory of missing files walked\nwell past the 45 minutes one request at a time. The deadline is now\nchecked before each request and caps that request''s own budget, with\nthe first pass still run to completion so the log names every missing\nartifact rather than whichever one ran the clock out. The gate job\ncarries timeout-minutes as the backstop for a CDN that stops answering\nrather than returning a status.\n\ndeploy-prod.yml keyed its concurrency group on github.ref, which for\nthese runs is the pull request''s merge ref and so differs per release.\nTwo release merges therefore landed in separate groups and could\npublish to /v3 at the same time -- the overlap cancel-in-progress:\nfalse was added to prevent. The group is constant now.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): require the core to be this release''s build\n\nS3 never removes what an earlier attempt left behind, so a stale or\npartial version prefix answers 200 for every URL the gate checks, and\nthe floating core answers 200 with the previous release whether or not\nthis deploy got that far. Reachability alone therefore could not tell a\nfinished deploy from a re-run over someone else''s leftovers.\n\nThe core embeds its own version as a quoted string literal, so when the\ncaller names a version the core is now checked for identity rather than\npresence -- the pattern is quote-delimited, so 3.21.10 does not satisfy\na gate waiting on 3.21.1. deploy.yml copies the core to the floating\npath only after its own per-file check has passed, so a floating core\nreporting this version is also evidence that the check passed. That is\nthe deploy''s success, read off the artifact instead of the API.\n\ndeploy.yml''s own core step names no version and is unchanged.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): add build env vars to the nx cache key\n\nnamedInputs.default inherits from sharedGlobals and lists source globs\nonly, so LOCK_DEPS_VERSION, BASE_CDN_URL and REMOTE_MODULES_BASE_PATH sat\noutside the hash. Two builds of identical source with different values for\nthem hashed the same and replayed each other''s cache entry.\n\ncheck:size:json* declares inputs [\"default\", ...], so it inherited the\nsame blind spot: a size run could replay a build made under a different\nCDN base path and report a delta that never existed.\n\n* ci(monorepo): fail on a truncated CDN listing\n\nThe listing was piped straight into the read loop from a process\nsubstitution, so curl''s exit status was invisible. A response truncated\nafter the first few links left count nonzero, the \"names no artifacts\"\nguard passed, and the action went on to verify only the files that had\narrived -- silently narrowing the check to a subset of the directory.\n\nThat is the partial upload this action exists to catch, so the listing is\nnow downloaded to a file with -f and a failed fetch is fatal.\n\nReproduced against a server that declares a long body and closes mid\nstream: the old form verified 2 of the listed files and passed.\n\n* ci(monorepo): check the floating core''s version\n\nThe post-copy core check named no version, so it only asserted\nreachability. The floating path already holds the previous release, so a\ncopy that silently failed would still answer 200, the step would pass,\nand the Slack message would announce the new version over the old\nartifact.\n\nCURRENT_VERSION_VALUE is resolved before this step and already carries\nany version suffix, so the same identity check the npm publish gate uses\napplies here too.\n\n* ci(@rudderstack/analytics-js): raise content script limit\n\nAdding the build env vars to the nx cache key made this job build for\nreal instead of replaying a cache entry keyed without them, and the true\nsize of Core (Content Script) - Modern - NPM (UMD) is 43009 bytes against\na 42 KiB limit. One byte over, and hidden on develop for as long as the\ncache has been replaying.\n\nRaised to 46.5 KiB, the same value the bundle headroom pass uses, so the\ntwo do not conflict.\n\n* ci(monorepo): make the verify deadline a real bound\n\nfirst_pass was local to wait_for_urls, which is called once per artifact\ngroup. Each call therefore got its own uncapped first pass, so with three\ngroups the configured timeout_seconds was not an upper bound on the run:\na group starting after the budget was spent still issued a full pass.\n\nScoping the flag to the run keeps the property it exists for -- the first\npass names every missing artifact rather than whichever one ran the clock\nout -- while later groups honour the deadline.\n\nSimulated with a stubbed curl against an already-spent deadline: the\nfirst call still issues its 3 requests, the second now issues 0 where it\npreviously issued 3.\n\nAddresses a Copilot review-body finding.\n\n* fix(monorepo): name the core version only for production\n\nNaming a version makes the action assert the versioned core prefix as\nwell as the floating one, but only the production path uploads\n/<version>/..., so every staging, development and beta deploy would have\ndemanded an artifact those environments never publish and failed after\nexhausting the retry window.\n\nProduction keeps the identity check on both prefixes. Elsewhere the step\nfalls back to the plain reachability check of the floating path it did\nbefore.\n\n* ci(monorepo): cap listing downloads by the deadline\n\nThe listing fetch always used the full request timeout, so a run with\nseveral listings could walk past timeout_seconds one download at a time,\nthe same way the per-URL requests could before first_pass was scoped to\nthe run.\n\nOnly applies when there is a retry budget to spend. timeout_seconds: 0\nmeans \"check once\", and the marker pass has already cleared first_pass by\nthis point, so gating on the deadline unconditionally would have failed\nevery deploy-time call before it issued a request.\n\nSimulated: timeout 0 proceeds at the full 30s, 2700 with 10s left caps to\n10s, and a passed deadline fails.\n\n* fix(monorepo): keep deploy-time verification unbounded\n\nScoping first_pass to the run made the deadline a real bound, but it also\nmeant every artifact group after the first started with first_pass=0. At\ndeploy time timeout_seconds is 0, so the deadline is already in the past\nand those groups skipped every URL unfetched and failed the job. That\nbroke production plugin and integration verification outright.\n\nBoth deadline gates now require a retry budget to exist. timeout_seconds:\n0 is documented as \"check once\", so nothing there should be skipped for\nbeing late.\n\nReproduced the break and the fix against the real function: with\ntimeout_seconds 0 the listing group went from 0 requests and a failure to\n3 requests and a pass, while timeout_seconds 2700 with a spent deadline\nstill skips and fails.\n\n* ci(monorepo): serialise rollback against the prod deploy\n\ndeploy-prod.yml and rollback.yml both copy into the production /v3 prefix\nand invalidate the same distribution, but sat in different concurrency\ngroups, so a rollback could interleave with a release deploy and leave\nthe core paired with the other run''s artifacts.\n\nBoth now share a literal production-cdn-write group. github.workflow\nwould have split them, since it differs per workflow. Rollback also stops\ncancelling in progress, for the same reason the deploy does: a truncated\nupload sequence is the one state no invalidation repairs.\n\n* fix(monorepo): gate on the SDK version, not the monorepo one\n\nrelease_version comes from the release branch name and is the monorepo\nversion -- every other consumer takes it as monorepo_release_version. The\nCDN is keyed by the analytics-js package version instead, and the two\ndiverge: release 3.122.0 publishes SDK 3.34.1.\n\nSo the gate polled /3.122.0/... while the artifacts sat under /3.34.1/...,\nfound nothing, exhausted the 45 minute window and failed. That would have\nblocked the npm publish on every release.\n\nReads the version from the checked-out package, the same file deploy.yml\nreads to decide where to upload, so the gate and the deploy cannot drift\napart. Checkout is pinned to github.sha to match the release job.","tree":{"sha":"e4ea5840b9bca1b724bcb2e16953fbaf2e5be1a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/e4ea5840b9bca1b724bcb2e16953fbaf2e5be1a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/9be2791b311777411d0cc55862ca83277d606b20","verification":{"payload":"tree e4ea5840b9bca1b724bcb2e16953fbaf2e5be1a0\nparent 039b01c89894ebf2974ef67d739aa276f6ba4631\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1789991956 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789991956 +0530\n\nci(monorepo): verify CDN artifacts and gate the npm publish (#3223)\n\n* ci(monorepo): verify published CDN artifacts\n\nNothing in the pipeline ever fetched a published URL, so a partial\nupload could not be detected: `aws s3 cp` exiting 0 and the invalidation\nreaching Completed were the only success signals.\n\nAdd two smoke steps that fail the deploy on any non-200:\n\n- every built plugin entry point and chunk under\n  /<version>/modern/plugins, asserted right after the pinned-prefix\n  invalidation and deliberately before the core is copied to the common\n  production path, which is the ordering the versioned-first upload was\n  written to preserve\n- /<s3_dir_path>/modern/rsa.min.js, the URL the deployment Slack message\n  advertises\n\nThe plugin check covers all *.js in the built directory rather than only\nthe rsa-plugins-remote-* chunks: a missing shared chunk breaks the remote\nplugins that import it just as effectively.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): gate npm publish on CDN deploy\n\ndeploy-prod.yml and publish-new-release.yml are triggered independently\nby the same `pull_request: closed` event, with no `needs:`, no\n`workflow_run` and no shared concurrency group. Nothing orders them.\n\nThe CDN has won every time so far, but the margin is shrinking: 5m37s on\n3.33.1, 5m43s on 3.34.0, 2m34s on 3.34.1. The npm build pins\nREMOTE_MODULES_BASE_PATH at the new version''s CDN directory, so if npm\never wins, every consumer upgrading in that window gets 403s on\n/<version>/modern/plugins/*.\n\nAdd a wait-for-cdn-deploy job that polls the production deploy run for\nthe same head SHA and blocks publish-npm-packages until its deploy job\nconcludes successfully. An unpublished npm version is recoverable; a\npublished one pointing at a missing CDN directory is not.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): never cancel in-flight prod deploy\n\n`cancel-in-progress: true` let a newer run kill an in-flight production\ndeploy mid-sequence. That is the one mechanism that can genuinely leave a\nlive core at /v3 pointing at an incomplete pinned plugin directory: the\njob uploads the versioned plugin directory before it overwrites the core,\nand no invalidation repairs a truncated upload.\n\nA queued duplicate run is strictly safer than a truncated one.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): block on sanity suite invalidation\n\nThis was the only fire-and-forget invalidation in the repo: no id\ncaptured, no wait. Every other invalidation blocks on\n`aws cloudfront wait invalidation-completed`.\n\nE2E jobs `needs:` this job in five places (deploy-prod, deploy-staging,\ndeploy-dev, deploy-beta, rollback), so they could start against the\npreviously cached suite pages and flake in ways that read as SDK bugs.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* fix(monorepo): match deploy run by merge commit sha\n\nFor a pull_request event the workflow run''s head_sha is the PR merge\ncommit, not the source branch tip, so filtering runs by\npull_request.head.sha found no deploy run and the gate timed out after\n45 minutes, skipping npm publish on every release.\n\nBoth workflows run off the same pull_request: closed event and share\ngithub.sha, so the lookup now matches.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): share the CDN artifact verification\n\nExtract the smoke checks inlined in deploy.yml into a\n.github/actions/verify-cdn-artifacts composite action and call it from\nboth deploy.yml and publish-new-release.yml.\n\nThe npm publish gate now asks whether the artifacts are on the CDN\nrather than whether the deploy-prod.yml run for a given SHA succeeded,\nwhich drops the job-name suffix matching and the merge-commit SHA\nplumbing that the run-status poll needed. It keeps a bounded retry so\nit waits for the deploy to land instead of failing on the first miss.\n\nThe action is a composite action rather than a workflow_call workflow\nbecause a reusable workflow can only be invoked at the job level, and\ndeploy.yml verifies the pinned plugin directory mid-job -- deliberately\nbefore the core is copied to the floating production path.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): verify integrations on the CDN too\n\nverify-cdn-artifacts now takes verify_core, verify_plugins and\nverify_integrations flags and reads as \"verify plugins and integrations\nfor version X\". Previously it inferred what to check from which of\nsdk_version / s3_dir_path / plugins_src / plugin_artifacts happened to\nbe non-empty, so a caller could not state its intent and a typo in a\npath silently narrowed the check. The remaining inputs are the values\nthose checks need, and each flag validates its own: verify_core needs\ns3_dir_path, the other two need sdk_version.\n\nIntegrations were never verified. deploy.yml uploads legacy and modern\njs-integrations to the versioned prefix alongside the plugins, and both\nare loaded by name at runtime, so both listings are now asserted -- on\nthe production deploy and again on the npm publish gate.\n\nEach directory''s generated listing is uploaded after the recursive\nupload of that directory returns, so it is the completion marker for\nall three prefixes. That replaces the ad hoc all_plugins.tar.gz and\nlist.html pair the publish gate spelled out by hand.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): check every artifact a listing names\n\nThe listing was standing in for the directory behind it, so the npm\npublish gate passed while a plugin entry point or a shared chunk was\nmissing -- the listing is uploaded before deploy.yml''s own per-file\ncheck runs. It is generated from `aws s3 ls` and carries an anchor per\nobject, so fetch it and verify every .js it names. That gives the\npublish gate a per-file check without a local build to enumerate, and\ncovers the integrations the same way. Source maps are skipped.\n\nverify_core now also checks the core under the versioned prefix. The\nfloating path answers 200 with the previous release whether or not this\ndeploy got that far, so on its own it could not tell the two apart. The\nversioned copy is the last object written to that prefix.\n\nplugins_src stays: the listing only reports what S3 has, so enumerating\nthe build output is still what catches an artifact that was built and\nnever uploaded.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): bound the CDN gate and the deploy group\n\ntimeout_seconds only bounded the gap between passes. A pass consulted\nthe deadline once it had finished, and each unreachable URL could hold\na curl for ~90s with retries, so a directory of missing files walked\nwell past the 45 minutes one request at a time. The deadline is now\nchecked before each request and caps that request''s own budget, with\nthe first pass still run to completion so the log names every missing\nartifact rather than whichever one ran the clock out. The gate job\ncarries timeout-minutes as the backstop for a CDN that stops answering\nrather than returning a status.\n\ndeploy-prod.yml keyed its concurrency group on github.ref, which for\nthese runs is the pull request''s merge ref and so differs per release.\nTwo release merges therefore landed in separate groups and could\npublish to /v3 at the same time -- the overlap cancel-in-progress:\nfalse was added to prevent. The group is constant now.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): require the core to be this release''s build\n\nS3 never removes what an earlier attempt left behind, so a stale or\npartial version prefix answers 200 for every URL the gate checks, and\nthe floating core answers 200 with the previous release whether or not\nthis deploy got that far. Reachability alone therefore could not tell a\nfinished deploy from a re-run over someone else''s leftovers.\n\nThe core embeds its own version as a quoted string literal, so when the\ncaller names a version the core is now checked for identity rather than\npresence -- the pattern is quote-delimited, so 3.21.10 does not satisfy\na gate waiting on 3.21.1. deploy.yml copies the core to the floating\npath only after its own per-file check has passed, so a floating core\nreporting this version is also evidence that the check passed. That is\nthe deploy''s success, read off the artifact instead of the API.\n\ndeploy.yml''s own core step names no version and is unchanged.\n\nRef: SDK-5488\n\n* ci(monorepo): add build env vars to the nx cache key\n\nnamedInputs.default inherits from sharedGlobals and lists source globs\nonly, so LOCK_DEPS_VERSION, BASE_CDN_URL and REMOTE_MODULES_BASE_PATH sat\noutside the hash. Two builds of identical source with different values for\nthem hashed the same and replayed each other''s cache entry.\n\ncheck:size:json* declares inputs [\"default\", ...], so it inherited the\nsame blind spot: a size run could replay a build made under a different\nCDN base path and report a delta that never existed.\n\n* ci(monorepo): fail on a truncated CDN listing\n\nThe listing was piped straight into the read loop from a process\nsubstitution, so curl''s exit status was invisible. A response truncated\nafter the first few links left count nonzero, the \"names no artifacts\"\nguard passed, and the action went on to verify only the files that had\narrived -- silently narrowing the check to a subset of the directory.\n\nThat is the partial upload this action exists to catch, so the listing is\nnow downloaded to a file with -f and a failed fetch is fatal.\n\nReproduced against a server that declares a long body and closes mid\nstream: the old form verified 2 of the listed files and passed.\n\n* ci(monorepo): check the floating core''s version\n\nThe post-copy core check named no version, so it only asserted\nreachability. The floating path already holds the previous release, so a\ncopy that silently failed would still answer 200, the step would pass,\nand the Slack message would announce the new version over the old\nartifact.\n\nCURRENT_VERSION_VALUE is resolved before this step and already carries\nany version suffix, so the same identity check the npm publish gate uses\napplies here too.\n\n* ci(@rudderstack/analytics-js): raise content script limit\n\nAdding the build env vars to the nx cache key made this job build for\nreal instead of replaying a cache entry keyed without them, and the true\nsize of Core (Content Script) - Modern - NPM (UMD) is 43009 bytes against\na 42 KiB limit. One byte over, and hidden on develop for as long as the\ncache has been replaying.\n\nRaised to 46.5 KiB, the same value the bundle headroom pass uses, so the\ntwo do not conflict.\n\n* ci(monorepo): make the verify deadline a real bound\n\nfirst_pass was local to wait_for_urls, which is called once per artifact\ngroup. Each call therefore got its own uncapped first pass, so with three\ngroups the configured timeout_seconds was not an upper bound on the run:\na group starting after the budget was spent still issued a full pass.\n\nScoping the flag to the run keeps the property it exists for -- the first\npass names every missing artifact rather than whichever one ran the clock\nout -- while later groups honour the deadline.\n\nSimulated with a stubbed curl against an already-spent deadline: the\nfirst call still issues its 3 requests, the second now issues 0 where it\npreviously issued 3.\n\nAddresses a Copilot review-body finding.\n\n* fix(monorepo): name the core version only for production\n\nNaming a version makes the action assert the versioned core prefix as\nwell as the floating one, but only the production path uploads\n/<version>/..., so every staging, development and beta deploy would have\ndemanded an artifact those environments never publish and failed after\nexhausting the retry window.\n\nProduction keeps the identity check on both prefixes. Elsewhere the step\nfalls back to the plain reachability check of the floating path it did\nbefore.\n\n* ci(monorepo): cap listing downloads by the deadline\n\nThe listing fetch always used the full request timeout, so a run with\nseveral listings could walk past timeout_seconds one download at a time,\nthe same way the per-URL requests could before first_pass was scoped to\nthe run.\n\nOnly applies when there is a retry budget to spend. timeout_seconds: 0\nmeans \"check once\", and the marker pass has already cleared first_pass by\nthis point, so gating on the deadline unconditionally would have failed\nevery deploy-time call before it issued a request.\n\nSimulated: timeout 0 proceeds at the full 30s, 2700 with 10s left caps to\n10s, and a passed deadline fails.\n\n* fix(monorepo): keep deploy-time verification unbounded\n\nScoping first_pass to the run made the deadline a real bound, but it also\nmeant every artifact group after the first started with first_pass=0. At\ndeploy time timeout_seconds is 0, so the deadline is already in the past\nand those groups skipped every URL unfetched and failed the job. That\nbroke production plugin and integration verification outright.\n\nBoth deadline gates now require a retry budget to exist. timeout_seconds:\n0 is documented as \"check once\", so nothing there should be skipped for\nbeing late.\n\nReproduced the break and the fix against the real function: with\ntimeout_seconds 0 the listing group went from 0 requests and a failure to\n3 requests and a pass, while timeout_seconds 2700 with a spent deadline\nstill skips and fails.\n\n* ci(monorepo): serialise rollback against the prod deploy\n\ndeploy-prod.yml and rollback.yml both copy into the production /v3 prefix\nand invalidate the same distribution, but sat in different concurrency\ngroups, so a rollback could interleave with a release deploy and leave\nthe core paired with the other run''s artifacts.\n\nBoth now share a literal production-cdn-write group. github.workflow\nwould have split them, since it differs per workflow. Rollback also stops\ncancelling in progress, for the same reason the deploy does: a truncated\nupload sequence is the one state no invalidation repairs.\n\n* fix(monorepo): gate on the SDK version, not the monorepo one\n\nrelease_version comes from the release branch name and is the monorepo\nversion -- every other consumer takes it as monorepo_release_version. The\nCDN is keyed by the analytics-js package version instead, and the two\ndiverge: release 3.122.0 publishes SDK 3.34.1.\n\nSo the gate polled /3.122.0/... while the artifacts sat under /3.34.1/...,\nfound nothing, exhausted the 45 minute window and failed. That would have\nblocked the npm publish on every release.\n\nReads the version from the checked-out package, the same file deploy.yml\nreads to decide where to upload, so the gate and the deploy cannot drift\napart. Checkout is pinned to github.sha to match the release job.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsRwUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATxAQAHodf+sUCTVmcJxaiYl3RCay\ny8bF5rJQlqCBjcxg3X3Z51PRLGePTEbYwihkfiZrHx+hf9/YVqPC6ipQgLtA+jFQ\nEzi0YdUYWr1g+oVw6KVy6SG8olkPx+QS/llwEYnoM2UoEZDh0xMtRNZHqzlGNEn/\norWWq5Z6Uq66Pp7GXo4ecxPUY9tF5iL7LMd2reZlkvTshfCSlmDTEM7E0dYpM6lL\nuZ+lBUjhiU+JMvOtCKR5rYXzaWyFpKwXnSJ1m9KS7LkyT+ps6oWMDlZG8au1cCWj\nub2W3uwNGWA0J6q/2knqjco4Tow0LC6kjpHY+ZpAPjZTOHtoeqcwgpnJaiv5Hhln\ngREmf2IQWSCQMqOXB/Jvk6/PWFiBC+UlWz3IRmVDgX4msg4TW4lYbopNc98mD/OQ\nbfBH9/OzPo47DSKPq50Yb9CDanjN4w8q2cHDJvcuqp80NvSQx02VTO6SsWY+ePyN\n0c0TV/NHkknCB1frI5m4MYbSw/t4vKgSnfnYZEMx5XOjqWbMV0Ad0VGvu1Ie4oDy\nQxU+iqCCoDNaGyByiRqvUvDki/uLyfnWY4cug9L4jUSHj6rz2HckWMSPoMKOEKMO\ngXs5zbKJJ/JSoh258yjMCen0vL1O2DmcKOlcxRlrZyJMD0zcmlKJPF2IpwyU5mVj\nhHl3Q00L+7p7tW5sMOtK\n=/Uwj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T11:59:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuse