":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/756d922f45f985340d271836f1ed276f6d86881c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:10:02Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:10:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(analytics-js): accept an absolute dataServiceEndpoint (#3206)\n\n* feat(analytics-js): accept an absolute dataServiceEndpoint for server-side cookies\n\nThe rsaRequest host was derived from the cookie domain, so a request on the\ncurrent origin with cookies scoped to the parent domain was unreachable. An\nabsolute `dataServiceEndpoint` now states the host explicitly.\n\n- Use an absolute `dataServiceEndpoint` as the final request URL as it is\n- Reject a data service host outside the webpage''s domain, since it can only\n  set cookies that the webpage will never be able to read\n- Derive the default host from the browser-verified top domain, which fixes\n  compound TLDs (shop.example.co.uk resolved to the public suffix co.uk)\n\nEvery currently supported combination of setCookieDomain and\nsameDomainCookiesOnly behaves exactly as before.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): keep the webpage port in the derived data service URL\n\nThe cookie domain probe reports a hostname without the port, while the string\nparsing it replaced carried the port along. Pages served on a custom port were\nlosing it from the rsaRequest URL.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): tighten the data service host check for server-side cookies\n\nAddresses review feedback on #3206.\n\n- Require the exact webpage host when sameDomainCookiesOnly is set, since\n  CookieStorage drops the cookie domain in that mode and a host-only cookie\n  set by a sibling host is unreadable by the webpage\n- Keep the client-side fallback cookie options intact when the host check\n  disables the feature, instead of leaving SameSite=None and Secure on a\n  cookie that document.cookie will then reject on an HTTP page\n- Extract the host check into isWebpageDataServiceHost with its own coverage\n- Report the rejection as an error and say the cookies fall back to\n  client-side instead of server-side\n- Read the location through globalThis, and space out the test blocks\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): apply cookie options last\n\nThe cookie domain guard disables server-side cookies after the cross-site\nbranch has already forced SameSite=None and Secure, so the client-side\nfallback inherited options that document.cookie rejects on an HTTP page.\nMoving the mutation below both checks lets the sscEnabled guard cover them.\n\nRaises the modern UMD core limit by half a KiB to fit the host check.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): reject unreadable cookie domains\n\nAn absolute endpoint could satisfy the existing cookie domain guard by\npointing at the configured domain itself, so `setCookieDomain` and the\nendpoint host both set to a sibling subdomain enabled the feature while\nCookieStorage scoped the cookies where the webpage could never read them.\nThe page-origin endpoint used to rule that combination out on its own.\n\nServer-side cookies now also require the webpage to fall under the\nconfigured cookie domain.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): fold cookie domain checks\n\nAddresses review feedback and the SonarCloud findings on #3206.\n\n- Collapse the two overlapping cookie domain guards into one that asks\n  whether the data service can set the domain and the webpage can read it,\n  replacing the exact host equality that an absolute endpoint made too narrow\n- Report the cookie domain rejection as an error, matching the host rejection\n- Extract getWebpageTopDomain and isServerSideCookiesUsable, which brings\n  getServerSideCookiesStateData back under the cognitive complexity limit\n- Skip the cookie domain check once the feature is already disabled\n- Prefer Array.at() over length arithmetic in getTopDomain\n\nRaises the modern ESM core limit by half a KiB, matching its siblings.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): keep getTopDomain off Array.at\n\nArray.prototype.at is absent from the IE11 production target and from the\nlegacy polyfill capability list, and getTopDomain runs during server-side\ncookie configuration, so the legacy bundle could throw before the SDK\nfinished loading. slice(-2).join(''.'') reads the same without the index\narithmetic that prompted the change.\n\nAlso canonicalises a configured cookie domain before matching it, since\nhostnames arrive lowercased and setCookieDomain does not.\n\nRaises the bundled modern CJS limit by half a KiB, matching its siblings.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): reject public suffix domains\n\nA cookie domain above the webpage''s registrable domain, ex: ''co.uk'' on\nshop.example.co.uk, satisfied both suffix checks while the browser refuses\nto scope cookies to it. The feature stayed enabled and every cookie was\ndropped with nothing in the console to say why.\n\nThe configured domain now also has to sit at or below the browser-verified\ndomain of the webpage.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): guard data service URL parsing\n\nisValidURL falls back to a regex check when globalThis.URL is missing,\nso on a legacy JS engine with polyfills disabled the unguarded\nnew URL(dataServiceUrl) threw out of the config initialisation instead\nof disabling server-side cookies. Parse the hostname through a\ntry/catch helper, mirroring getDomain, and treat an unparsable URL the\nsame as an invalid one.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): guard the top domain parsing\n\ngetTopDomain called new URL unconditionally, so on legacy JS engines the\npolyfills had not loaded yet and the reference threw. isWebpageTopLevelDomain\nruns it before any other URL parsing, hence providing setCookieDomain or\nstorage.cookie.domain alongside useServerSideCookies aborted config init\naltogether instead of falling back to client-side cookies.\n\nFall back to the anchor element parser the top-domain module already uses for\nthe same reason.\n\nRef: SDK-5464\n\n* fix(analytics-js): log an invalid data service URL\n\nA dataServiceEndpoint that does not parse disabled server-side cookies\nsilently, leaving a typo in an absolute URL indistinguishable from the\nfeature being switched off. Report it through DATA_SERVER_URL_INVALID_ERROR,\nwhich already carried this exact message but had no caller.\n\nRef: SDK-5464\n\n* fix(analytics-js): ignore the data service port\n\nThe cross-site check compared getDomain values, which carry the port, so an\nabsolute dataServiceEndpoint on the webpage''s own hostname at another port\nwas read as cross-site and forced SameSite=None with Secure. On an HTTP page\nthat Secure attribute leaves the cookie unstorable.\n\nCookies are not isolated by port, hence compare the hostnames that are\nalready resolved for the data service host check.\n\nRef: SDK-5464","tree":{"sha":"c42654b6d821b92d97ca48abfb3a0e038a96b148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/c42654b6d821b92d97ca48abfb3a0e038a96b148"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/756d922f45f985340d271836f1ed276f6d86881c","verification":{"payload":"tree c42654b6d821b92d97ca48abfb3a0e038a96b148\nparent a680c717cc5be711a5561a81d82d28c4971443ec\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1789481402 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789481402 +0530\n\nfeat(analytics-js): accept an absolute dataServiceEndpoint (#3206)\n\n* feat(analytics-js): accept an absolute dataServiceEndpoint for server-side cookies\n\nThe rsaRequest host was derived from the cookie domain, so a request on the\ncurrent origin with cookies scoped to the parent domain was unreachable. An\nabsolute `dataServiceEndpoint` now states the host explicitly.\n\n- Use an absolute `dataServiceEndpoint` as the final request URL as it is\n- Reject a data service host outside the webpage''s domain, since it can only\n  set cookies that the webpage will never be able to read\n- Derive the default host from the browser-verified top domain, which fixes\n  compound TLDs (shop.example.co.uk resolved to the public suffix co.uk)\n\nEvery currently supported combination of setCookieDomain and\nsameDomainCookiesOnly behaves exactly as before.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): keep the webpage port in the derived data service URL\n\nThe cookie domain probe reports a hostname without the port, while the string\nparsing it replaced carried the port along. Pages served on a custom port were\nlosing it from the rsaRequest URL.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): tighten the data service host check for server-side cookies\n\nAddresses review feedback on #3206.\n\n- Require the exact webpage host when sameDomainCookiesOnly is set, since\n  CookieStorage drops the cookie domain in that mode and a host-only cookie\n  set by a sibling host is unreadable by the webpage\n- Keep the client-side fallback cookie options intact when the host check\n  disables the feature, instead of leaving SameSite=None and Secure on a\n  cookie that document.cookie will then reject on an HTTP page\n- Extract the host check into isWebpageDataServiceHost with its own coverage\n- Report the rejection as an error and say the cookies fall back to\n  client-side instead of server-side\n- Read the location through globalThis, and space out the test blocks\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): apply cookie options last\n\nThe cookie domain guard disables server-side cookies after the cross-site\nbranch has already forced SameSite=None and Secure, so the client-side\nfallback inherited options that document.cookie rejects on an HTTP page.\nMoving the mutation below both checks lets the sscEnabled guard cover them.\n\nRaises the modern UMD core limit by half a KiB to fit the host check.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): reject unreadable cookie domains\n\nAn absolute endpoint could satisfy the existing cookie domain guard by\npointing at the configured domain itself, so `setCookieDomain` and the\nendpoint host both set to a sibling subdomain enabled the feature while\nCookieStorage scoped the cookies where the webpage could never read them.\nThe page-origin endpoint used to rule that combination out on its own.\n\nServer-side cookies now also require the webpage to fall under the\nconfigured cookie domain.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): fold cookie domain checks\n\nAddresses review feedback and the SonarCloud findings on #3206.\n\n- Collapse the two overlapping cookie domain guards into one that asks\n  whether the data service can set the domain and the webpage can read it,\n  replacing the exact host equality that an absolute endpoint made too narrow\n- Report the cookie domain rejection as an error, matching the host rejection\n- Extract getWebpageTopDomain and isServerSideCookiesUsable, which brings\n  getServerSideCookiesStateData back under the cognitive complexity limit\n- Skip the cookie domain check once the feature is already disabled\n- Prefer Array.at() over length arithmetic in getTopDomain\n\nRaises the modern ESM core limit by half a KiB, matching its siblings.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): keep getTopDomain off Array.at\n\nArray.prototype.at is absent from the IE11 production target and from the\nlegacy polyfill capability list, and getTopDomain runs during server-side\ncookie configuration, so the legacy bundle could throw before the SDK\nfinished loading. slice(-2).join(''.'') reads the same without the index\narithmetic that prompted the change.\n\nAlso canonicalises a configured cookie domain before matching it, since\nhostnames arrive lowercased and setCookieDomain does not.\n\nRaises the bundled modern CJS limit by half a KiB, matching its siblings.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): reject public suffix domains\n\nA cookie domain above the webpage''s registrable domain, ex: ''co.uk'' on\nshop.example.co.uk, satisfied both suffix checks while the browser refuses\nto scope cookies to it. The feature stayed enabled and every cookie was\ndropped with nothing in the console to say why.\n\nThe configured domain now also has to sit at or below the browser-verified\ndomain of the webpage.\n\nSDK-5464\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): guard data service URL parsing\n\nisValidURL falls back to a regex check when globalThis.URL is missing,\nso on a legacy JS engine with polyfills disabled the unguarded\nnew URL(dataServiceUrl) threw out of the config initialisation instead\nof disabling server-side cookies. Parse the hostname through a\ntry/catch helper, mirroring getDomain, and treat an unparsable URL the\nsame as an invalid one.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wfDLKmKCDQqoSMMEwY4Rq\n\n* fix(analytics-js): guard the top domain parsing\n\ngetTopDomain called new URL unconditionally, so on legacy JS engines the\npolyfills had not loaded yet and the reference threw. isWebpageTopLevelDomain\nruns it before any other URL parsing, hence providing setCookieDomain or\nstorage.cookie.domain alongside useServerSideCookies aborted config init\naltogether instead of falling back to client-side cookies.\n\nFall back to the anchor element parser the top-domain module already uses for\nthe same reason.\n\nRef: SDK-5464\n\n* fix(analytics-js): log an invalid data service URL\n\nA dataServiceEndpoint that does not parse disabled server-side cookies\nsilently, leaving a typo in an absolute URL indistinguishable from the\nfeature being switched off. Report it through DATA_SERVER_URL_INVALID_ERROR,\nwhich already carried this exact message but had no caller.\n\nRef: SDK-5464\n\n* fix(analytics-js): ignore the data service port\n\nThe cross-site check compared getDomain values, which carry the port, so an\nabsolute dataServiceEndpoint on the webpage''s own hostname at another port\nwas read as cross-site and forced SameSite=None with Secure. On an HTTP page\nthat Secure attribute leaves the cookie unstorable.\n\nCookies are not isolated by port, hence compare the hostnames that are\nalready resolved for the data service host check.\n\nRef: SDK-5464","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqVG6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxxAQAENX98M1ld1g8MP5uLaFI+L2\nQ3NSnI+3rOUDaX3emcjyVfW1COr5nBKWVwOnIJhMoC7BDCp0WDi9n8S3I3QJ+3oo\nuPedcQ8mDJ1hdmyLHSGmAVQy0VQlWmhuYtGHBVqYFrGEs/ywz4yv2/PfOOzTYB8O\nIbKj3ub0MWhSHe/G4hwlcxdTZkZLHnMvr+bVIfCDEMuvGBqRNXJhYgq9SXHekOk8\nTDrqvGhIgRQZ7Sis+zlI7F4yTGTTWMZwEk4eiYRY20QvQ4IBd3t6DqqjWxnox5pF\nNyBxd89cMcWOfhLBs1CcDVkoA0c9rFmoD/VXmaPetB9bcb4A+W88ki/Kiqudb400\nT/pwG8QNLUqS4/AC11Bi+f5OLITVlgL3T/elRcD4SMl3Jo65YCCPmId/mAee3Hw6\nz1MC+TnoqSdA3tQ/4d6zm1UHqI7DTqExebNKrDgBUCujOuN9+lWujHQjKly8u0zb\nitK6ZJV9NamFzIWb0aGQ1hp0V8Ondh3Z7p5RcBOwpq3iuVDHyCO3Oi1hY/SxoT/I\nm5Fh056oWFpItwxpc9F/I12UaCg2g4DBgobpv9eLPWzR6e0HQYrHPQTlDdIU78VB\neLhDuJWyrRNyYUnbzGl77nv+wWyGTLlW7GYdDbD0vnkdPNAosfVci7H8nRh6Matw\nvhEd2QBbTf/KulbARUKY\n=2/kr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:10:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_