m/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/651e97875083b189dbe46a5dca8ff3f389a3db5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:13:36Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:13:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(release): suffix and deprecate betas for all packages (#3192)\n\n* fix(release): suffix every publishable version\n\nThe step only appended the version suffix to analytics-js and analytics-v1.1,\nso analytics-js-service-worker and analytics-js-cookies kept their released\nversions. When either of them lands in the affected set, nx skips publishing\nthem because the version already exists on the registry and runs\n`npm dist-tag add` instead. That fails, nx bails, and analytics-js is never\npublished either, so the whole beta deploy produces nothing.\n\nThe list is now derived from the `private` flag, mirroring the filter that\ndetermines affected publishable projects, so a new package cannot be missed.\nThe step is gated on `version_suffix != ''''`, so production deploys are\nunaffected.\n\nFixes SDK-5452.\n\n* fix(release): deprecate betas for every package\n\nNow that beta deploys publish every publishable package, the deprecation run\nhas to cover them all. The hardcoded list was missing rudder-sdk-js, whose\nbeta versions have never been deprecated.\n\nDerived from the same `private` flag as the versioning step so the two lists\ncannot drift apart again.\n\n* fix(release): harden package version derivation\n\nAddresses the review round on #3192:\n\n- Pass the new version to jq with --arg instead of interpolating it into the\n  jq program. version_suffix is a workflow_dispatch input, so a value with a\n  quote or backslash could corrupt the program or inject into it.\n- Skip an unmatched glob and manifests without a name, in both the versioning\n  loop and the affected-project filter, so the two stay aligned.\n- Anchor the deprecation script''s package lookup to its own location. Deriving\n  the list from a relative glob made it depend on the caller''s directory, which\n  the previous hardcoded list did not.","tree":{"sha":"4af2c70af2b7db6e302494bcc6b4705e69b3c842","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/4af2c70af2b7db6e302494bcc6b4705e69b3c842"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/651e97875083b189dbe46a5dca8ff3f389a3db5b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4af2c70af2b7db6e302494bcc6b4705e69b3c842\nparent 0d92edb85c94e55a454aedfd97f66b79eab8bfc2\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1788876816 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788876816 +0530\n\nfix(release): suffix and deprecate betas for all packages (#3192)\n\n* fix(release): suffix every publishable version\n\nThe step only appended the version suffix to analytics-js and analytics-v1.1,\nso analytics-js-service-worker and analytics-js-cookies kept their released\nversions. When either of them lands in the affected set, nx skips publishing\nthem because the version already exists on the registry and runs\n`npm dist-tag add` instead. That fails, nx bails, and analytics-js is never\npublished either, so the whole beta deploy produces nothing.\n\nThe list is now derived from the `private` flag, mirroring the filter that\ndetermines affected publishable projects, so a new package cannot be missed.\nThe step is gated on `version_suffix != ''''`, so production deploys are\nunaffected.\n\nFixes SDK-5452.\n\n* fix(release): deprecate betas for every package\n\nNow that beta deploys publish every publishable package, the deprecation run\nhas to cover them all. The hardcoded list was missing rudder-sdk-js, whose\nbeta versions have never been deprecated.\n\nDerived from the same `private` flag as the versioning step so the two lists\ncannot drift apart again.\n\n* fix(release): harden package version derivation\n\nAddresses the review round on #3192:\n\n- Pass the new version to jq with --arg instead of interpolating it into the\n  jq program. version_suffix is a workflow_dispatch input, so a value with a\n  quote or backslash could corrupt the program or inject into it.\n- Skip an unmatched glob and manifests without a name, in both the versioning\n  loop and the affected-project filter, so the two stay aligned.\n- Anchor the deprecation script''s package lookup to its own location. Deriving\n  the list from a relative glob made it depend on the caller''s directory, which\n  the previous hardcoded list did not.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoBgQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASZ0QAI5zD7EGqtxlBrpGA1T+Wvj4\nw6HmOuzgGqH2+QCHQY4BYmGwwnaBpqfwNH3EQzW3+AHJzH5GM2xEPhoolgnKw7wH\nHoEc6RF79YZIoK7ea8/RN0fFZ5d354vl9/rR/AwYDpM5r7ws6v1DpQ5v5G63yGIf\n47UH484TO9fAJiwDUVdSKA0C7UF1uuZhx50XHlJ5Xkq/MHKsKFBBIx+8hM9xmdeh\nn7X6U4mIUPqSk5w26+c6dbeWYWMdWP/4fDn8/bgkjnTO+gcPqs8w1GAqMPNOOcfn\nqZ/vChT4AdoJNIzUzwWr3pCxlMDhSsyNph1cz9LNFfM6tpxGiBfoYiDPaClFw5lT\nc+7rZkwuuxxltb2Pix2PWJyZVEGYuAtwe8hUuX1iEyD4dul6Vi6h3j48LSzBiwA5\ncVc3OX5+nVNwAe6j619VeW9yrD+ULlhxGT3B+2EkSYIOiuo+Uv8laGhjijf5+Xgf\nXOVa0TXbkRShf0qcf6yT32Uvx9+XDm7mzkiYX4REwFqwzpsBP/eMrdG6W86/Uggp\nRoyXiC4Bk1Ly8y7oKvBkXklhFXG0xVRuqN5gHoMxWualsoZTBGDQ/UBcjQXDwqq+\nf31AcGL/pH6CiteBBMRsqRrFinXIrZ5r2N8eVWSlqLN1odV55urjBKkp+KyN5de+\n/glIF6Qt1rbaLrooo0Ez\n=DJxn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T14:13:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/651e97875083b189dbe46a5dca8ff3f389a3db5b","node_id":"C_kwDODMcke9oAKDY1MWU5Nzg3NTA4M2IxODlkYmU0NmE1ZGNhOGZmM2YzODlhM2RiNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commit/0d92edb85c94e55a454aedfd97f66b79eab8bfc2","sha":"0d92edb85c94e55a454aedfd97f66b79eab8bfc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0d92edb85c94e55a454aedfd97f66b79eab8bfc2"}],"sha":"651e97875083b189dbe46a5dca8ff3f389a3db5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/651e97875083b189dbe46a5dca8ff3f389a3db5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0d92edb85c94e55a454aedfd97f66b79eab8bfc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:12:51Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:12:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(analytics-js): deprecate pre-consent storage strategy (#3188)\n\n* test(analytics-js): pre-consent storage baseline\n\nLocks in how every `preConsent.storage.strategy` value resolves against\nthe load API storage options, all the way from the load options through\nto `state.storage.entries`.\n\nPasses against unmodified `develop`, so it guards the deprecation of\n`strategy` rather than restating it.\n\nPart of SDK-5448\n\n* feat(analytics-js): deprecate pre-consent storage strategy\n\nThe storage load API option now decides what is persisted before consent\nis given. Only the fallback changes while pre-consent is active: an\nentry is persisted only if a storage type has been explicitly\nconfigured, so nothing is persisted by default.\n\nThis makes any combination expressible, including persisting both the\nanonymous ID and the session info, without configuring storage twice.\n\n`strategy` is deprecated and warns at runtime. When it is set it still\ntakes precedence and behaves exactly as before, so existing\nconfigurations are unaffected. Removal is deferred to the next major.\n\nPart of SDK-5448\n\n* test(analytics-js): cover the unconfigured storage load path\n\nRuns the load options through `normalizeLoadOptions`, as the load API\ndoes, to pin that no storage type or entry defaults are filled in. That\nis what makes the pre-consent phase persist nothing when the storage\noption is not supplied at all.\n\nPart of SDK-5448\n\n* fix(analytics-js): reject invalid entry types before consent\n\nEntry storage types are not validated at config time, so an unsupported\nvalue such as `anonymousId: { type: ''localStoarge'' }` fell through to\nthe availability fallback and resolved to a persistent storage type,\npersisting the identifier before consent was given.\n\nWhile the storage options drive the pre-consent phase, an unsupported\ntype now resolves to no storage with the existing validation warning.\nResolution after consent is unchanged.\n\nAlso stops `logMessages` from depending on the deprecated\n`StorageStrategy` type, and marks the files that must read the\ndeprecated strategy option with the repo''s `sonarjs/deprecation`\ndirective so they do not report as new code smells.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): ignore an invalid storage type before consent\n\nAn unsupported `storage.type` is normalized to the default type at\nconfig time, so `type: ''localStoarge''` reached the store manager as\n`cookieStorage` and read as an explicitly configured type, persisting\nevery entry before consent was given.\n\nWhile the storage options drive the pre-consent phase, the configured\ntype is now checked against the supported types before it counts as\nconfigured. Resolution after consent is unchanged, so an unsupported\ntype still falls back to the default type once consent is given.\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): validate the storage type in one place\n\nAn unsupported `storage.type` was coerced to the default type at config\ntime, so the store manager could not tell a configured `cookieStorage`\nfrom a substituted one. That is what made a typo persist data before\nconsent, and it needed a second check in the resolution path to undo.\n\nThe config manager now leaves an unsupported type undefined, which the\nresolution chain already handles, so the extra check is gone. The entry\ntypes stay validated in the store manager, where the applicable default\nis known, and that check no longer skips the post-consent phase.\n\nThe warning no longer names a default type, since which one applies\ndepends on the consent phase.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): drop the bundled ESM size limit bump\n\nThe single validation site is smaller than the two checks it replaced,\nso the bundled ESM output is back under its original limit. Only the\ntwo modern UMD entries still need the 0.5 KiB raise.\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): report storage options where they enter\n\nThe storage type validation is now a single `validateStorageOptions`\ncalled on the load API options and on the consent API options, so the\nconsent API storage options are reported for the first time. It only\nwarns; the store manager resolves an unsupported value against the\ndefault that applies to the current consent phase.\n\nThe storage options also persist across consent API invocations, so an\ninvocation that provides none leaves the storage as it is. Previously\nthe global type carried over through `state.storage.type` while the\nentries silently reverted to the load API options, relocating any entry\na previous invocation had overridden.\n\nThat makes `state.storage.type` dead, so it is removed along with the\nwrite back it existed for.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): guard the storage options validation\n\nThe consent API storage options come straight from the caller, so\n`validateStorageOptions` now requires an object literal before reading\nit. Anything else is ignored rather than partially inspected.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): address the static analysis findings\n\nUses `Array.prototype.at` for the trailing host parts in `getTopDomain`,\nmatching the existing usage in the error handler utils, and switches the\nthree generic undefined assertions to `toBeUndefined`.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): require opting in to storage before consent\n\nThe storage load API options reached the pre-consent phase as soon as\nthe strategy was absent, so an existing configuration that enabled\npre-consent and configured storage started persisting every entry,\nincluding the user traits and the auth token, before consent was given.\nThat inverted the documented `none` default silently on upgrade.\n\n`preConsent.storage.enabled` now gates it. Without it the strategy\nfalls back to `none` exactly as before, so no existing configuration\nchanges. With it, the storage load API options drive the phase.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): correct the pre-consent storage test options\n\nTwo scenarios carried a nested `storage` object inside the pre-consent\nstorage options, which is not part of the type and was ignored, so they\nwere not configured the way they read.\n\nAlso documents that enabling the storage takes precedence over the\ndeprecated strategy.\n\n* docs(analytics-js): correct the pre-consent storage option docs\n\nNot enabling the storage does not mean nothing is persisted. The\ndeprecated strategy still decides in that case, so only a configuration\nwith neither of them persists nothing before consent.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): name the opt-in in the warning\n\nMigrating off `preConsent.storage.strategy` also requires opting in with\n`preConsent.storage.enabled`. Without that, removing the strategy and\nconfiguring the `storage` load API options would silently persist nothing\nbefore consent is given.\n\nAddresses a Copilot review comment on the deprecation message.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): revert unrelated .at() usage\n\n`Array.prototype.at` is neither transpiled (`useBuiltIns: \"entry\"` with no\ncore-js entry import) nor listed in `legacyJSEngineRequiredPolyfills`, so it\nwould throw in the legacy bundle. `getTopDomain` is unrelated to this change\nanyway, so it goes back to index access and the file no longer touches it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Denis Ciccale <539546+dciccale@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bc62619dcb136d12bf0b57ef74d35fafec9b888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/1bc62619dcb136d12bf0b57ef74d35fafec9b888"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/0d92edb85c94e55a454aedfd97f66b79eab8bfc2","verification":{"payload":"tree 1bc62619dcb136d12bf0b57ef74d35fafec9b888\nparent 49168b5198b52ea082fde3635ff1128a4d5dbd2f\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1788876771 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788876771 +0530\n\nfeat(analytics-js): deprecate pre-consent storage strategy (#3188)\n\n* test(analytics-js): pre-consent storage baseline\n\nLocks in how every `preConsent.storage.strategy` value resolves against\nthe load API storage options, all the way from the load options through\nto `state.storage.entries`.\n\nPasses against unmodified `develop`, so it guards the deprecation of\n`strategy` rather than restating it.\n\nPart of SDK-5448\n\n* feat(analytics-js): deprecate pre-consent storage strategy\n\nThe storage load API option now decides what is persisted before consent\nis given. Only the fallback changes while pre-consent is active: an\nentry is persisted only if a storage type has been explicitly\nconfigured, so nothing is persisted by default.\n\nThis makes any combination expressible, including persisting both the\nanonymous ID and the session info, without configuring storage twice.\n\n`strategy` is deprecated and warns at runtime. When it is set it still\ntakes precedence and behaves exactly as before, so existing\nconfigurations are unaffected. Removal is deferred to the next major.\n\nPart of SDK-5448\n\n* test(analytics-js): cover the unconfigured storage load path\n\nRuns the load options through `normalizeLoadOptions`, as the load API\ndoes, to pin that no storage type or entry defaults are filled in. That\nis what makes the pre-consent phase persist nothing when the storage\noption is not supplied at all.\n\nPart of SDK-5448\n\n* fix(analytics-js): reject invalid entry types before consent\n\nEntry storage types are not validated at config time, so an unsupported\nvalue such as `anonymousId: { type: ''localStoarge'' }` fell through to\nthe availability fallback and resolved to a persistent storage type,\npersisting the identifier before consent was given.\n\nWhile the storage options drive the pre-consent phase, an unsupported\ntype now resolves to no storage with the existing validation warning.\nResolution after consent is unchanged.\n\nAlso stops `logMessages` from depending on the deprecated\n`StorageStrategy` type, and marks the files that must read the\ndeprecated strategy option with the repo''s `sonarjs/deprecation`\ndirective so they do not report as new code smells.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): ignore an invalid storage type before consent\n\nAn unsupported `storage.type` is normalized to the default type at\nconfig time, so `type: ''localStoarge''` reached the store manager as\n`cookieStorage` and read as an explicitly configured type, persisting\nevery entry before consent was given.\n\nWhile the storage options drive the pre-consent phase, the configured\ntype is now checked against the supported types before it counts as\nconfigured. Resolution after consent is unchanged, so an unsupported\ntype still falls back to the default type once consent is given.\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): validate the storage type in one place\n\nAn unsupported `storage.type` was coerced to the default type at config\ntime, so the store manager could not tell a configured `cookieStorage`\nfrom a substituted one. That is what made a typo persist data before\nconsent, and it needed a second check in the resolution path to undo.\n\nThe config manager now leaves an unsupported type undefined, which the\nresolution chain already handles, so the extra check is gone. The entry\ntypes stay validated in the store manager, where the applicable default\nis known, and that check no longer skips the post-consent phase.\n\nThe warning no longer names a default type, since which one applies\ndepends on the consent phase.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): drop the bundled ESM size limit bump\n\nThe single validation site is smaller than the two checks it replaced,\nso the bundled ESM output is back under its original limit. Only the\ntwo modern UMD entries still need the 0.5 KiB raise.\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): report storage options where they enter\n\nThe storage type validation is now a single `validateStorageOptions`\ncalled on the load API options and on the consent API options, so the\nconsent API storage options are reported for the first time. It only\nwarns; the store manager resolves an unsupported value against the\ndefault that applies to the current consent phase.\n\nThe storage options also persist across consent API invocations, so an\ninvocation that provides none leaves the storage as it is. Previously\nthe global type carried over through `state.storage.type` while the\nentries silently reverted to the load API options, relocating any entry\na previous invocation had overridden.\n\nThat makes `state.storage.type` dead, so it is removed along with the\nwrite back it existed for.\n\n* fix(analytics-js): guard the storage options validation\n\nThe consent API storage options come straight from the caller, so\n`validateStorageOptions` now requires an object literal before reading\nit. Anything else is ignored rather than partially inspected.\n\n* chore(analytics-js): address the