9287278659787d67915e6b4e2d0"}],"sha":"0bb2c81186cf2bcc499b49ee1d12fc6fc7631029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/0bb2c81186cf2bcc499b49ee1d12fc6fc7631029"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88789928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saikumarrs","id":88789928,"login":"saikumarrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzg5OTI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saikumarrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/commits/15e0fc47b3ed79287278659787d67915e6b4e2d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:24:02Z","email":"88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sai Kumar Battinoju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:24:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics-js): skip no-op server-side cookie writes (#3176)\n\n* fix(analytics-js): skip no-op server-side cookie writes\n\nWith useServerSideCookies enabled, every cookie-backed session key\nthat held a value fired a POST /rsaRequest on each page load, even\nwhen the value was byte-identical to the cookie already stored.\nTypically four requests per load, three of them redundant.\n\nSkip the request when the persisted cookie already holds the exact\nvalue being written, reusing the same stringifyWithoutCircular\ncomparison the response verification already performs. Values are\ncompared after decryption, so the check is unaffected by the\nencryption version a cookie was written with.\n\nThe comparison fails safe: string equality can only hold for\ngenuinely identical content, so a differing key order causes an\nunnecessary write rather than a missed one.\n\nrl_session still syncs on every page load because expiresAt\ngenuinely moves, which keeps session continuity intact.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* fix(analytics-js): only skip when no cookie write is pending\n\nAddresses review feedback on the skip guard.\n\nReading the persisted cookie is not sufficient on its own. If a write\nis already queued or in flight for the same key and the state reverts\nto the value the cookie still holds, the guard would skip and the\npending write would land afterwards, leaving the cookie and the state\ndivergent with nothing to reconcile them.\n\nSkip only while nothing is pending for that key. An A -> B -> A\ntransition now falls through, clears the pending timer and schedules\nthe write, which is the behaviour before the guard existed. The\noptimisation still applies on page load, where nothing is pending.\n\nAlso mark the helper private, and restore the shared store''s\nprototype methods after the new tests so their overrides cannot leak\ninto later tests.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* test(analytics-js): drive the pending cookie write for real\n\nThe regression test set serverSideCookiesRequestInProgress directly,\nso it asserted the guard''s precondition rather than the A -> B -> A\ntransition its comment described.\n\nIt now writes B through the real debounced path and lets the debounce\nelapse, so the request is genuinely in flight and unresolved when the\nvalue reverts to A. Verified it still fails with the\nserverSideCookiesRequestInProgress condition removed.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* fix(analytics-js): do not skip syncing client-written cookies\n\nStorage migration rewrites cookies client-side via store.set, and that\nruns before the effects register. The equal-value guard then saw the\ncookie already holding the right value and skipped the server request,\nso a migrated cookie stayed a script-written cookie permanently. Under\nSafari ITP that is capped at 7 days, after which the anonymous ID is\nregenerated - the exact outcome server-side cookies exist to prevent.\n\nJavaScript cannot tell whether a cookie was set by the server or by\nscript, so track the keys the SDK has written during this page load\nand never skip those. The flag is set by storage migration, by the\nmigration between storage types, and when a server-side request is\nissued, and is never cleared.\n\nThis also replaces the in-progress check in the guard. That flag is\ncleared by whichever request completes first, so with two writes in\nflight for one key it could read false while a write was still\noutstanding, letting the guard skip and the later write land last.\nThe new flag is monotonic and cannot go stale, so it subsumes that\ncheck. Reported by @dciccale in review.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): rename the cookie write tracking flag\n\nserverSideCookieSyncRequired read as \"a sync is needed\", but a key\nwithout the flag set often needs a sync too - that is the first-load\npath. It is also set on two purely client-side write paths, so the\nserver-side prefix was wrong.\n\ncookieWrittenInPageLoad states what the set sites actually record.\n\nRef: SDK-5409","tree":{"sha":"bef80bbcce04597bda03c05d577a3b87b9fa955c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/trees/bef80bbcce04597bda03c05d577a3b87b9fa955c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rudderlabs/rudder-sdk-js/git/commits/15e0fc47b3ed79287278659787d67915e6b4e2d0","verification":{"payload":"tree bef80bbcce04597bda03c05d577a3b87b9fa955c\nparent ab7d44b0154f97a74c98391b7ecd32ba4ed64479\nauthor Sai Kumar Battinoju <88789928+saikumarrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1788351842 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788351842 +0200\n\nfix(analytics-js): skip no-op server-side cookie writes (#3176)\n\n* fix(analytics-js): skip no-op server-side cookie writes\n\nWith useServerSideCookies enabled, every cookie-backed session key\nthat held a value fired a POST /rsaRequest on each page load, even\nwhen the value was byte-identical to the cookie already stored.\nTypically four requests per load, three of them redundant.\n\nSkip the request when the persisted cookie already holds the exact\nvalue being written, reusing the same stringifyWithoutCircular\ncomparison the response verification already performs. Values are\ncompared after decryption, so the check is unaffected by the\nencryption version a cookie was written with.\n\nThe comparison fails safe: string equality can only hold for\ngenuinely identical content, so a differing key order causes an\nunnecessary write rather than a missed one.\n\nrl_session still syncs on every page load because expiresAt\ngenuinely moves, which keeps session continuity intact.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* fix(analytics-js): only skip when no cookie write is pending\n\nAddresses review feedback on the skip guard.\n\nReading the persisted cookie is not sufficient on its own. If a write\nis already queued or in flight for the same key and the state reverts\nto the value the cookie still holds, the guard would skip and the\npending write would land afterwards, leaving the cookie and the state\ndivergent with nothing to reconcile them.\n\nSkip only while nothing is pending for that key. An A -> B -> A\ntransition now falls through, clears the pending timer and schedules\nthe write, which is the behaviour before the guard existed. The\noptimisation still applies on page load, where nothing is pending.\n\nAlso mark the helper private, and restore the shared store''s\nprototype methods after the new tests so their overrides cannot leak\ninto later tests.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* test(analytics-js): drive the pending cookie write for real\n\nThe regression test set serverSideCookiesRequestInProgress directly,\nso it asserted the guard''s precondition rather than the A -> B -> A\ntransition its comment described.\n\nIt now writes B through the real debounced path and lets the debounce\nelapse, so the request is genuinely in flight and unresolved when the\nvalue reverts to A. Verified it still fails with the\nserverSideCookiesRequestInProgress condition removed.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* fix(analytics-js): do not skip syncing client-written cookies\n\nStorage migration rewrites cookies client-side via store.set, and that\nruns before the effects register. The equal-value guard then saw the\ncookie already holding the right value and skipped the server request,\nso a migrated cookie stayed a script-written cookie permanently. Under\nSafari ITP that is capped at 7 days, after which the anonymous ID is\nregenerated - the exact outcome server-side cookies exist to prevent.\n\nJavaScript cannot tell whether a cookie was set by the server or by\nscript, so track the keys the SDK has written during this page load\nand never skip those. The flag is set by storage migration, by the\nmigration between storage types, and when a server-side request is\nissued, and is never cleared.\n\nThis also replaces the in-progress check in the guard. That flag is\ncleared by whichever request completes first, so with two writes in\nflight for one key it could read false while a write was still\noutstanding, letting the guard skip and the later write land last.\nThe new flag is monotonic and cannot go stale, so it subsumes that\ncheck. Reported by @dciccale in review.\n\nRef: SDK-5409\n\n* refactor(analytics-js): rename the cookie write tracking flag\n\nserverSideCookieSyncRequired read as \"a sync is needed\", but a key\nwithout the flag set often needs a sync too - that is the first-load\npath. It is also set on two purely client-side write paths, so the\nserver-side prefix wa