636b4b10ff0991370e65","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKDhmNmVmMmQyYzFiOGM2MGMwMDljNjM2YjRiMTBmZjA5OTEzNzBlNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52","sha":"9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52"}],"sha":"8f6ef2d2c1b8c60c009c636b4b10ff0991370e65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/8f6ef2d2c1b8c60c009c636b4b10ff0991370e65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:14:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:14:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: count the login failure when an ignore-pattern test cannot complete (JAHIA-SEC-362) (#98)\n\nFixes the fail-open reported in Jahia/jahia-security-scan#1400 (GHSA-7qgr-2hqv-r344, CVSS 4.8 medium).\n\n`ignore_patterns` is an EXEMPTION list: matchesIgnorePattern() returning true means \"do not count\nthis login failure\". The 50 ms match ran on a worker thread and the timeout branch returned MATCHED,\nbelieving it was \"failing closed\" — but for an exemption, granting the exemption IS failing open. An\nunauthenticated attacker who appended a backtracking suffix to every username was never counted,\nnever banned and never audited: the harder the module was attacked, the less it recorded.\n\nA second instance, not named in the advisory, was found while fixing it: submitMatchTask() returned\na completed MATCHED future on RejectedExecutionException. Saturating the bounded pool with a flood\nof slow usernames is an easier trigger than one slow regex, so fixing only the timeout would have\nleft the hole reachable. Both paths now resolve to NOT_MATCHED.\n\nAlso hardened: usernames longer than 256 chars are no longer handed to the regex engine and are\nnever exempted, so they cannot burn the match budget. Rejecting rather than truncating, since\ntruncation could make a pattern match input the operator never wrote.\n\nBREAKING (documented in CHANGELOG under 3.1.3-SNAPSHOT with \"are you impacted / what must I do\"):\nan operator whose pattern is not linear-time may now see genuinely-ignored accounts counted, and\neventually banned, rather than silently skipped. The abort is logged at WARN. No config change is\nrequired on upgrade.\n\nTests — BruteForceTrackerIgnorePatternTest#catastrophicRegex_failClosed_eventSkipped asserted the\nvulnerable behaviour as correct, so it is inverted rather than added to; the suite was actively\ndefending the bug. Reverting the production change now fails 3 of that spec''s 11 cases. New e2e\nspec 05-ignore-patterns.cy.ts reproduces the advisory''s two-arm measurement live, closing a gap\nwhere ignore_patterns had no behavioural e2e coverage at all.\n\nThird commit, unrelated failure found while verifying: 02''s \"shows the admin panel to a user granted\nONLY bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin\" asserted something unreachable by construction — register.jsx\nattaches the screen with targets [''administration-server-configuration:10''], so requiredPermission\ngates only the menu entry inside the administration console, whose route tree Jahia gates on\nadministrationAccess. The …-module-only role from #66 is NOT useless (its GraphQL arm passes, making\nit a working API-only role); only the UI claim was wrong. The test is inverted to assert the real\nconstraint and roles.xml gains a scope note.\n\nVerified: JUnit 345/345, BUILD SUCCESS (Java 17). Cypress 41/41 across all 5 specs on a clean\nJahia 8-SNAPSHOT cluster-mode stack, with jahia.log confirming the timeout branch genuinely fired\nrather than the arm passing vacuously.\n\nBackport: community module on a single main train, version-independent of Jahia, so 3.1.3 covers\nevery affected version. No 8.2.3.x / 8.2.2.x / 8.1.9.x branch backport applies.\n\nRefs: Jahia/jahia-security-scan#1400","tree":{"sha":"9f611ae2499076736b6d95911784fc990fa8aa74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/9f611ae2499076736b6d95911784fc990fa8aa74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f611ae2499076736b6d95911784fc990fa8aa74\nparent ee3a1df402fba0cd1bc0bed70f83ebe5ac362321\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1789992847 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789992847 +0200\n\nfix: count the login failure when an ignore-pattern test cannot complete (JAHIA-SEC-362) (#98)\n\nFixes the fail-open reported in Jahia/jahia-security-scan#1400 (GHSA-7qgr-2hqv-r344, CVSS 4.8 medium).\n\n`ignore_patterns` is an EXEMPTION list: matchesIgnorePattern() returning true means \"do not count\nthis login failure\". The 50 ms match ran on a worker thread and the timeout branch returned MATCHED,\nbelieving it was \"failing closed\" — but for an exemption, granting the exemption IS failing open. An\nunauthenticated attacker who appended a backtracking suffix to every username was never counted,\nnever banned and never audited: the harder the module was attacked, the less it recorded.\n\nA second instance, not named in the advisory, was found while fixing it: submitMatchTask() returned\na completed MATCHED future on RejectedExecutionException. Saturating the bounded pool with a flood\nof slow usernames is an easier trigger than one slow regex, so fixing only the timeout would have\nleft the hole reachable. Both paths now resolve to NOT_MATCHED.\n\nAlso hardened: usernames longer than 256 chars are no longer handed to the regex engine and are\nnever exempted, so they cannot burn the match budget. Rejecting rather than truncating, since\ntruncation could make a pattern match input the operator never wrote.\n\nBREAKING (documented in CHANGELOG under 3.1.3-SNAPSHOT with \"are you impacted / what must I do\"):\nan operator whose pattern is not linear-time may now see genuinely-ignored accounts counted, and\neventually banned, rather than silently skipped. The abort is logged at WARN. No config change is\nrequired on upgrade.\n\nTests — BruteForceTrackerIgnorePatternTest#catastrophicRegex_failClosed_eventSkipped asserted the\nvulnerable behaviour as correct, so it is inverted rather than added to; the suite was actively\ndefending the bug. Reverting the production change now fails 3 of that spec''s 11 cases. New e2e\nspec 05-ignore-patterns.cy.ts reproduces the advisory''s two-arm measurement live, closing a gap\nwhere ignore_patterns had no behavioural e2e coverage at all.\n\nThird commit, unrelated failure found while verifying: 02''s \"shows the admin panel to a user granted\nONLY bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin\" asserted something unreachable by construction — register.jsx\nattaches the screen with targets [''administration-server-configuration:10''], so requiredPermission\ngates only the menu entry inside the administration console, whose route tree Jahia gates on\nadministrationAccess. The …-module-only role from #66 is NOT useless (its GraphQL arm passes, making\nit a working API-only role); only the UI claim was wrong. The test is inverted to assert the real\nconstraint and roles.xml gains a scope note.\n\nVerified: JUnit 345/345, BUILD SUCCESS (Java 17). Cypress 41/41 across all 5 specs on a clean\nJahia 8-SNAPSHOT cluster-mode stack, with jahia.log confirming the timeout branch genuinely fired\nrather than the arm passing vacuously.\n\nBackport: community module on a single main train, version-independent of Jahia, so 3.1.3 covers\nevery affected version. No 8.2.3.x / 8.2.2.x / 8.1.9.x branch backport applies.\n\nRefs: Jahia/jahia-security-scan#1400","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsR+PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEkgQACRhYM/XtBiBmOcIhvP8Fnu8\nGicxSu4QsIeTUKiYtq2KRQbkqj6CfVFb5QVJda4ZwsEPNH858ypd/9pI2YQ4iyAf\neG2kHnDG96wjU3zZwMyLiy8UU37+wWQWkmiGluHr0rM9//ceoct27ZEeiYoJHpgS\nGH3/bIpPVgxL1vMbarDoBziT/bYy9zDtKaM73Kh2vwmTP/KOXVM1ZnZm/snDolGM\ndXrH2WTwjtVefvY13GO267G0yzl1srrdc3Zgxz1Ks7v9r/LNVTm7ciuAFfOdEPdw\nTWwJoefnInUjywqlLpDZP3Bym7HR03T61dXKio/VKeX0fNA8/dd/cg0SIvUiNd2t\nXb7RdC32RK9XDSj7uors2Aj1JOyBEBI5CiSdGyS+8B5Nga0y/4MA+isZRQaaCRje\nm9/K40Hx1pSHZuVfrtnG3as+XmGMnUliaUTPl3gvOjlDXD4D5SG637wrQT0xh0SS\ny0DCR6SiXpFAf47/DI0F8/p12yDczGN1dL/hxBDAMW8X596fCUAFPE26kF6+VsxW\nz+Q37yTwVyPCv5IHjPeFS1FEKP/FkH4x1wx38IY5T+TOH3lA0ZamE4VnFxltMaHr\n1/pRDCeioM3Lcqys9AHJxleq06pLBFm2wN4zRo/1Z5erYFTWDAAWyuZERUcM46tG\n2SircTApOB8ctYugTrjA\n=zMzQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T12:14:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKDkyOTJmNDFlZWY4OTIxNDVlZWU1MzAwNzFmY2UwZDE3YjQxMjhjNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/ee3a1df402fba0cd1bc0bed70f83ebe5ac362321","sha":"ee3a1df402fba0cd1bc0bed70f83ebe5ac362321","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/ee3a1df402fba0cd1bc0bed70f83ebe5ac362321"}],"sha":"9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/9292f41eef892145eee530071fce0d17b4128c52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.co