c3ZjcwNTQ3NTkxODlmZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/a093106ee5934e49fd15e2ed0c3bde939240d7ae","sha":"a093106ee5934e49fd15e2ed0c3bde939240d7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/a093106ee5934e49fd15e2ed0c3bde939240d7ae"}],"sha":"acf4f1c4e79f97a0851cbb9477f7054759189feb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/acf4f1c4e79f97a0851cbb9477f7054759189feb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/a093106ee5934e49fd15e2ed0c3bde939240d7ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:04:17Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:04:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add ignore_paths to exempt non-login endpoints from detection (#54)\n\n* feat: add ignore_paths to exempt non-login endpoints from detection\n\nThe enforcement valve runs at auth-pipeline position 0 on every request,\nand the Basic/APIToken/jahiatoken detectors fire on credential-header\npresence regardless of the target URL. A non-login endpoint hit with a\nstale or wrong Authorization header (e.g. a client polling a public\ncontent URL) was therefore counted as a failed login and could ban a\nlegitimate client.\n\nAdd an `ignore_paths` global setting: a list of literal, case-sensitive\nURI substrings matched against request.getRequestURI() in\nAuthValveFailureSource before the detector chain runs. Matching requests\nare exempt from failure DETECTION only; ban ENFORCEMENT (banned-IP\nshort-circuit + blocklist) still applies on every path.\n\nSubstring (not regex) matching is deliberate: it stays allocation-light\nand ReDoS-free on the hot path and is robust to Jahia''s vanity-vs-\n/cms/render URI rewriting, where both forms share a distinctive tail.\n\nWired end-to-end: GlobalSettings/GlobalSettingsUpdate/GlobalConfigHolder,\nSettingsService (persist + validateIgnorePaths: no control chars/CRLF,\n<= 512 chars), GraphQL saveGlobalSettings arg + globalSettings field,\nGeneral tab UI, i18n, and the shipped default .cfg with a documented\nexample (modules-repository.moduleList.json).\n\nTests: IgnorePathMatchingTest (8) + IgnorePathValidationTest (7); full\nsuite 249/249 green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: snapshot request URI before invokeNext for ignore-path check\n\nThe ignore-path exemption compared request.getRequestURI() after\nvalveContext.invokeNext(). Downstream valves can internally forward the\nrequest (e.g. to render the 401/login page), and per the servlet spec a\nforward rewrites getRequestURI() to the forwarded path — so the check\nsaw the wrong URI and the audited requestPath was the forwarded page,\nnot the original inbound URL.\n\nCapture the URI once at the start of invoke(), before invokeNext(), and\nuse that snapshot both for matchesIgnoredPath() and for the audited\nrequestPath. This is the correct value for any path-based decision.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add e2e spec positively exercising ignore_paths\n\nAdds tests/cypress/e2e/04-ignore-paths.cy.ts (4 tests) and extends the\nsaveGlobalSettings/getGlobalSettings fixtures with ignorePaths:\n\n- persists ignorePaths through save/get\n- an ignored path accrues no failures even past maxRetry (no ban, no\n  tracked window)\n- the same endpoint IS detected when not in ignorePaths (control)\n- bans are still enforced while ignorePaths is configured\n\nThe spec drives /modules/graphql with a bad Basic header: an API\nendpoint is rendered in place with a stable request URI, unlike\nbrowser-facing paths (admin/pages) which forward a failed auth to the\nlogin page — the same non-forwarding shape as the real store\nmodules-repository.moduleList.json fetch.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"365e26f5424e16c0e0d8cba7397335244337fb56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/365e26f5424e16c0e0d8cba7397335244337fb56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/a093106ee5934e49fd15e2ed0c3bde939240d7ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 365e26f5424e16c0e0d8cba7397335244337fb56\nparent e6f70e0f6ac99c2ddb3b5d93873a4a585c379b87\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783605857 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783605857 +0200\n\nfeat: add ignore_paths to exempt non-login endpoints from detection (#54)\n\n* feat: add ignore_paths to exempt non-login endpoints from detection\n\nThe enforcement valve runs at auth-pipeline position 0 on every request,\nand the Basic/APIToken/jahiatoken detectors fire on credential-header\npresence regardless of the target URL. A non-login endpoint hit with a\nstale or wrong Authorization header (e.g. a client polling a public\ncontent URL) was therefore counted as a failed login and could ban a\nlegitimate client.\n\nAdd an `ignore_paths` global setting: a list of literal, case-sensitive\nURI substrings matched against request.getRequestURI() in\nAuthValveFailureSource before the detector chain runs. Matching requests\nare exempt from failure DETECTION only; ban ENFORCEMENT (banned-IP\nshort-circuit + blocklist) still applies on every path.\n\nSubstring (not regex) matching is deliberate: it stays allocation-light\nand ReDoS-free on the hot path and is robust to Jahia''s vanity-vs-\n/cms/render URI rewriting, where both forms share a distinctive tail.\n\nWired end-to-end: GlobalSettings/GlobalSettingsUpdate/GlobalConfigHolder,\nSettingsService (persist + validateIgnorePaths: no control chars/CRLF,\n<= 512 chars), GraphQL saveGlobalSettings arg + globalSettings field,\nGeneral tab UI, i18n, and the shipped default .cfg with a documented\nexample (modules-repository.moduleList.json).\n\nTests: IgnorePathMatchingTest (8) + IgnorePathValidationTest (7); full\nsuite 249/249 green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: snapshot request URI before invokeNext for ignore-path check\n\nThe ignore-path exemption compared request.getRequestURI() after\nvalveContext.invokeNext(). Downstream valves can internally forward the\nrequest (e.g. to render the 401/login page), and per the servlet spec a\nforward rewrites getRequestURI() to the forwarded path — so the check\nsaw the wrong URI and the audited requestPath was the forwarded page,\nnot the original inbound URL.\n\nCapture the URI once at the start of invoke(), before invokeNext(), and\nuse that snapshot both for matchesIgnoredPath() and for the audited\nrequestPath. This is the correct value for any path-based decision.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add e2e spec positively exercising ignore_paths\n\nAdds tests/cypress/e2e/04-ignore-paths.cy.ts (4 tests) and extends the\nsaveGlobalSettings/getGlobalSettings fixtures with ignorePaths:\n\n- persists ignorePaths through save/get\n- an ignored path accrues no failures even past maxRetry (no ban, no\n  tracked window)\n- the same endpoint IS detected when not in ignorePaths (control)\n- bans are still enforced while ignorePaths is configured\n\nThe spec drives /modules/graphql with a bad Basic header: an API\nendpoint is rendered in place with a stable request URI, unlike\nbrowser-facing paths (admin/pages) which forward a failed auth to the\nlogin page — the same non-forwarding shape as the real store\nmodules-repository.moduleList.json fetch.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6phCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOrAQAGDrpoNdGUBWcXhg8Xd2vFuL\nj/DlsA49gZ0eI1SP2/Sdq+u5r0+voy9QzweQCnIEH6Xb9qxpviA3/CahrulGNwmP\nvauzj3IKuE1Btct4AdzqFFqbKVDWHsOLLCBWGozGLu8upZwxXGsiA8l41RhQwh3U\nOY939QCtIG7zTMJ3EWJ73yBhfWxiGOuHvs4VM0odz/qnJ2/FPf4T7HEhZ8f1HkUb\nRyuHTiDoP4ffvUn+xuiWOhE99hHE6q8GpcAr+7kNwk0U4HivPI+Sq2fNjUD8jioQ\nXdl+ET8QV84rA2Jw9LQ7uXx8QyDjr5u4WKRVC9MuENyivjwSy1HfpCEOPlBoIwU7\nTvcTXR0H9FRU15+M4eeUrOC6D2kbkzoJ0OWjCLIo5BsKi1TBv2JoZRNGhfjt2Gx8\nhhhUOl2u9eoXTaw1jUA4HyK9IlLvWnQKpBnHbuV4pLnKZWmrpYpsbH33TkFoG8M+\nfdumHlHdhtJWFwmRpMu93l5n27CAhZbZxtvsqsEgQ4iFKChypj2X0xkTzAO7wPfs\ngUlZsoKFCh/ehm0QSavVrW0cfnLQq7VoKSJld91cAr3D3C8j3g8tABDv74AvZ/LS\ncFqcyhMb20f5kRcPAJgFF6PSWI3gC7fepx5Jbg6QzaNhNwvj3Y7GVMhL8AHKWEM5\nJnXv28r6YgvBwaZlZudE\n=vuUw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T14:04:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}",