url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/c70fbde376fc70c5f02d7a19c8b3de8d4bd0e198/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T19:33:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T19:33:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: terminate Hazelcast on deactivate instead of graceful shutdown (#51)\n\nGraceful shutdown blocks the OSGi bundle stop until all partition replicas\nof the leaving member are migrated. When those migrations stall (base+2 port\nfirewalled in one direction, classloader teardown mid-update), the surviving\nnode loops on ''Remaining migration tasks in queue => N, completedMigrations=0''\nand the module update hangs for up to hazelcast.graceful.shutdown.max.wait.\n\nterminate() leaves the cluster immediately. Safe because no Hazelcast state\nis authoritative-and-irrecoverable: bans are JCR-mirrored and restored by the\nstartup reconciliation pass (ADR 0004), failure windows are transient, and\nnotification markers only throttle. Same availability-over-continuity\ntrade-off as ADR 0002, now recorded as ADR 0005.\n\nAlso documents the recommended cluster update procedure in the README\n(stop everywhere, update, start + bidirectional base+2 port requirement).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac1fc465784868c74f9759c74c8df22761f353c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/ac1fc465784868c74f9759c74c8df22761f353c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/c70fbde376fc70c5f02d7a19c8b3de8d4bd0e198","verification":{"payload":"tree ac1fc465784868c74f9759c74c8df22761f353c9\nparent 528af0a08675c7bdb0309c5938dd90ffb25efcfd\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783020792 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783020792 +0200\n\nfix: terminate Hazelcast on deactivate instead of graceful shutdown (#51)\n\nGraceful shutdown blocks the OSGi bundle stop until all partition replicas\nof the leaving member are migrated. When those migrations stall (base+2 port\nfirewalled in one direction, classloader teardown mid-update), the surviving\nnode loops on ''Remaining migration tasks in queue => N, completedMigrations=0''\nand the module update hangs for up to hazelcast.graceful.shutdown.max.wait.\n\nterminate() leaves the cluster immediately. Safe because no Hazelcast state\nis authoritative-and-irrecoverable: bans are JCR-mirrored and restored by the\nstartup reconciliation pass (ADR 0004), failure windows are transient, and\nnotification markers only throttle. Same availability-over-continuity\ntrade-off as ADR 0002, now recorded as ADR 0005.\n\nAlso documents the recommended cluster update procedure in the README\n(stop everywhere, update, start + bidirectional base+2 port requirement).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRrz4CRC1aQ7uu