com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/a185da6bdc1508898ee039a3859b53e49bba10de","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKGExODVkYTZiZGMxNTA4ODk4ZWUwMzlhMzg1OWI1M2U0OWJiYTEwZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0","sha":"31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0"}],"sha":"a185da6bdc1508898ee039a3859b53e49bba10de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/a185da6bdc1508898ee039a3859b53e49bba10de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T19:12:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T19:12:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: static IP blocklist + dynamic Tor exit-node blocklist (#50)\n\n* feat: add blocklist settings plumbing (static CIDR list + Tor exit list config)\n\nNew global settings blocklist_ips, tor_blocklist_enabled, tor_blocklist_url,\ntor_blocklist_refresh_seconds wired through GlobalSettings, GlobalConfigHolder,\nGlobalSettingsUpdate and SettingsService. Blocklist CIDRs are validated strictly\nat save time; the Tor URL accepts http/https without userinfo (internal mirrors\nallowed); the refresh interval is clamped to [300, 604800] on both write and read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: extract reusable CidrListCache from BruteForceTracker whitelist cache\n\nSame CAS-cached parse-once behaviour, now shared: the tracker whitelist,\nthe upcoming BlocklistService (whitelist precedence + static blocklist)\nall consume one implementation instead of three copies.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: add TorExitNodeFetcher for the dynamic Tor exit-address blocklist\n\nPer-node scheduled fetcher (60s due-check tick, per-settings interval clamped\nto [300, 604800]s) that downloads and parses the TorDNSEL exit-addresses\nexport. Strict IP-literal parsing (no DNS), v4-mapped-v6 normalization, 5MB\nresponse cap, redirects disabled. Any failure — including a 200 response with\nzero valid entries — keeps the last-known list enforced and surfaces lastError\nfor the admin UI. forceRefresh() backs the upcoming ''Fetch now'' button.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: enforce static + Tor blocklists at the auth valve\n\nNew BlocklistService decides per request: activated flag, then whitelist\n(always wins — self-lockout safety valve), then static CIDR list, then Tor\nexit list. AuthValveFailureSource short-circuits blocklisted IPs right after\nthe ban check with the same BAD_PASSWORD valve result. Every hit is logged at\nINFO; a new BLOCKED audit event is written at most once per IP per hour\n(bounded in-memory throttle, pruned under IP-rotation floods).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: expose blocklist over GraphQL (settings fields, blocklistStatus, refreshTorBlocklist)\n\nsaveGlobalSettings gains blocklistIps / torBlocklistEnabled / torBlocklistUrl /\ntorBlocklistRefreshSeconds (null = unchanged). New blocklistStatus query returns\nstatic entry count plus per-node Tor list health (entry count, last fetch/attempt,\nage, last error). New refreshTorBlocklist mutation triggers a synchronous fetch\nfor the admin UI ''Fetch now'' button. All gated by bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: add Blocklist admin tab (static CIDRs, Tor toggle, live status, fetch now)\n\nSixth tab following the IntegrationsTab patterns: full-snapshot save\n(buildBaseSettings) so unrelated settings are never nulled, transient\nstatus + pre-rendered live regions for a11y, 30s-polled per-node blocklist\nstatus with last-fetch age and error surfacing, and a ''Fetch now'' button\nwired to the refreshTorBlocklist mutation. CIDRs are edited one-per-line\nand stored comma-separated.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: e2e coverage for the blocklist feature\n\nNew 03-blocklist spec: settings round-trip, static entry count via\nblocklistStatus, invalid-CIDR and non-http URL rejection, whitelist-precedence\nself-lockout safety (0.0.0.0/0 blocklist + docker-network whitelist, login\nstill succeeds), refreshTorBlocklist plumbing without asserting external\nnetwork success, and Blocklist tab visibility. Permissions spec extended to\nthe new blocklistStatus query. Actual request blocking stays unit-tested —\nthe blocklist has no unban escape hatch, so e2e-testing it would brick the\nharness.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: harden blocklist hot path and Tor fetcher after code review\n\n- Audit throttle: hard cap (20k) on the per-IP map so distinct-IP rotation\n  floods cannot grow the heap, and the stale-entry prune is time-boxed to\n  once a minute instead of a full scan per blocked request (amortized O(1)).\n- Blocked-attempt INFO logging now shares the 1/IP/hour throttle (every hit\n  still visible at DEBUG) so scanners cannot flood the application log.\n- TorExitNodeFetcher: single-flight guard so a manual ''Fetch now'' cannot race\n  the scheduled fetch and let a stale result overwrite a fresh one.\n- Auth valve''s BlocklistService reference is now OPTIONAL+GREEDY: a failure\n  in the blocklist component chain can never take down ban enforcement.\n- Reconciled i18n wording between en.json and the properties bundle;\n  documented the feature in the CHANGELOG.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"954d285feb90224a19e7c0aa9f3c3b87da6e3282","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/954d285feb90224a19e7c0aa9f3c3b87da6e3282"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0","verification":{"payload":"tree 954d285feb90224a19e7c0aa9f3c3b87da6e3282\nparent 94ec036a77fd32f8e9593d2f51a1b7dcb826e6b5\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783019527 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783019527 +0200\n\nfeat: static IP blocklist + dynamic Tor exit-node blocklist (#50)\n\n* feat: add blocklist settings plumbing (static CIDR list + Tor exit list config)\n\nNew global settings blocklist_ips, tor_blocklist_enabled, tor_blocklist_url,\ntor_blocklist_refresh_seconds wired through GlobalSettings, GlobalConfigHolder,\nGlobalSettingsUpdate and SettingsService. Blocklist CIDRs are validated strictly\nat save time; the Tor URL accepts http/https without userinfo (internal mirrors\nallowed); the refresh interval is clamped to [300, 604800] on both write and read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: extract reusable CidrListCache from BruteForceTracker whitelist cache\n\nSame CAS-cached parse-once behaviour, now shared: the tracker whitelist,\nthe upcoming BlocklistService (whitelist precedence + static blocklist)\nall consume one implementation instead of three copies.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: add TorExitNodeFetcher for the dynamic Tor exit-address blocklist\n\nPer-node scheduled fetcher (60s due-check tick, per-settings interval clamped\nto [300, 604800]s) that downloads and parses the TorDNSEL exit-addresses\nexport. Strict IP-literal parsing (no DNS), v4-mapped-v6 normalization, 5MB\nresponse cap, redirects disabled. Any failure — including a 200 response with\nzero valid entries — keeps the last-known list enforced and surfaces lastError\nfor the admin UI. forceRefresh() backs the upcoming ''Fetch now'' button.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: enforce static + Tor blocklists at the auth valve\n\nNew BlocklistService decides per request: activated flag, then whitelist\n(always wins — self-lockout safety valve), then static CIDR list, then Tor\nexit list. AuthValveFailureSource short-circuits blocklisted IPs right after\nthe ban check with the same BAD_PASSWORD valve result. Every hit is logged at\nINFO; a new BLOCKED audit event is written at most once per IP per hour\n(bounded in-memory throttle, pruned under IP-rotation floods).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: expose blocklist over GraphQL (settings fields, blocklistStatus, refreshTorBlocklist)\n\nsaveGlobalSettings gains blocklistIps / torBlocklistEnabled / torBlocklistUrl /\ntorBlocklistRefreshSeconds (null = unchanged). New blocklistStatus query returns\nstatic entry count plus per-node Tor list health (entry count, last fetch/attempt,\nage, last error). New refreshTorBlocklist mutation triggers a synchronous fetch\nfor the admin UI ''Fetch now'' button. All gated by bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: add Blocklist admin tab (static CIDRs, Tor toggle, live status, fetch now)\n\nSixth tab following the IntegrationsTab patterns: full-snapshot save\n(buildBaseSettings) so unrelated settings are never nulled, transient\nstatus + pre-rendered live regions for a11y, 30s-polled per-node blocklist\nstatus with last-fetch age and error surfacing, and a ''Fetch now'' button\nwired to the refreshTorBlocklist mutation. CIDRs are edited one-per-line\nand stored comma-separated.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: e2e coverage for the blocklist feature\n\nNew 03-blocklist spec: settings round-trip, static entry count via\nblocklistStatus, invalid-CIDR and non-http URL rejection, whitelist-precedence\nself-lockout safety (0.0.0.0/0 blocklist + docker-network whitelist, login\nstill succeeds), refreshTorBlocklist plumbing without asserting external\nnetwork success, and Blocklist tab visibility. Permissions spec extended to\nthe new blocklistStatus query. Actual request blocking stays unit-tested —\nthe blocklist has no unban escape hatch, so e2e-testing it would brick the\nharness.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: harden blocklist hot path and Tor fetcher after code review\n\n- Audit throttle: hard cap (20k) on the per-IP map so distinct-IP rotation\n  floods cannot grow the heap, and the stale-entry prune is time-boxed to\n  once a minute instead of a full scan per blocked request (amortized O(1)).\n- Blocked-attempt INFO logging now shares the 1/IP/hour throttle (every hit\n  still visible at DEBUG) so scanners cannot flood the application log.\n- TorExitNodeFetcher: single-flight guard so a manual ''Fetch now'' cannot race\n  the scheduled fetch and let a stale result overwrite a fresh one.\n- Auth valve''s BlocklistService reference is now OPTIONAL+GREEDY: a failure\n  in the blocklist component chain can never take down ban enforcement.\n- Reconciled i18n wording between en.json and the properties bundle;\n  documented the feature in the CHANGELOG.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRrgHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGP4QABSJNqqmBWZW/x+PwMjCmN5O\na36Vsu6bKXW0pXj/PW5m/ATUzzh3EZ7NcSFxX1OVuycPrXCuiGeynb30kDa4NAyn\nTsr0DnJ3nVTXZjkk2A0qCb1YcLByWGaXH2L90TLiJtz2TWZgGXylUOhRdCEjPWK8\no050XOqB+lkAiRFWUymSiJE1JlOm0MOwjoQCLl8k0PC5CD3bZ9XNDegibmGQT0pK\nV8eL6lNvydrfTJjowOFzvjU4tukHfeUcX+/m0ceBNGsPGqo9Ft//Yu4Kn6OzAT66\nz2UszynhzSQCxNNWq7cd01n4opQWi80vA8XMFHt2D21HyYokFStna6AKPDZuNacu\nTr0kGVScCiaVSaYTGcgqNT51Edo0Hq9wFh3HmTL5ldMsS8dOGdtET3BAMeS4KN+s\n5qCTqPUAKuH7UJkOQK/nIb7vr+6MTz+6cnixysLG8Jf8Q7d0EsamIM/p2BBtzbAX\nki/GTcd87cg1MJUYyh7LVzWnX6HOtR0meDJZTlcCYC1tRM4oDkhtzWw1rjiWR3zF\n53WCrMYWRAXw22MEzLWjcyAXwazrVKKu7FKx+D9hLyqo1CGT2lzOjfvX8W9+ifyH\nN/ZOweYtB5vdpXGcIOObcW9JdHTz1l0MjByvwh5RX99aTIGqu8KOMQRF1rJ/aizY\nXXS86QtmyJ5oPO3YoF5z\n=zbco\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-02T19:12:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKDMxZjU0YTQ0NzI0ZTM4OWE5ZmYyNTY3YjAyOGQ1MDMwYWNjOGU1YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/94ec036a77fd32f8e9593d2f51a1b7dcb826e6b5","sha":"94ec036a77fd32f8e9593d2f51a1b7dcb826e6b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/94ec036a77fd32f8e9593d2f51a1b7dcb826e6b5"}],"sha":"31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/31f54a44724e389a9ff2567b028d5030acc8e5b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/94ec036a77fd32f8e9593d2f51a1b7dcb826e6b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T09:47:47Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T09:47:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: rename root package org.jahia.modules.* to org.jahia.community.* (#43)\n\nMove the module''s own base package from org.jahia.modules.bruteforceloginprotection\nto org.jahia.community.bruteforceloginprotection across all sub-packages\n(spi, core, actions, detectors, hazelcast, sources, graphql.types), aligning it\nwith the org.jahia.community groupId already used by this community module.\n\nBecause this module''s OSGi config PIDs and the Hazelcast deserialization filter\nare package-derived, the rename also covers:\n- JailConfigTracker.FACTORY_PID and GlobalConfigHolder.PID -> org.jahia.community.*\n- the two PID-named default .cfg files renamed to match (jail-default, global)\n- ClassLoaderAwareObjectInputStream.MODULE_PACKAGE_PREFIX security filter\n\nTwo test files (AuditLoggerSanitizeTest, SettingsServiceValidationTest) embed\nliteral control-char test data (NUL/DEL), which classifies them as binary; their\npackage declarations were updated at the byte level (preserving the test data).\n\n- git mv of package directories (main + test) preserves history\n- repointed bnd _dsannotations scan to the new package\n- Jahia GraphQL provider API imports (org.jahia.modules.graphql.provider.*) unchanged\n\nVerified: 165 unit tests pass; full Cypress E2E 20/20 pass on the deployed bundle\n(cluster mode; config PIDs bound, bans/audit/Hazelcast all functional).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"31a34240c3fd542bb566d8cd3f5bb50f5382e6ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/31a34240c3fd542bb566d8cd3f5bb50f5382e6ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/94ec036a77fd32f8e9593d2f51a1b7dcb826e6b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 31a34240c3fd542bb566d8cd3f5bb50f5382e6ea\nparent 5c6b51879e88066db28710af3df1af7f2fea71d2\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782035267 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782035267 +0200\n\nrefactor: rename root package org.jahia.modules.* to org.jahia.community.* (#43)\n\nMove the module''s own base package from org.jahia.modules.bruteforceloginprotection\nto org.jahia.community.bruteforceloginprotection across all sub-packages\n(spi, core, actions, detectors, hazelcast, sources, graphql.types), aligning it\nwith the org.jahia.community groupId already used by this community module.\n\nBecause this module''s OSGi config PIDs and the Hazelcast deserialization filter\nare package-derived, the rename also covers:\n- JailConfigTracker.FACTORY_PID and GlobalConfigHolder.PID -> org.jahia.community.*\n- the two PID-named default .cfg files renamed to match (jail-default, global)\n- ClassLoaderAwareObjectInputStream.MODULE_PACKAGE_PREFIX security filter\n\nTwo test files (AuditLoggerSanitizeTest, SettingsServiceValidationTest) embed\nliteral control-char test data (NUL/DEL), which classifies them as binary; their\npackage declarations were updated at the byte level (preserving the test data).\n\n- git mv of package directories (main + test) preserves history\n- repointed bnd _dsannotations scan to the new package\n- Jahia GraphQL provider API imports (org.jahia.modules.graphql.provider.*) unchanged\n\nVerified: 165 unit tests pass; full Cypress E2E 20/20 pass on the deployed bundle\n(cluster mode; config PIDs bound, bans/audit/Hazelcast all functional).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN