-force-login-protection/git/trees/9fb1a34b6da8f77beb9a2f1f43881b250fda3cda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/cd88fa2f357112d375d9d4014c5b37d8a8dc3e0f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fb1a34b6da8f77beb9a2f1f43881b250fda3cda\nparent 709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781814328 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781814328 +0200\n\nfix: cycle-2 blind-review remediation (concurrency, security boundary, a11y AAA, i18n, docs) (#40)\n\nSecond blind-review cycle: Java concurrency hardening (AtomicReference, value-checked ban removal, CAS whitelist cache, bounded pattern cache, records), AuditLogger boundary sanitization, escape-aware ReDoS pre-filter, saveJail contract fix; frontend settings-clobber fix + WCAG 2.2 AAA pass; i18n bundle 2->146 keys; documentation doc-rot corrected. Verified: 165 unit tests + 20 Cypress E2E pass, JaCoCo gate met, SonarQube quality gate OK, yarn lint clean, CI green, 0 CodeQL alerts.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFQ4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf3YQAK0QbvL844jjkeGFUz7Oqenn\n/CGloMmLS5PTpKZrrOVQW+9n4c/JW8iILO7C/5Niz0i36bbnVQ8FKC2PxylXC3z0\nsdRT2hf2nv/1w63fRVd1cHmIqsxnKG3PyEj+jRHgtLPnCaxmc4kyESXlH4/bRYuB\nvR8A0KFekPRbRLLxskW/Vs/k/Nb08Eg/GXOP7yswVM6+uBTRVkxSoxGcbtJEWaM3\nJLILgCOS9Ou17U8gv6q3hhae7/IAOjlYUtMDXterYjdTF/HA/IjG4O7wl9NURMfz\nlZzEp2u9J1Kua+Ut6yVObrKZEMr9uiWZShckSUNlm7qMYt4oQ7ehFcy8/3rfVYaV\nXBMPrOBZ/M8x+CVxkoRc3JxTCHm3j37zTCxEGLFR9w/KWAysBcp/dlcNM9j7u/g7\ngvfEjGgsfnIn9sqk94aFPXbloEIR7E0tN9zAas7SZNcxq0iQ1n3tJWmHag0oWs3p\n85pE+//UmgkU+mIxfMUgguYIEUxzdoiBqi6Td2hfsAltz43NNVcdEVN9YxLvuDCf\nLXvrD2W4rpIsucmdjXZ0arjfzwhpe+6pjRwH2sHJ6zSk3X2p+lgiRe56LG+WV2Qi\na4mKuabQiI5vEdfjmTtM7DzdhJDPEo4gdUg+R5flw4xxQqzyLH7m8mGjLjoQNXDQ\nw63jcKliIAWYLO7wJaB/\n=w4Ba\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:25:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/cd88fa2f357112d375d9d4014c5b37d8a8dc3e0f","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKGNkODhmYTJmMzU3MTEyZDM3NWQ5ZDQwMTRjNWIzN2Q4YThkYzNlMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66","sha":"709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66"}],"sha":"cd88fa2f357112d375d9d4014c5b37d8a8dc3e0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/cd88fa2f357112d375d9d4014c5b37d8a8dc3e0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T16:24:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T16:24:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: remediate blind-review findings (security, a11y, code quality, tests, docs) (#36)\n\n* fix: remediate blind-review findings (security, a11y, quality, tests, docs)\n\nAddresses the multi-dimension review captured in SUPPORT-629.\n\nBackend (src/main/java):\n- OSGi lifecycle: move IGNORE_PATTERN_EXECUTOR / WEBHOOK_EXECUTOR and warn-throttle\n  counters from static to instance fields, created in @Activate and shut down in\n  @Deactivate (prevents terminated-pool reuse after bundle refresh).\n- Thread-safety: HazelcastInstanceManager.discoveryServices -> CopyOnWriteArrayList.\n- Consistency: add startup reconciliation dropping expired JCR ban nodes and\n  restoring only live bans (Hazelcast<->JCR divergence).\n- Hot path: stop JCR writes on isIpCurrentlyBanned expiry (gate on remove()!=null);\n  read JCR ban-count once before the CAS loop; guard UnbanScheduler duplicate dispatch.\n- Security: normalize username (trim+lowercase) before ignore-pattern matching;\n  raise Hazelcast-down fail-open log to alertable ERROR.\n- Sonar: reduce RegexSafetyCheck cognitive complexity; catch Exception not Throwable;\n  rethrow WebhookSecretCodec with context; conditional logging; pattern-matching\n  instanceof; remove dead CONST_REF; dedupe sanitize() to AuditLogger.sanitize.\n\nFrontend (src/javascript, scss, locales):\n- Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): arrow-key/Home/End tablist navigation; accessible\n  ConfirmDialog replacing window.confirm (focus trap, Esc, restore); required-field\n  + error identification; AAA contrast (>=7:1); prefers-reduced-motion; 44px targets;\n  focus appearance; table captions; aria-sort; heading hierarchy; live-region timing.\n- Ergonomy/i18n: surface validation errors; route hardcoded strings through i18n.\n\nTests:\n- Add jacoco-maven-plugin with a 0.30 line-coverage regression ratchet (0.80 target).\n- New unit tests: UnbanScheduler, ignore-pattern fail-closed, EmailBanAction header\n  injection, WebhookBanAction HMAC/JSON, SettingsService validation (89 -> 154 tests).\n\nDocs:\n- CHANGELOG.md, docs/adr/* (Hazelcast topology, fail-open, valve position, consistency),\n  SECURITY.md PII-retention note, AGENTS.md version sync.\n\nVerified: mvn install green (154 unit tests, JaCoCo gate pass), yarn lint clean,\nyarn build OK, Cypress E2E 20/20 against a live Jahia.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address blind PR-review regressions (iteration 1)\n\nBackend (src/main/java):\n- H1 ignore-pattern: fail-OPEN (NOT_MATCHED) when ignorePatternExecutor is null/\n  shutdown, so a deactivated module no longer silently stops failure recording.\n- H2 startup reconciliation: bail (no JCR mutation) when Hazelcast isn''t running,\n  so live bans are never lost instead of restored.\n- H3 doBan fallback: re-read JCR ban-count in the last-write-wins path (no stale\n  recidive count); CAS loop keeps the single pre-read.\n- H4 UnbanScheduler.sweep: value-checked bans.remove(key, value) so a concurrently\n  re-installed ban for the same IP is not silently dropped.\n- M1 sweep: revert to catch(Throwable) (correct for scheduleWithFixedDelay), log\n  ERROR, NOSONAR-justified.\n- M2 username normalization moved to match-time in matchesIgnorePattern (consistent\n  across all auth methods; audit log keeps original case).\n- M3 reconcile: collect stale JCR nodes, remove after iterator exhausted.\n- M4 reconcile: broaden catch to RepositoryException | RuntimeException so it can''t\n  escape @Activate and disable the component.\n- C1 WebhookBanAction: null-guard before executor submit.\n- L1 BruteForceTracker.deactivate: awaitTermination before shutdownNow.\n- L3 rename throttle field to lastHazelcastDownAlertMs (now gates an ERROR alert).\n\nTests:\n- UnbanSchedulerTest: stub the value-checked IMap.remove(key, value) overload used\n  by the H4 fix.\n\nVerified: mvn install green (154 tests, JaCoCo gate pass).\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: remove useless assignment in handleTabKeyDown (github-code-quality)\n\nThe initial `let next = activeIndex` was always overwritten by a handled-key\nbranch, and the unhandled-key path returns early before `next` is read, so the\ninitializer is dead. Drop it to `let next;`. Behavior-neutral.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb383b451c23cfe48a99bf5ed9e37d4f4c24b2bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/fb383b451c23cfe48a99bf5ed9e37d4f4c24b2bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66","verification":{"payload":"tree fb383b451c23cfe48a99bf5ed9e37d4f4c24b2bc\nparent c8eddb1c000f79afb2357b748eac973c0cbd84ee\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781799874 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781799874 +0200\n\nfix: remediate blind-review findings (security, a11y, code quality, tests, docs) (#36)\n\n* fix: remediate blind-review findings (security, a11y, quality, tests, docs)\n\nAddresses the multi-dimension review captured in SUPPORT-629.\n\nBackend (src/main/java):\n- OSGi lifecycle: move IGNORE_PATTERN_EXECUTOR / WEBHOOK_EXECUTOR and warn-throttle\n  counters from static to instance fields, created in @Activate and shut down in\n  @Deactivate (prevents terminated-pool reuse after bundle refresh).\n- Thread-safety: HazelcastInstanceManager.discoveryServices -> CopyOnWriteArrayList.\n- Consistency: add startup reconciliation dropping expired JCR ban nodes and\n  restoring only live bans (Hazelcast<->JCR divergence).\n- Hot path: stop JCR writes on isIpCurrentlyBanned expiry (gate on remove()!=null);\n  read JCR ban-count once before the CAS loop; guard UnbanScheduler duplicate dispatch.\n- Security: normalize username (trim+lowercase) before ignore-pattern matching;\n  raise Hazelcast-down fail-open log to alertable ERROR.\n- Sonar: reduce RegexSafetyCheck cognitive complexity; catch Exception not Throwable;\n  rethrow WebhookSecretCodec with context; conditional logging; pattern-matching\n  instanceof; remove dead CONST_REF; dedupe sanitize() to AuditLogger.sanitize.\n\nFrontend (src/javascript, scss, locales):\n- Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): arrow-key/Home/End tablist navigation; accessible\n  ConfirmDialog replacing window.confirm (focus trap, Esc, restore); required-field\n  + error identification; AAA contrast (>=7:1); prefers-reduced-motion; 44px targets;\n  focus appearance; table captions; aria-sort; heading hierarchy; live-region timing.\n- Ergonomy/i18n: surface validation errors; route hardcoded strings through i18n.\n\nTests:\n- Add jacoco-maven-plugin with a 0.30 line-coverage regression ratchet (0.80 target).\n- New unit tests: UnbanScheduler, ignore-pattern fail-closed, EmailBanAction header\n  injection, WebhookBanAction HMAC/JSON, SettingsService validation (89 -> 154 tests).\n\nDocs:\n- CHANGELOG.md, docs/adr/* (Hazelcast topology, fail-open, valve position, consistency),\n  SECURITY.md PII-retention note, AGENTS.md version sync.\n\nVerified: mvn install green (154 unit tests, JaCoCo gate pass), yarn lint clean,\nyarn build OK, Cypress E2E 20/20 against a live Jahia.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address blind PR-review regressions (iteration 1)\n\nBackend (src/main/java):\n- H1 ignore-pattern: fail-OPEN (NOT_MATCHED) when ignorePatternExecutor is null/\n  shutdown, so a deactivated module no longer silently stops failure recording.\n- H2 startup reconciliation: bail (no JCR mutation) when Hazelcast isn''t running,\n  so live bans are never lost instead of restored.\n- H3 doBan fallback: re-read JCR ban-count in the last-write-wins path (no stale\n  recidive count); CAS loop keeps the single pre-read.\n- H4 UnbanScheduler.sweep: value-checked bans.remove(key, value) so a concurrently\n  re-installed ban for the same IP is not silently dropped.\n- M1 sweep: revert to catch(Throwable) (correct for scheduleWithFixedDelay), log\n  ERROR, NOSONAR-justified.\n- M2 username normalization moved to match-time in matchesIgnorePattern (consistent\n  across all auth methods; audit log keeps original case).\n- M3 reconcile: collect stale JCR nodes, remove after iterator exhausted.\n- M4 reconcile: broaden catch to RepositoryException | RuntimeException so it can''t\n  escape @Activate and disable the component.\n- C1 WebhookBanAction: null-guard before executor submit.\n- L1 BruteForceTracker.deactivate: awaitTermination before shutdownNow.\n- L3 rename throttle field to lastHazelcastDownAlertMs (now gates an ERROR alert).\n\nTests:\n- UnbanSchedulerTest: stub the value-checked IMap.remove(key, value) overload used\n  by the H4 fix.\n\nVerified: mvn install green (154 tests, JaCoCo gate pass).\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: remove useless assignment in handleTabKeyDown (github-code-quality)\n\nThe initial `let next = activeIndex` was always overwritten by a handled-key\nbranch, and the unhandled-key path returns early before `next` is read, so the\ninitializer is dead. Drop it to `let next;`. Behavior-neutral.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNBvCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh6UQAEEEzo4mlMFVtLydbpkmGSOy\n8T0ksY+idnS/nfHxnph5n3Cf9m9RiTZnPHFSSi90ALm2wRxPLmPs2SGo0xFHLe+L\nO7iIjyPJqzG9B6iI/mTt80fKYfj9HfvJihOTzrVBosNYNlnJsqT2utjzv5G9ylqW\nC1l4+dZ0mKl3StVrXmPVuLnC7YU57DpXjzyFWQ1RfsakwwjyCtcOfS/7dR8bQ4ci\nDYHXEUxoxwaIZPYEZC/SReB2HoAUcIf68H0fgkOBEqm0XRT2+Q4nahtA6kYilxUZ\nMxwiNAtT8bJtRsAza1rK8XFVuvW9JlSJ0Zmcs0EkPglfE46COW39YNstMNGAgGXL\ngtLef6iy+ywvUM9ZbEQHyqDH1CT6bLKyYKvkuzE9qfxM3eFOycrE5AqneB9GgK0E\nv808fuS9Dhc5IOrF9b+grlBeDXhKNTkomrY4rRTI4Tqm1D3h5sSNpiCnVYaJL74Y\nkTUVBFhoaQ0hVjEnz5dpF4GYFkBJ4w1pfTf8IeJANyD6y2iqGdgGM3AlS2W0lCSg\njQgHvYx4e/vbxU9KUeEL2LSSGL7BjL5kQrSi3l7fCqz/+LefAvp11POqm1cbsQ2p\nqrzJwlFblRkSjJ/Ag5QzZAawNJ4Kd5lnedOjnLIa0++UwzeT/XyTqunF167hWKlB\nnEgiHCO0YV+PbKCd4FhG\n=Vq2Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T16:24:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKDcwOWY1ODg3YTViZWNkMmQ2NGY1NDgwY2RlZDljNTMzZWQ3OTBiNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/c8eddb1c000f79afb2357b748eac973c0cbd84ee","sha":"c8eddb1c000f79afb2357b748eac973c0cbd84ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/c8eddb1c000f79afb2357b748eac973c0cbd84ee"}],"sha":"709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/709f5887a5becd2d64f5480cded9c533ed790b66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/c8eddb1c000f79afb2357b748eac973c0cbd84ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:07:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:07:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#34)\n\nGuards the `bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin` permission gate across the stack so it\ncannot be silently removed or mismatched between backend, frontend, and RBAC content.\n\n- Add src/main/import/roles.xml shipping an assignable server role\n  `brute-force-login-protection-administrator` granting only\n  `administrationAccess bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin` (no full admin), so the\n  module''s admin UI + GraphQL API can be delegated with least privilege.\n- Add tests/cypress/e2e/02-bruteForceLoginProtection-Permissions.cy.ts with 4 tests:\n  - GraphQL deny: a user without the permission gets \"Permission denied\" on the\n    gated `bruteForceLoginProtectionGlobalSettings` query.\n  - GraphQL allow: a user granted only the module role reads global settings with\n    no errors.\n  - Admin UI hidden: the admin panel (\"Flush all\" control) is absent for the\n    denied user at /jahia/administration/bruteForceLoginProtection.\n  - Admin UI shown: the panel renders for the user granted only the module role.\n- Bump module version 3.0.1-SNAPSHOT -> 3.0.2-SNAPSHOT so the new roles.xml import\n  content is re-imported on deploy.\n\nValidated with ./ci.build.sh && ./ci.startup.sh: 20/20 specs pass (16 existing\n+ 4 new), license health clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"17ee34e72df3ae2f5fdc13c8dc968563ee74b849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/17ee34e72df3ae2f5fdc13c8dc968563ee74b849"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/c8eddb1c000f79afb2357b748eac973c0cbd84ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 17ee34e72df3ae2f5fdc13c8dc968563ee74b849\nparent 1b472fc01a1d8fc2a5898de540b5cc8400840780\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118424 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118424 +0200\n\ntest: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#34)\n\nGuards the `bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin` permission gate across the stack so it\ncannot be silently removed or mismatched between backend, frontend, and RBAC content.\n\n- Add src/main/import/roles.xml shipping an assignable server role\n  `brute-force-login-protection-administrator` granting only\n  `administrationAccess bruteForceLoginProtectionAdmin` (no full admin), so the\n  module''s admin UI + GraphQL API can be delegated with least privilege.\n- Add tests/cypress/e2e/02-bruteForceLoginProtection-Permissions.cy.ts with 4 tests:\n  - GraphQL deny: a user without the permission gets \"Permission denied\" on the\n    gated `bruteForceLoginProtectionGlobalSettings` query.\n  - GraphQL allow: a user granted only the module role reads global settings with\n    no errors.\n  - Admin UI hidden: the admin panel (\"Flush all\" control) is absent for the\n    denied user at /jahia/administration/bruteForceLoginProtection.\n  - Admin UI shown: the panel renders for the user granted only the module role.\n- Bump module version 3.0.1-SNAPSHOT -> 3.0.2-SNAPSHOT so the new roles.xml import\n  content is re-imported on deploy.\n\nValidated with ./ci.build.sh && ./ci.startup.sh: 20/20 specs pass (16 existing\n+ 4 new), license health clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbXYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4YUQAJLI2dTtm5E1ZWixgCT4PfsA\nO60yligOektz2LxIbx8SJcwE2Ou6rgvksa3I1zO1ZBuQQO2GNHnxew1nB/TdoG3f\n0ptVNgYu8Iakj9T47wGet0TlwD6hrvxApwyvDjNTbJ4FdfDXVg44q35mQKr3/j72\nAXT0qdgUi47a1LRSnqUPdHhFzzwaq6OW/9l0njd//SIIQxSGZyGjys7qp/T7Pz/e\nQ3o83gFuWjlEWSsOY5CqNsWviCWvkVXf18CAt+AkLjHTvzoCisHSDmGMa7QIol7Z\nm2IUEqLkPwufD4h02/mfrRVO25rtoEhvuyYXEvh8XsK3nve8l7w3t55Kg62qIlIL\nf6eCzEY9yh8FisbEkCkjVh5RtbQsExLMaP7aoiX7hdDILHnzp+0OBIncu0/8cJwi\nDoAi8GF2kfdJgeKvyzTIdxxMSgtQ7lVoJ1IBS3fMIpjV9AnVIouxCTd1txuzsVIi\nsRSWwA7xdZN7G4w573ommoizRUNGok18