cjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/ec97c4c7e80af0cc346f511a40d25cbd9021f14e","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKGVjOTdjNGM3ZTgwYWYwY2MzNDZmNTExYTQwZDI1Y2JkOTAyMWYxNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/e91e31b3b595f7e50c364062d93fca60a1718c65","sha":"e91e31b3b595f7e50c364062d93fca60a1718c65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/e91e31b3b595f7e50c364062d93fca60a1718c65"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/a5d27809acf536cc159353fe413a82c34bb9bc60","sha":"a5d27809acf536cc159353fe413a82c34bb9bc60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/a5d27809acf536cc159353fe413a82c34bb9bc60"}],"sha":"ec97c4c7e80af0cc346f511a40d25cbd9021f14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/ec97c4c7e80af0cc346f511a40d25cbd9021f14e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/a5d27809acf536cc159353fe413a82c34bb9bc60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T19:57:55Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T19:57:55Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"harden: validation, distributed-state atomicity, lifecycle robustness + tests\n\nStrengthens the brute-force-login-protection module across input validation, concurrency,\nand resource lifecycle. No behavioural change to the happy-path ban flow (E2E 16/16 green).\n\nSecurity:\n- banManually / GraphQL banIp: reject non-IP literals (hostname/garbage) before storing a ban\n  key, preventing DNS lookups on the ban-check path and map/JCR key poisoning.\n- banManually: clamp duration to >= 1s so a misconfigured jail can''t store an instant-expiry ban.\n- SettingsService: validate emailRecipient (reject CR/LF/control chars + lenient shape check)\n  before persisting, as defense-in-depth against SMTP header injection.\n- RegexSafetyCheck: reject group nesting beyond a bounded depth instead of silently degrading the\n  ReDoS quantifier-density check (previously the >63 case stopped tracking and drifted depth).\n\nRobustness / concurrency:\n- BruteForceTracker: make the per-IP failure-window read-modify-write atomic across the cluster\n  via an IMap per-key lock (closes a lost-update race that could delay/miss bans); the lock is\n  held only around the window state, never across audit/JCR/webhook I/O.\n- isIpCurrentlyBanned: guard a non-running Hazelcast (throttled WARN) and remain deliberately\n  fail-open to avoid a login self-DoS if the distributed store is down.\n- UnbanScheduler: wrap the whole sweep (incl. audit-log trim) in catch(Throwable) and iterate a\n  snapshot, so a transient failure can''t permanently cancel scheduled ban expiry.\n- HazelcastInstanceManager: await discovery-scheduler termination on @Deactivate; make\n  discoveredMembers volatile.\n- AuditLogger: CAS the trim-counter reset so concurrent writes aren''t lost.\n\nTests (+35): WebhookUrlValidator SSRF allowlist, RegexSafetyCheck ReDoS lint incl. the new depth\ncap, CidrMatcher.isIpLiteral, WebhookSecretCodec null/legacy paths, AuditLogger.sanitize, and\nbanManually IP-rejection / valid-ban / fail-open behaviour.\n\nValidated: JAVA_HOME=<jdk17> mvn clean install -> 89 unit tests pass; full Cypress E2E 16/16.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"67dec8636341ae4fd3f8976e345f437439131125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/67dec8636341ae4fd3f8976e345f437439131125"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/a5d27809acf536cc159353fe413a82c34bb9bc60","verification":{"payload":"tree 67dec8636341ae4fd3f8976e345f437439131125\nparent e91e31b3b595f7e50c364062d93fca60a1718c65\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781035075 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781035075 +0200\n\nharden: validation, distributed-state atomicity, lifecycle robustness + tests\n\nStrengthens the brute-force-login-protection module across input validation, concurrency,\nand resource lifecycle. No behavioural change to the happy-path ban flow (E2E 16/16 green).\n\nSecurity:\n- banManually / GraphQL banIp: reject non-IP literals (hostname/garbage) before storing a ban\n  key, preventing DNS lookups on the ban-check path and map/JCR key poisoning.\n- banManually: clamp duration to >= 1s so a misconfigured jail can''t store an instant-expiry ban.\n- SettingsService: validate emailRecipient (reject CR/LF/control chars + lenient shape check)\n  before persisting, as defense-in-depth against SMTP header injection.\n- RegexSafetyCheck: reject group nesting beyond a bounded depth instead of silently degrading the\n  ReDoS quantifier-density check (previously the >63 case stopped tracking and drifted depth).\n\nRobustness / concurrency:\n- BruteForceTracker: make the per-IP failure-window read-modify-write atomic across the cluster\n  via an IMap per-key lock (closes a lost-update race that could delay/miss bans); the lock is\n  held only around the window state, never across audit/JCR/webhook I/O.\n- isIpCurrentlyBanned: guard a non-running Hazelcast (throttled WARN) and remain deliberately\n  fail-open to avoid a login self-DoS if the distributed store is down.\n- UnbanScheduler: wrap the whole sweep (incl. audit-log trim) in catch(Throwable) and iterate a\n  snapshot, so a transient failure can''t permanently cancel scheduled ban expiry.\n- HazelcastInstanceManager: await discovery-scheduler termination on @Deactivate; make\n  discoveredMembers volatile.\n- AuditLogger: CAS the trim-counter reset so concurrent writes aren''t lost.\n\nTests (+35): WebhookUrlValidator SSRF allowlist, RegexSafetyCheck ReDoS lint incl. the new depth\ncap, CidrMatcher.isIpLiteral, WebhookSecretCodec null/legacy paths, AuditLogger.sanitize, and\nbanManually IP-rejection / valid-ban / fail-open behaviour.\n\nValidated: JAVA_HOME=<jdk17> mvn clean install -> 89 unit tests pass; full Cypress E2E 16/16.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoocEMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3k9KAgAsgMrYIePALN2VE8pWdlwfzzPJkYlnHVmk0XZ6UMoqViYLJFWwfwH/y9r\nqyfvU7Ur6MlZ7/lwhERlONMegNmwU+gsAMiQLP3AA5cz4PRuqOMa+aCei0iWeHUV\nuHzKUPfUhf0eohAtcY1O3R9xCSjT/ILbfXpCX2d5M93+Wj0DqvoHKMhS4QYuDhYH\nCWt4q4OfpoKC4zKQB3FS