ourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/9ba333053cdc9c58120a2a92ed76b3f27b44ad54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T08:37:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T08:37:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor(bflp): clean up dead JCR schema after OSGi config migration\n\nGlobal settings and jail definitions moved to OSGi ConfigurationAdmin in\n61683f4, leaving the corresponding CND declarations and Java constants\nas dead storage. Drop them:\n\n- definitions.cnd: remove all property declarations on\n  [jnt:bruteForceLoginProtection] and the `+ jails ...` child. The node\n  type itself stays as the anchor for the still-JCR-backed `+ bans` and\n  `+ auditLog` children. Remove now-unused container/leaf node types\n  [jnt:bruteForceLoginProtectionJails] and\n  [jnt:bruteForceLoginProtectionJail].\n- BruteForceLoginProtectionConstants: drop JAILS_NODE_NAME,\n  JAILS_NODE_PATH, NT_JAIL, NT_JAILS_CONTAINER, all PROP_* global\n  settings constants and all PROP_JAIL_* constants. Verified no\n  remaining references in src/main/java or src/test/java. Ban/audit\n  constants and MAP_*/DEFAULT_* values are kept (still consumed).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"04b633f4db43bc3de36e83da338c9fb77f564463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/04b633f4db43bc3de36e83da338c9fb77f564463"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/9ba333053cdc9c58120a2a92ed76b3f27b44ad54","verification":{"payload":"tree 04b633f4db43bc3de36e83da338c9fb77f564463\nparent 61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779439058 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779439058 +0200\n\nrefactor(bflp): clean up dead JCR schema after OSGi config migration\n\nGlobal settings and jail definitions moved to OSGi ConfigurationAdmin in\n61683f4, leaving the corresponding CND declarations and Java constants\nas dead storage. Drop them:\n\n- definitions.cnd: remove all property declarations on\n  [jnt:bruteForceLoginProtection] and the `+ jails ...` child. The node\n  type itself stays as the anchor for the still-JCR-backed `+ bans` and\n  `+ auditLog` children. Remove now-unused container/leaf node types\n  [jnt:bruteForceLoginProtectionJails] and\n  [jnt:bruteForceLoginProtectionJail].\n- BruteForceLoginProtectionConstants: drop JAILS_NODE_NAME,\n  JAILS_NODE_PATH, NT_JAIL, NT_JAILS_CONTAINER, all PROP_* global\n  settings constants and all PROP_JAIL_* constants. Verified no\n  remaining references in src/main/java or src/test/java. Ban/audit\n  constants and MAP_*/DEFAULT_* values are kept (still consumed).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoQFdIACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mqKgf/QvcHzQdFVUCiI9Gy9T9dwkzt2FnInvAyCYxhB8TdF4J0fkJam2L2ExtF\nCMw9l70fy1QRX1ThY3cHt9AJWPzRyj0pwxN1QF100MNfmLZ1NrSdfNfu4+nS8ZE9\n0VAWH0nrz9LyiLXqTca8SOPDS87SAfw4zGDxBbPFHfIT8ts0o8i+e46h81NZcCTP\nfnWhgB5E5OReV81G9Y9WXPnf3q9fx6zrhAdwE/O+SVT9cz/Lr7uTRkOL7u3rOQLZ\noO0Ri0/vyr85qBKMPsg7swKdAn7M5gIq+01vJdQL+n5I5ab+bAq2BoFYOGsTQxBs\nEUHyUejS4gG1kBA4ajhuK0mkL5Gzgw==\n=XGWm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T11:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/9ba333053cdc9c58120a2a92ed76b3f27b44ad54","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKDliYTMzMzA1M2NkYzljNTgxMjBhMmE5MmVkNzZiM2YyN2I0NGFkNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8","sha":"61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8"}],"sha":"9ba333053cdc9c58120a2a92ed76b3f27b44ad54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/9ba333053cdc9c58120a2a92ed76b3f27b44ad54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T08:29:41Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T08:29:41Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor(bflp): move settings + jails from JCR to OSGi ConfigurationAdmin\n\nGlobal settings and jail definitions are now persisted as OSGi configuration\nunder <jahia-var>/karaf/etc/ instead of /settings/bruteforceloginprotection\nin JCR. Bans and the audit log remain JCR-backed (runtime state).\n\nPIDs:\n  - org.jahia.modules.bruteforceloginprotection.global  (singleton)\n  - org.jahia.modules.bruteforceloginprotection.jail    (factory, one .cfg per jail)\n\nNew components:\n  - GlobalConfigHolder: ManagedService for the singleton PID, exposes a\n    thread-safe AtomicReference<GlobalSettings> snapshot.\n  - JailConfigTracker: ManagedServiceFactory for the factory PID, keyed by\n    each jail''s mandatory ''name'' property.\n  - WebhookSecretCodec: shared helper for the {enc} prefix encryption.\n\nSettingsService is now a thin facade: reads delegate to the two new\ncomponents, writes go through ConfigurationAdmin so Felix file-install\nrewrites the corresponding .cfg on disk. getOrCreateSettingsNode() is\nretained so AuditLogger and BruteForceTracker can still anchor their JCR\nchildren, but the global properties on that node are no longer read.\n\nTri-state webhookSecret contract is preserved (null=unchanged, \"\"=clear,\nvalue=encrypted-replace). Operator-pasted plaintext is opportunistically\nre-encrypted on the next save.\n\nDefault .cfg files are shipped under\nsrc/main/resources/META-INF/configurations/ and dropped into karaf/etc/\non first deploy.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: existing v3.0.0-SNAPSHOT installs must re-enter their\nsettings — old JCR values are no longer read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9dfd6f3ee79b7bc325307579292e362228902a91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/9dfd6f3ee79b7bc325307579292e362228902a91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8","verification":{"payload":"tree 9dfd6f3ee79b7bc325307579292e362228902a91\nparent d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779438581 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779438581 +0200\n\nrefactor(bflp): move settings + jails from JCR to OSGi ConfigurationAdmin\n\nGlobal settings and jail definitions are now persisted as OSGi configuration\nunder <jahia-var>/karaf/etc/ instead of /settings/bruteforceloginprotection\nin JCR. Bans and the audit log remain JCR-backed (runtime state).\n\nPIDs:\n  - org.jahia.modules.bruteforceloginprotection.global  (singleton)\n  - org.jahia.modules.bruteforceloginprotection.jail    (factory, one .cfg per jail)\n\nNew components:\n  - GlobalConfigHolder: ManagedService for the singleton PID, exposes a\n    thread-safe AtomicReference<GlobalSettings> snapshot.\n  - JailConfigTracker: ManagedServiceFactory for the factory PID, keyed by\n    each jail''s mandatory ''name'' property.\n  - WebhookSecretCodec: shared helper for the {enc} prefix encryption.\n\nSettingsService is now a thin facade: reads delegate to the two new\ncomponents, writes go through ConfigurationAdmin so Felix file-install\nrewrites the corresponding .cfg on disk. getOrCreateSettingsNode() is\nretained so AuditLogger and BruteForceTracker can still anchor their JCR\nchildren, but the global properties on that node are no longer read.\n\nTri-state webhookSecret contract is preserved (null=unchanged, \"\"=clear,\nvalue=encrypted-replace). Operator-pasted plaintext is opportunistically\nre-encrypted on the next save.\n\nDefault .cfg files are shipped under\nsrc/main/resources/META-INF/configurations/ and dropped into karaf/etc/\non first deploy.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: existing v3.0.0-SNAPSHOT installs must re-enter their\nsettings — old JCR values are no longer read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoQE/UACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kA4wgAhMX/cmotLodBpNpbakxq0mSDfDQL54cHrA6WYAtt2FnU4CdRE/41JwTN\nZjK6nMwULGrftWw9vJHSdlRWuYkZ0WQgnF6Ir30pFzPSuOvhe7Xp6XEPBsNGDDCB\nbfoViW8Gn3iQwsTIT0cvCjB9bk5eaGxLcMjG7odJMgqHhYcRBjXt6/kdQsOpfiW8\n4SCZMs202BH204CqjfRp37nPf2La6SeTWsDag4rjRLgq51JSLfXDpLbz+Blws8oY\nwnM98HamZfls9UT7aBO6hxTHtb1A1FkfN5kzEb40CoETcFYtJt4mPOlNIyaccrsP\n+kbfF/Yec6VpFrogTKe3/mrZYyBCJA==\n=hgkr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T11:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKDYxNjgzZjQ2Mjk0MzFmNTliNDIzN2Q1ZTkyZjVlYjk3NDM1Zjc4Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8","sha":"d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8"}],"sha":"61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/61683f4629431f59b4237d5e92f5eb97435f78f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T08:16:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T08:16:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Harden BFLP: SSRF v6, jail-name, CAS bans, ReDoS fail-closed, secret encryption\n\n- WebhookUrlValidator: block IPv6 link-local (fe80::/10) and IPv4-mapped IPv6\n  (::ffff:x.x.x.x) addresses via raw-bytes inspection of Inet6Address.\n- SettingsService: reject jail names containing ''/'', ''\\\\'', ''..'' or '':'' in\n  saveJail/deleteJail to prevent JCR path traversal.\n- BruteForceTracker.doBan: replace read-then-write with a CAS loop using\n  IMap.putIfAbsent / replace (max 5 retries, fallback to put + warn) so\n  concurrent ban triggers can no longer both observe the same prevCount.\n- BruteForceTracker.matchesIgnorePattern: treat a regex timeout as MATCHED\n  (fail-closed) to deny ReDoS-based counter-bypass; cancel the future and\n  keep the rate-limited warning.\n- EmailBanAction: sanitize MailService.defaultSender() via stripHeaderInjection\n  to prevent SMTP header injection through a malicious default-sender config.\n- SettingsService: encrypt webhookSecret at rest in JCR using\n  EncryptionUtils.passwordBaseEncrypt with a ''{enc}'' marker prefix; legacy\n  plaintext values are transparently read and re-encrypted on next save.\n- HazelcastInstanceManager: best-effort ACL fallback when POSIX permissions\n  aren''t supported (Windows), granting only the owner access via\n  AclFileAttributeView; WARN if both POSIX and ACL fail.\n- ClassLoaderAwareObjectInputStream: drop java.lang.Enum from the\n  deserialization allowlist (concrete enum subclasses are already covered by\n  the module-prefix check).\n- WebhookBanAction: wrap the entire HTTP exchange in a Future with a 10s\n  overall deadline backed by a small static daemon pool; on timeout cancel\n  the task and forcibly disconnect the connection.\n- BruteForceTrackerTest: mock IMap.putIfAbsent and IMap.replace so the\n  in-memory store reflects the new CAS-based doBan path.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebf9c14ea73eecf99cec20eaa705a896db82f0e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/ebf9c14ea73eecf99cec20eaa705a896db82f0e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8","verification":{"payload":"tree ebf9c14ea73eecf99cec20eaa705a896db82f0e0\nparent d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779437811 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779437811 +0200\n\nHarden BFLP: SSRF v6, jail-name, CAS bans, ReDoS fail-closed, secret encryption\n\n- WebhookUrlValidator: block IPv6 link-local (fe80::/10) and IPv4-mapped IPv6\n  (::ffff:x.x.x.x) addresses via raw-bytes inspection of Inet6Address.\n- SettingsService: reject jail names containing ''/'', ''\\\\'', ''..'' or '':'' in\n  saveJail/deleteJail to prevent JCR path traversal.\n- BruteForceTracker.doBan: replace read-then-write with a CAS loop using\n  IMap.putIfAbsent / replace (max 5 retries, fallback to put + warn) so\n  concurrent ban triggers can no longer both observe the same prevCount.\n- BruteForceTracker.matchesIgnorePattern: treat a regex timeout as MATCHED\n  (fail-closed) to deny ReDoS-based counter-bypass; cancel the future and\n  keep the rate-limited warning.\n- EmailBanAction: sanitize MailService.defaultSender() via stripHeaderInjection\n  to prevent SMTP header injection through a malicious default-sender config.\n- SettingsService: encrypt webhookSecret at rest in JCR using\n  EncryptionUtils.passwordBaseEncrypt with a ''{enc}'' marker prefix; legacy\n  plaintext values are transparently read and re-encrypted on next save.\n- HazelcastInstanceManager: best-effort ACL fallback when POSIX permissions\n  aren''t supported (Windows), granting only the owner access via\n  AclFileAttributeView; WARN if both POSIX and ACL fail.\n- ClassLoaderAwareObjectInputStream: drop java.lang.Enum from the\n  deserialization allowlist (concrete enum subclasses are already covered by\n  the module-prefix check).\n- WebhookBanAction: wrap the entire HTTP exchange in a Future with a 10s\n  overall deadline backed by a small static daemon pool; on timeout cancel\n  the task and forcibly disconnect the connection.\n- BruteForceTrackerTest: mock IMap.putIfAbsent and IMap.replace so the\n  in-memory store reflects the new CAS-based doBan path.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoQEPMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mc2gf/QBCFm6OYwp3m6T2udUNeFYLvunyaGGqixGIgj651DRTjcHTXnXL9Y4Fz\nrco23NbiVSKuMKeOeyZjEfWlD0rut5ed94kO1htzSio00w6pLBG/ik/ZjgzyqZUq\nEpN8A3DgRRgoH1uOq4PUUFEx/JKTG/BGgvX1HKARPbWZcAfThsDoz+EpTfkeOTtB\nsW5HllK81S0rOqYr8qVWG0zf7LncDM6RoA0E8XfNz60z+rYMTec8iJjLsXI5es6p\nrQ7ph0Ptr3pnYnMVuXnKH19w7XKPjKSzjFAKWbZriu6xh3fc0XN69EeC4UUD8/6T\nSmMt0KgPCttxVclKPkIQn0RD27KPvQ==\n=V1dP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T11:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKGQwMGQ5MmE5NjMxYWVlMjY1ZGVkOTUwMDk1Y2FkZmU1NTAzZjdhYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd","sha":"d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd"}],"sha":"d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/d00d92a9631aee265ded950095cadfe5503f7ac8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T07:56:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T07:56:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Harden BFLP module: deserialization allowlist, SSRF guard, ReDoS limits, cluster secret\n\nSecurity hardening pass covering the brute-force-login-protection module:\n\n- Hazelcast deserialization: restrict resolveClass to a tight JDK + module-package\n  allowlist; reject all proxy classes outright.\n- Hazelcast group password: generate a per-install random secret stored in\n  karaf/etc/bflp-cluster-secret.properties (POSIX rw-------); inject via the\n  bflp.cluster.password system property so the XML placeholder resolves.\n- Hazelcast TLS: opt-in via -Dbflp.cluster.keystore=... etc.; documented in README.\n- Webhook SSRF guard: validate scheme, userinfo, and resolved-IP class (loopback,\n  link-local, site-local, multicast, 169.254.169.254, IPv6 ULA) both at settings-save\n  time and before each POST. DNS-rebinding via resolved-IP+Host pinning was not\n  implemented (TLS SNI interaction); host-based pre-check is in place.\n- ignorePatterns: lint user regexes (length, syntax, nested quantifiers, group\n  quantifier density); run matches in a daemon executor with a 50ms timeout and a\n  rate-limited warning on timeout.\n- X-Forwarded-For: new trustedProxyCidrs setting; XFF only honoured when the socket\n  remote address matches one of the configured CIDRs. Empty list while trust flag is\n  on logs a one-time warning and falls back to getRemoteAddr.\n- auditLogMaxEntries: clamped to [100, 100000].\n- EmailBanAction: strip CR/LF and percent-encoded equivalents from recipient and\n  subject to prevent SMTP header injection.\n- Webhook receiver guidance: README now documents constant-time signature verification.\n- GraphQL mutations: confirmed all already gated by @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"admin\");\n  no permission changes required.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d122172b59040d82e5d09c6b5898b271a2cb6d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/d122172b59040d82e5d09c6b5898b271a2cb6d0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd","verification":{"payload":"tree d122172b59040d82e5d09c6b5898b271a2cb6d0c\nparent ce566b33a00d70d1180fd91879cc5546efb27eb4\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779436581 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779436581 +0200\n\nHarden BFLP module: deserialization allowlist, SSRF guard, ReDoS limits, cluster secret\n\nSecurity hardening pass covering the brute-force-login-protection module:\n\n- Hazelcast deserialization: restrict resolveClass to a tight JDK + module-package\n  allowlist; reject all proxy classes outright.\n- Hazelcast group password: generate a per-install random secret stored in\n  karaf/etc/bflp-cluster-secret.properties (POSIX rw-------); inject via the\n  bflp.cluster.password system property so the XML placeholder resolves.\n- Hazelcast TLS: opt-in via -Dbflp.cluster.keystore=... etc.; documented in README.\n- Webhook SSRF guard: validate scheme, userinfo, and resolved-IP class (loopback,\n  link-local, site-local, multicast, 169.254.169.254, IPv6 ULA) both at settings-save\n  time and before each POST. DNS-rebinding via resolved-IP+Host pinning was not\n  implemented (TLS SNI interaction); host-based pre-check is in place.\n- ignorePatterns: lint user regexes (length, syntax, nested quantifiers, group\n  quantifier density); run matches in a daemon executor with a 50ms timeout and a\n  rate-limited warning on timeout.\n- X-Forwarded-For: new trustedProxyCidrs setting; XFF only honoured when the socket\n  remote address matches one of the configured CIDRs. Empty list while trust flag is\n  on logs a one-time warning and falls back to getRemoteAddr.\n- auditLogMaxEntries: clamped to [100, 100000].\n- EmailBanAction: strip CR/LF and percent-encoded equivalents from recipient and\n  subject to prevent SMTP header injection.\n- Webhook receiver guidance: README now documents constant-time signature verification.\n- GraphQL mutations: confirmed all already gated by @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"admin\");\n  no permission changes required.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoQDCUACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3l3OAf+IUKXneDyZwOq/QTcgiYWgA0RgcR2h4xE8DVStkNAxmyxY99m60DNc3al\nXD6k07GgorJ7L9wnbQOfdTA0V/EijDn6FjKc8RrJsOosKrEKXwiamvDlw57JL56F\nLRKDIoRbVEUKdWs2ngds671RJh3Io5uMDN0hNnVmOi4z5uMQSQ1O3kBfMQ1LRgUr\nIDnW4uc35Ffyl6JJCllWYUznmma9585haSXETQDbWBlTIsLOa1lNLWTxhDFYQ7lU\n8bB5hDMbcGN7jopmBk3aOw+6KmGoFWbXKonddR0DLRueDPMsmqPhJoKn8AbGTepY\ngx6/xAmtlCZWhXkoXHyxq2rUT8Ts7g==\n=f+uz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T11:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd","node_id":"C_kwDODN31CNoAKGQxM2NhZWJlODYzOWY3MmY5OWYzMmU1NTFiZTBlOWJlYjIzMjk3Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commit/ce566b33a00d70d1180fd91879cc5546efb27eb4","sha":"ce566b33a00d70d1180fd91879cc5546efb27eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/ce566b33a00d70d1180fd91879cc5546efb27eb4"}],"sha":"d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/d13caebe8639f72f99f32e551be0e9beb23297cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/commits/ce566b33a00d70d1180fd91879cc5546efb27eb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T07:38:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T07:38:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor(bflp): resolve all 40 SonarQube issues\n\nQuality gate already green; cleanup brings the open issue count to zero.\n\nHighlights:\n- Cognitive complexity: extracted helpers in AuditLogger.list() (26→<15)\n  and SettingsService.saveGlobalSettings() (34→<15).\n- Builder pattern for value objects with too many constructor params:\n  BanContext, GlobalSettings, FailureEvent. SaveGlobalSettings now takes\n  a GlobalSettingsUpdate parameter object.\n- `record` is a reserved word in Java 16+: renamed SPI method\n  FailureRecorder.record() → recordEvent(); updated implementers and\n  tests.\n- HazelcastInstanceManager: dropped the unused clusterManager field and\n  the dead `discoveryServices != null` check; OSGi binding kept as a\n  no-op setter for DS wiring.\n- Various: removed unused imports, redundant casts, unguarded logger\n  calls, deprecated Proxy.getProxyClass usage (suppressed with\n  justification — it is the contract API for\n  ObjectInputStream.resolveProxyClass).\n\nSuppressions (with reason):\n- java:S1075 on Constants — JCR paths use ''/'' by spec\n- java:S1874 in ClassLoaderAwareObjectInputStream — Proxy.getProxyClass\n  required by resolveProxyClass contract\n- java:S107 on the GraphQL saveGlobalSettings mutation — argument names\n  form the public GraphQL schema and cannot be collapsed\n\nTests: 34/34 pass. SonarQube post-scan: 0 open issues.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e69de2b4bf80d4d0f117071a45ae900b759e934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/trees/7e69de2b4bf80d4d0f117071a45ae900b759e934"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/brute-force-login-protection/git/commits/ce566b33a00d70d1180fd91879cc5546efb27eb4","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e69de2b4bf80d4d0f117071a45ae900b759e934\nparent 59ea1ab1679a144d2245cd301e2dc19f1fb916d6\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779435487 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779435487 +0200\n\nrefactor(bflp): resolve all 40 SonarQube issues\n\nQuality gate already green; cleanup brings the open issue count to zero.\n\nHighlights:\n- Cognitive complexity: extracted helpers in AuditLogger.list() (26→<15)\n  and SettingsService.saveGlobalSettings() (34→<15).\n- Builder pattern for value objects with too many constructor params:\n  BanContext, GlobalSettings, FailureEvent. SaveGlobalSettings now takes\n  a GlobalSettingsUpdate parameter object.\n- `record` is a reserved word in Java 16+: renamed SPI method\n  FailureRecorder.record() → recordEvent(); updated implementers and\n  tests.\n- HazelcastInstanceManager: dropped the unused clusterManager field and\n  the dead `discoveryServices != null` check; OSGi binding kept as a\n  no-op setter for DS wiring.\n- Various: removed unused imports, redundant casts, unguarded logger\n  calls, deprecated Proxy.getProxyClass usage (suppressed with\n  justification — it is the contract API for\n  ObjectInputStream.resolveProxyClass).\n\nSuppressions (with reason):\n- java:S1075 on Constants — JCR paths use ''/'' by spec\n- java:S1874 in ClassLoaderAwareObjectInputStream — Proxy.getProxyClass\n  required by resolveProxyClass contract\n- java:S107 on the GraphQL saveGlobalSettings mutation — argument names\n  form the public GraphQL schema and cannot be collapsed\n\nTests: 34/34 pass. SonarQube post-scan: 0 open issues.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoQB98ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3m1+wgAviWGiQ7sQK2lxZxGeVrNeB8CGtEBSXao/BW8shjphaKdpJ0d76PlM36o\nu9+UvVJO5fq+JXDn4pOyPiEGqLAhlny8NFY0GEt/c/vdfluyfM3Iwfn26HAW8l3R\n6sgxY8gQb9lSMw3sNm2lRKwgRT7ayaKHOKEL74eoAKQGn1f5Vfb3BIP9/itpU/Ax\nr33J8NRPi3hhqbd2jvVQrxelE0PDS7u0OsCgfNLu55LS09klio4YDKQeD3dg3OtC\n9cNyt2HsnC1F4ceIeIgDEshodfYzV/Nidk3ztUUFDjw+YeQ8K/hln4WDhtt+hXiW\ngb4hv72QAbsMk0LtnXwC0/3SJYNXkA==\n=L32P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T11:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fboura