pi.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/commit/23aadc11299be89565fc10fb7100bb2b558dfe3f","node_id":"C_kwDODSHTqtoAKDIzYWFkYzExMjk5YmU4OTU2NWZjMTBmYjcxMDBiYjJiNTU4ZGZlM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/commit/72105a2dd21c2bdd19669b142a960b12846df362","sha":"72105a2dd21c2bdd19669b142a960b12846df362","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/commits/72105a2dd21c2bdd19669b142a960b12846df362"}],"sha":"23aadc11299be89565fc10fb7100bb2b558dfe3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/commits/23aadc11299be89565fc10fb7100bb2b558dfe3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/commits/72105a2dd21c2bdd19669b142a960b12846df362/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:39Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(SUPPORT-646): coverage + audit logging, D5 route alignment, e2e fixes (#24)\n\n* test: add JUnit coverage for token generation, matching, node-expiry, login-request and ungated Karaf commands\n\n- SupportTokenGeneratorTest (G8/S4): RFC-4122 v4 format + no collisions over 1000 samples\n- SupportTokenCommandGateTest (G1/S13/U14): proves Karaf create/list/clear run with no\n  authorization/session context (behavioural) and carry no permission gate, contrasted with\n  the @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"supportTokenAdmin\") GraphQL resolvers (structural)\n- SupportTokenMatchTest (G6/S5): isTokenMatch bcrypt hit/miss + fail-closed (missing prop, blank token)\n- SupportTokenNodeExpiryTest (G7/S6): isTokenExpired node-level, fail-closed on missing expiration\n- SupportTokenLoginRequestedTest (G15/S27): doLogin=true/1/false recognition variants\n- Minimal seam: isTokenMatch/isTokenExpired/isLoginRequested made package-private (behaviour unchanged)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add Cypress coverage for mutation gate, session containment, login identity and token replay\n\n- 03 permissions (G3/S19): prove create + clearAll mutation denial without supportTokenAdmin\n  (previously only listTokens query denial was tested); (G3b/D5): siteAdminUsers-only holder is\n  denied every GraphQL op, pinning the site-route/GraphQL gate mismatch\n- 04 login (G10/S7-S8): positively assert resulting session identity (currentUser) is the intended\n  target, incl. root; (G9/U2/D7): CHARACTERIZATION that the same token authenticates twice (not single-use)\n- 05 session containment (G2/S12/U15/D1): NEW — token-authed session of a supportTokenAdmin holder\n  still gets listTokens=[], create=null, clearAll=false via the token session cookie\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): finalize mutation-denial and session-containment Cypress specs\n\nComplete the G3 create/clearAll mutation permission-denial (03) and the\nG2/S12/U15 session-containment (05) specs left uncommitted in the Stage-5\nCypress work. Run deferred to Stage 6.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: add impersonation audit logging, align D5 route permission, fix e2e GraphQL origin\n\nStage 7 genuine fixes:\n- U18: add [AUDIT] INFO logging using trusted resolved identities — minter on\n  supportToken.create, target on mint (SupportTokenUtils.addToken), and a distinct\n  successful token-login line in the valve (impersonation vs password login).\n- D5: align the site-settings admin UI route (register.jsx) to require\n  supportTokenAdmin, matching the GraphQL resolver gate (was siteAdminUsers, which\n  showed the menu but had every backend call refused).\n- U14: document the Karaf shell commands as a trusted server-administrator surface\n  (no per-caller Jahia identity to authorize against); keep the tripwire test.\n\nDocs (AGENTS.md): reconcile version to pom 3.1.2-SNAPSHOT, correct GraphQL ops to the\nnamespaced supportToken.* form, correct required permission to supportTokenAdmin, and\ncorrect the stale note that claimed the session block was removed (it is present).\n\nE2E: add the same-origin Origin header to raw cy.request GraphQL calls (Jahia GraphQL\nSecurityFilter/CSRF), keep currentUser identity assertion for the root regression, and\nassert the plain-user identity via the valve''s per-username credential binding.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5b335a56988d45523761ed94b08086fd8c04dfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/git/trees/b5b335a56988d45523761ed94b08086fd8c04dfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/support-token-authentication-valve/git/commits/72105a2dd21c2bdd19669b142a960b12846df362","verification":{"payload":"tree b5b335a56988d45523761ed94b08086fd8c04dfc\nparent 05adb5bfc64e2640b899f180d4e50151fd381eb2\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100459 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100459 +0200\n\ntest(SUPPORT-646): coverage + audit logging, D5 route alignment, e2e fixes (#24)\n\n* test: add JUnit coverage for token generation, matching, node-expiry, login-request and ungated Karaf commands\n\n- SupportTokenGeneratorTest (G8/S4): RFC-4122 v4 format + no collisions over 1000 samples\n- SupportTokenCommandGateTest (G1/S13/U14): proves Karaf create/list/clear run with no\n  authorization/session context (behavioural) and carry no permission gate, contrasted with\n  the @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"supportTokenAdmin\") GraphQL resolvers (structural)\n- SupportTokenMatchTest (G6/S5): isTokenMatch bcrypt hit/miss + fail-closed (missing prop, blank token)\n- SupportTokenNodeExpiryTest (G7/S6): isTokenExpired node-level, fail-closed on missing expiration\n- SupportTokenLoginRequestedTest (G15/S27): doLogin=true/1/false recognition variants\n- Minimal seam: isTokenMatch/isTokenExpired/isLoginRequested made package-private (behaviour unchanged)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add Cypress coverage for mutation gate, session containment, login identity and token replay\n\n- 03 permissions (G3/S19): prove create + clearAll mutation denial without supportTokenAdmin\n  (previously only listTokens query denial was tested); (G3b/D5): siteAdminUsers-only holder is\n  denied every GraphQL op, pinning the site-route/GraphQL gate mismatch\n- 04 login (G10/S7-S8): positively assert resulting session identity (currentUser) is the intended\n  target, incl. root; (G9/U2/D7): CHARACTERIZATION that the same token authenticates twice (not single-use)\n- 05 session containment (G2/S12/U15/D1): NEW — token-authed session of a supportTokenAdmin holder\n  still gets listTokens=[], create=null, clearAll=false via the token session cookie\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): finalize mutation-denial and session-containment Cypress specs\n\nComplete the G3 create/clearAll mutation permission-denial (03) and the\nG2/S12/U15 session-containment (05) specs left uncommitted in the Stage-5\nCypress work. Run deferred to Stage 6.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: add impersonation audit logging, align D5 route permission, fix e2e GraphQL origin\n\nStage 7 genuine fixes:\n- U18: add [AUDIT] INFO logging using trusted resolved identities — minter on\n  supportToken.create, target on mint (SupportTokenUtils.addToken), and a distinct\n  successful token-login line in the valve (impersonation vs password login).\n- D5: align the site-settings admin UI route (register.jsx) to require\n  supportTokenAdmin, matching the GraphQL resolver gate (was siteAdminUsers, which\n  showed the menu but had every backend call refused).\n- U14: document the Karaf shell commands as a trusted server-administrator surface\n  (no per-caller Jahia identity to authorize against); keep the tripwire test.\n\nDocs (AGENTS.md): reconcile version to pom 3.1.2-SNAPSHOT, correct GraphQL ops to the\nnamespaced supportToken.* form, correct required permission to supportTokenAdmin, and\ncorrect the stale note that claimed the session block was removed (it is present).\n\nE2E: add the same-origin Origin header to raw cy.request GraphQL calls (Jahia GraphQL\nSecurityFilter/CSRF), keep currentUser identity assertion for the root regression, and\nassert the plain-user identity via the valve''s per-username credential binding.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzZrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJaAQAKXR0kDZaiXf0dcLc5pCEOcN\nEJV2OTk4Ltg4vrsSj3Fr4InyoInIkNNIqIWJaS/LztmWuvx4UydHzz229s4ejKT2\ngk